/* TOTKmap · 声之记忆（Voice Memories · 240 条）独立数据文件
 * 由 tools/fetch_voice_memories.py + tools/merge_vm_zh.py 生成，请勿手工修改。
 * 包含 240 条官方简中标题、地名、精翻中文台词与 Zelda Wiki 完整英文原文。
 * 坐标口径：x = -gameY (北负南正), y = gameX (东正西负), z = gameZ (HUD 海拔)
 */
window.TOTK_VM_DATA = [{"seq":1,"id":"vm_rauru_001","no":"No.001","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":1690,"y":379,"z":2334,"gx":379,"gy":-1690,"gz":2334,"title_zh":"左纳乌神木","title_en":"Sacred Tree of the Zonai","place_zh":"初始空岛","place_en":"Great Sky Island","transcript_zh":"吾等一族的命脉与这棵树息息相连。族人繁盛之时，它亦随之枝繁叶茂。昔日，无数仪式曾在此举行。如今这份职责虽已交由时之神殿承继，但我深信，这棵神木至今仍在静静守护着我们。","transcript_en":"The lives of our people and this tree are interconnected. As we prospered, so too did it. It was the site for many of our rituals, and though that role has since been taken up by the Temple of Time, I am sure this sacred tree watches over us still."},{"seq":2,"id":"vm_rauru_002","no":"No.002","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":165,"y":365,"z":2298,"gx":365,"gy":-165,"gz":2298,"title_zh":"逐渐消失的遗产","title_en":"Fading Legacy","place_zh":"觉醒室","place_en":"Room of Awakening","transcript_zh":"这是一台结晶精炼机，所承担的精炼工艺极为繁复。正因如此，仅有极少数魔像能够胜任这项工作，而如今仍在运转的也只剩两台。好在眼下尚且够用，只是听说在很久以前，这种设施曾遍布整个王国……","transcript_en":"A crystal refinery, and one responsible for a highly complex manufacturing process. The nature of the work was such that only a select few constructs could perform it, and only two of those remain in operation. Fortunately that is enough for now, though apparently there was a time when they could be found throughout the kingdom..."},{"seq":3,"id":"vm_rauru_003","no":"No.003","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":899,"y":452,"z":1446,"gx":452,"gy":-899,"gz":1446,"title_zh":"驱邪破魔之楔","title_en":"Piercing Evil","place_zh":"时之神殿","place_en":"Temple of Time","transcript_zh":"时之神殿既是一座忠实报时的钟楼，也是这片土地的精神寄托。它沿袭了左纳乌族传统的建筑形制，向上直指苍穹，向下深扎大地。古人相信，唯有如此形制，方能贯穿并破除世间邪祟。","transcript_en":"The Temple of Time is a bell tower and faithful time keeper as well as a spiritual center of this land. It was constructed in a traditional Zonai architectural style that extends both up into the sky and down into the ground. It was believed in ancient times that such a design could pierce through evil."},{"seq":4,"id":"vm_rauru_004","no":"No.004","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":638,"y":453,"z":1472,"gx":453,"gy":-638,"gz":1472,"title_zh":"祭坛","title_en":"The Altar","place_zh":"时之神殿","place_en":"Temple of Time","transcript_zh":"这座祭坛被视作神殿中最为神圣之所。我们曾在此献上供品，祈愿世间物阜民丰、和平安宁。我曾听闻古老的传说，言此地能与某种神圣之力共鸣，从而往来于时光之间……至于究竟如何实现，便连我也无从知晓了。","transcript_en":"This altar is considered the most holy place in the temple, and it is where we give offerings as part of our prayers for a bountiful, peaceful world. I have heard ancient legends that it could interact with a sacred power, allowing travel back and forth through time... Though how this was done is a mystery to me."},{"seq":5,"id":"vm_rauru_005","no":"No.005","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":1032,"y":403,"z":1422,"gx":403,"gy":-1032,"gz":1422,"title_zh":"森林鸵鸟","title_en":"The Forest Ostrich","place_zh":"时之庭院","place_en":"Garden of Time","transcript_zh":"森林鸵鸟曾一度濒临灭绝。多亏王妃提议加以保护，这一物种方才重新繁衍生息。它们本是栖息于寒冷地带的生灵，却有着极强的适应力，除了酷寒的极地之外，在各地皆能蓬勃生长。","transcript_en":"The forest ostriches were once on the brink of extinction. However, a proposal by the queen was made to protect them, and eventually this species flourished once more. Though they were originally only found in colder lands, they are highly adaptable, thriving in all but the frigid polar regions."},{"seq":6,"id":"vm_rauru_006","no":"No.006","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":946,"y":323,"z":1442,"gx":323,"gy":-946,"gz":1442,"title_zh":"能源运输线","title_en":"Energy Lines","place_zh":"时之庭院","place_en":"Garden of Time","transcript_zh":"这些轨道本用于运送物资，同时也兼作通过管道输送能源的设施。鼓隆族人广泛运用着类似的机关，或许他们的设计，正是借鉴了吾等的技术也未可知……","transcript_en":"These rails are intended to transport materials, but they also supply energy through pipes. The Goron people make extensive use of this kind of mechanism, and I believe it is possible they modeled their designs on our own technology..."},{"seq":7,"id":"vm_rauru_007","no":"No.007","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":1083,"y":176,"z":1415,"gx":176,"gy":-1083,"gz":1415,"title_zh":"魔像的秩序","title_en":"Construct Compassion","place_zh":"时之庭院","place_en":"Garden of Time","transcript_zh":"偶尔能见到魔像们排起长队，静候空出的充能之位。更有趣的是，有些魔像还会主动让出位置，好让更急需补充能源的同伴先行充能。若是世人皆能常怀这般体恤之心，该有多好啊……","transcript_en":"On occasion, constructs have been observed forming a line as they wait for an available charging spot. More interestingly, some will give up their place in that line to allow constructs with a greater need to recharge first. Were it that everyone always acted with such empathy..."},{"seq":8,"id":"vm_rauru_008","no":"No.008","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":1169,"y":115,"z":1417,"gx":115,"gy":-1169,"gz":1417,"title_zh":"模仿试吃","title_en":"A Sense of Taste","place_zh":"时之庭院","place_en":"Garden of Time","transcript_zh":"料理魔像被赋予了烹调佳肴与调制药物的知识。尽管它们并无味觉，却学会了模仿我们品尝食物时的神态与动作。就连当初赋予它们学习能力的妹妹，见它们单凭观察便能领悟至此，也不禁大感惊奇。","transcript_en":"Our Culinary Constructs were imparted with knowledge of both cooking meals and concocting medicines. Though they have no taste buds, they learned to mimic the movements we make when tasting food. Even my sister, who gifted them with the ability to learn in the first place, was surprised by what they glean through simple observation."},{"seq":9,"id":"vm_rauru_009","no":"No.009","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":1675,"y":446,"z":1442,"gx":446,"gy":-1675,"gz":1442,"title_zh":"不断思考","title_en":"Musings","place_zh":"时之庭院","place_en":"Garden of Time","transcript_zh":"此物名为左纳乌装置制造机，但将结果托付于运气的理念，在吾等文明中实属罕见。我私下以为，它最初的用途应当另有他意。或许曾用于消遣娱乐，又或许它原本就并非出自左纳乌族之手……先祖留下的诸多事物虽时常令人费解，细细推敲起来，倒也不失为一番趣事。","transcript_en":"This is known as a Zonai device dispenser, but the concept of leaving things to chance is not one often seen in our civilization. I myself believe that it was originally created with a different purpose. Maybe it was used for entertainment, or maybe it was not even originally made by the Zonai... The ways of our ancestors are sometimes unclear, but they are also interesting puzzles to unravel."},{"seq":10,"id":"vm_rauru_010","no":"No.010","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":1517,"y":492,"z":1439,"gx":492,"gy":-1517,"gz":1439,"title_zh":"空岛的守卫","title_en":"Sky Island Guardians","place_zh":"初始空岛","place_en":"Great Sky Island","transcript_zh":"方块魔像在非战斗状态下虽能进入待机模式以节省能源，但在吾等诸多造物之中，它们的能耗效率依旧偏低。鉴于这份局限，我本想改良其构造以拓展行动范围，可妹妹却说，先祖留下的设计图纸实在晦涩难解。","transcript_en":"Though the Flux Constructs can enter a standby mode, reducing energy consumption outside of battle, they remain one of our less energy-efficient creations. Considering their limitations, I would love to improve on their design and give them greater range, but my sister says the ancients' schematics for them are quite abstruse."},{"seq":11,"id":"vm_rauru_011","no":"No.011","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":1626,"y":634,"z":1485,"gx":634,"gy":-1626,"gz":1485,"title_zh":"人工创造的银色世界","title_en":"Crafted Snowscape","place_zh":"初始空岛","place_en":"Great Sky Island","transcript_zh":"我们曾在此处借助冰龙头的力量，造就了一片终年积雪的银白天地。以寒气笼罩整座空岛，便形成了一处检验魔像与左纳乌装置耐久性的绝佳试验场。至今我仍清晰记得，初次与索尼娅一同造访此地时，她脸上流露出的惊叹神情。","transcript_en":"It was here that we used the capabilities of frost emitters to create a permanently snowy region. By encircling the island in cold air, we created an ideal place to test the durability of constructs and Zonai devices. I'll always remember the look of wonder on Sonia's face the first time we came here."},{"seq":12,"id":"vm_rauru_012","no":"No.012","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":1287,"y":742,"z":1562,"gx":742,"gy":-1287,"gz":1562,"title_zh":"禁止双人搭乘","title_en":"Solo Riders Only","place_zh":"初始空岛","place_en":"Great Sky Island","transcript_zh":"这座起降场原是为了便于在空岛之间运送物资而建。我本希望海拉鲁的子民也能善加利用，只是这些飞行器操控起来着实不易。我曾想在索尼娅练习时与她同乘，却被一旁的魔像拦了下来，执意称此装置仅限单人搭乘……","transcript_en":"We intended for this airfield to allow easy transportation of goods between sky islands—while I hoped the people of Hyrule would make use of it, the flying machines proved challenging to control. I once sought to join Sonia while she practiced with one, but a construct stopped me, insisting that the devices are limited to one rider..."},{"seq":13,"id":"vm_rauru_013","no":"No.013","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":1357,"y":634,"z":1427,"gx":634,"gy":-1357,"gz":1427,"title_zh":"新人魔像","title_en":"Inexperienced Constructs","place_zh":"初始空岛","place_en":"Great Sky Island","transcript_zh":"论起操控左纳乌装置的娴熟程度，恐怕无人能出制造魔像其右。不过，面对资历尚浅的魔像所打造的器物，还是得留个心眼。我还记得有一次乘筏渡水，因风扇机装偏了位置，木筏几乎难以掌舵，场面一片狼藉。我全程胆战心惊，索尼娅王妃反倒乐在其中。","transcript_en":"I do not believe anyone else is as proficient at handling Zonai devices as the Maker Constructs. That said, one should be careful around the inventions of less experienced ones. I recall a very chaotic rafting ride when a misaligned fan made it nearly impossible to steer. I was scared half to death throughout, but Queen Sonia enjoyed herself."},{"seq":14,"id":"vm_rauru_014","no":"No.014","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":1005,"y":1847,"z":861,"gx":1847,"gy":-1005,"gz":861,"title_zh":"圆环","title_en":"Circular Design","place_zh":"北哈特尔天空诸岛","place_en":"North Necluda Sky Archipelago","transcript_zh":"圆环之形常象征永恒的羁绊，古时更被认为具有辟邪之效。或许正是出于这番寓意，此地的诸多建筑皆呈环状。这里曾是一座珍藏着无数重要文献的档案馆，只是如今，仅余妹妹妥善保管的那些典籍留存于世了。","transcript_en":"Circular designs often represent an eternal bond and were even thought to ward off evil. Perhaps with that in mind, many of the structures here have been constructed with a circular shape. Though this was once an archive containing many important records, now only those my sister keeps remain."},{"seq":15,"id":"vm_rauru_015","no":"No.015","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":1702,"y":2396,"z":1475,"gx":2396,"gy":-1702,"gz":1475,"title_zh":"左纳尼乌姆制炼之岛","title_en":"Zonaite Forge Island","place_zh":"左纳尼乌姆制炼之岛","place_en":"Zonaite Forge Island","transcript_zh":"昔日，即便在空岛之上，左纳尼乌姆也俯拾皆是。这座庞大的制炼设施，正是那个无人会忧虑其匮乏的年代所留下的遗迹。当然，为制炼厂提供动力的熔岩至今仍在流淌。我应当与妹妹商议一番，看看这座熔炉是否还能派上用场……","transcript_en":"Zonaite was once readily found even on sky islands; this giant refinery is a remnant of a time where its scarcity seemed impossible. Of course, the lava that powered the refinery still remains. I should consult with my sister and see whether we can yet find a use for this furnace..."},{"seq":16,"id":"vm_rauru_016","no":"No.016","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":864,"y":4448,"z":2620,"gx":4448,"gy":-864,"gz":2620,"title_zh":"测试大勇之岛","title_en":"Valor Island","place_zh":"测试大勇之岛","place_en":"Valor Island","transcript_zh":"通过高空俯冲试炼之人，将被赐予蕴含力量的装束。穿戴此衣不仅能在空中自如掌控身形，若集齐全套，任凭从多高之处坠落，亦无需畏惧触地之险。远古的左纳乌族人偶尔也会失足坠向大地，想来正是这套装束护住了他们的周全。","transcript_en":"Those that complete the skydiving trial are bestowed empowering attire. It allows them to better control their movement in the air, and if all the pieces are worn together, the wearer need not fear striking the ground no matter how far they fall. The ancient Zonai even fell to the surface at times, but I believe this attire kept them safe too."},{"seq":17,"id":"vm_rauru_017","no":"No.017","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":-293,"y":3644,"z":1192,"gx":3644,"gy":293,"gz":1192,"title_zh":"低重力空间","title_en":"Low-Gravity Space","place_zh":"水涌之岛","place_en":"Wellspring Island","transcript_zh":"听说这片低重力空间最初是为了减轻货物运送途中的颠簸而设。然而它如今却多了另一番妙用——卓拉族人似乎格外沉醉于在长空中畅游的滋味。","transcript_en":"I have heard that the original reason for the lower gravity in this space was to reduce the jolts cargo could experience during transit. However, it has an additional use; it seems the Zora greatly enjoy the sensation of swimming through the sky."},{"seq":18,"id":"vm_rauru_018","no":"No.018","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":-406,"y":3578,"z":1202,"gx":3578,"gy":406,"gz":1202,"title_zh":"浮游水球","title_en":"Floating Spheres of Water","place_zh":"水涌之岛","place_en":"Wellspring Island","transcript_zh":"得益于此地充沛的水源，这里成了研究水之特性的绝佳场所。譬如这些浮游水球，本有望为物资运输带来革新，可惜它们难以长久维持形态，因此仅能用于部分空岛之上。","transcript_en":"Thanks to the plentiful water available here, this is a prime spot for conducting water-related research. The floating spheres, for example, have the potential to revolutionize logistics, but as they do not retain their shape for long, their use is limited to certain islands."},{"seq":19,"id":"vm_rauru_019","no":"No.019","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":-793,"y":3349,"z":1750,"gx":3349,"gy":793,"gz":1750,"title_zh":"水涌之岛","title_en":"Wellspring Island","place_zh":"水之神殿","place_en":"Water Temple","transcript_zh":"从这里涌出的水流终将化作云雨，润泽下方的大地。远古时期的卓拉族曾与左纳乌族有所往来，想来他们便是借助这挂巍峨的瀑布，往返于大地与云霄之间。嗯，世人将这道瀑布称作“桥梁”，倒也恰如其分。","transcript_en":"The water that flows from here eventually becomes clouds and rain, bringing water down to the land. The Zora people in ancient times had dealings with the Zonai, and I can imagine they used the immense waterfall to travel from the surface to the sky. Hmm. It is appropriate some refer to this waterfall as a bridge."},{"seq":20,"id":"vm_rauru_020","no":"No.020","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":-538,"y":4080,"z":602,"gx":4080,"gy":538,"gz":602,"title_zh":"鱼鳞飞舞之岛","title_en":"Floating Scales Island","place_zh":"鱼鳞飞舞之岛","place_en":"Floating Scales Island","transcript_zh":"当初听卓拉族人说起天空中有条大鱼，我还觉得颇为古怪，如今亲眼所见，总算明白他们所言何意了。他们还嘱咐我站在中央高台的边缘向西南眺望，可我……哦……原来如此！嗯，这番巧思，果真极具卓拉族的风范。","transcript_en":"I thought it very strange when I heard from the Zora that there was a fish in the sky, but now I see what they meant. They also told me to stand on the edge of the center platform and look out to the southwest, but I... Oh... I understand! Mmm. Quite befitting the Zora."},{"seq":21,"id":"vm_rauru_021","no":"No.021","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":-1505,"y":3702,"z":1162,"gx":3702,"gy":1505,"gz":1162,"title_zh":"投射装置","title_en":"Launch Mechanism","place_zh":"南阿卡莱天空诸岛","place_en":"Sokkala Sky Archipelago","transcript_zh":"这附近散落着不少残骸。看来昔日曾在此处装卸货物……嗯……莫非是因为容器形状奇特，才使得投射装置难以精准操控么……","transcript_en":"A lot of debris is scattered in the area. It is likely that cargo was handled here and...hmm... Perhaps the strange shape of the container made it difficult to control the launch mechanism..."},{"seq":22,"id":"vm_rauru_022","no":"No.022","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":-2128,"y":4525,"z":1160,"gx":4525,"gy":2128,"gz":1160,"title_zh":"采石之岛","title_en":"Sky Mine","place_zh":"采石之岛","place_en":"Sky Mine","transcript_zh":"这片空域曾以星罗棋布的浮岛中蕴藏着丰富矿石而闻名。昔日无数人慕名而来，只为追逐财富，而今却只余寥寥几处矿场。不过，若有佳人相伴身侧，共赏矿脉在夜空下熠熠生辉之景，那份珍贵，终究远胜世间财宝吧……","transcript_en":"This area was once known for the abundance of ore that could be mined from the numerous floating islands. Many gathered here to make their fortunes, though today, only a few mines remain. The sight of ore deposits sparkling in the night sky—wonderful company at one's side—is a better kind of fortune, in any case..."},{"seq":23,"id":"vm_rauru_023","no":"No.023","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":-3513,"y":4654,"z":1010,"gx":4654,"gy":3513,"gz":1010,"title_zh":"龙所司掌的迷宫","title_en":"Ruled by the Dragon","place_zh":"洛美岛上层","place_en":"Lomei Sky Labyrinth","transcript_zh":"相传在得到迷宫守护者的指引之前，灵魂将永远徘徊于这些长廊之中。或许这里正是裁决自欺之人的厅堂……是此地守护者衡量灵魂勇气之所在。","transcript_en":"It is said that until the guardian of this labyrinth offered guidance, a soul would be set to wander these halls. Perhaps this was the room where those dishonest with themselves were judged...where the guardian of this place weighed the courage of a soul."},{"seq":24,"id":"vm_rauru_024","no":"No.024","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":-2055,"y":221,"z":1988,"gx":221,"gy":2055,"gz":1988,"title_zh":"测试刚勇之岛","title_en":"Bravery Island","place_zh":"测试刚勇之岛","place_en":"Bravery Island","transcript_zh":"在左纳乌装置足以轻而易举化解诸多阻碍的时代，不假外物翱翔天际、克服坠落之惧的念头，已被视作毫无必要的空想。然而如今吾等一族仅剩妹妹与我二人，我发自肺腑地深信，不断磨砺自身、力求精进，比以往任何时候都更为重要。","transcript_en":"In a time when Zonai devices make it easy to overcome many of life's obstacles, the idea of flying through the sky without assistance—of overcoming one's fear of falling—has been dismissed as unnecessary idealism. But now that only my sister and I remain, I believe, with my whole being, that it is more important than ever to always strive to grow."},{"seq":25,"id":"vm_rauru_025","no":"No.025","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":-3535,"y":-955,"z":1011,"gx":-955,"gy":3535,"gz":1011,"title_zh":"枭所司掌的迷宫","title_en":"Ruled by the Owl","place_zh":"北洛美城堡上层","place_en":"North Lomei Castle Top Floor","transcript_zh":"我曾听闻，在此得到迷宫守护者的指引之前，灵魂便会一直迷失于这座迷宫。这么看来，或许正是智慧的守护者在此以明察秋毫之智，裁决那些欺瞒他人之辈吧……","transcript_en":"I have heard that, until a soul here receives guidance from the labyrinth's guardian, it will wander this maze. Perhaps it was here, then, that the guardian of wisdom, with their keen mind, would pass judgment on those who deceived others..."},{"seq":26,"id":"vm_rauru_026","no":"No.026","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":-2985,"y":-2813,"z":861,"gx":-2813,"gy":2985,"gz":861,"title_zh":"渡船","title_en":"Traversal Challenges","place_zh":"通往天空的连绵岛屿","place_en":"Rising Island Chain","transcript_zh":"我为破除邪祟而踏上此行，索尼娅亦随行相伴。只是我未曾料到，这段旅途竟如此崎岖难行。若我拥有妹妹那般的力量，或许就能驱动这艘船只了……","transcript_en":"I traveled here on a quest to cleanse evil, and Sonia has accompanied me. However, I had not considered how challenging it would be to traverse this path. If I had my sister's power, I could perhaps move this vessel..."},{"seq":27,"id":"vm_rauru_027","no":"No.027","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":-2927,"y":-2858,"z":1517,"gx":-2858,"gy":2927,"gz":1517,"title_zh":"天鸟船","title_en":"Stormwind Ark","place_zh":"风之神殿","place_en":"Wind Temple","transcript_zh":"啊，我似乎想起来了……\n“左纳乌族坠长空，\n利特振翅急相从。\n为报昔日救命恩，\n遂造天鸟船相奉。\n左纳乌赠此厚礼，\n利特族欢欣满怀。”\n这是吾等一族流传已久的古谣。眼前这艘船，莫非便是传说中的天鸟船？","transcript_en":"Ah, I think I remember...\n\"When a Zonai tumbled,\nRito wings gave chase.\nIn thanks for their salvation,\nThe Stormwind Ark was made.\nA gift given from the Zonai,\nAnd the Rito filled with joy.\"\nIt is an old legend of my people. Could this be that vessel?"},{"seq":28,"id":"vm_rauru_028","no":"No.028","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":-927,"y":-2222,"z":1642,"gx":-2222,"gy":927,"gz":1642,"title_zh":"测试勇气之岛","title_en":"Courage Island","place_zh":"测试勇气之岛","place_en":"Courage Island","transcript_zh":"在此举行的仪式，是一场考验心、体、技的试炼。曾几何时，凡是步入成年的族人皆须接受这场考验；但随着左纳乌装置日渐发达普及，唯有渴望磨砺自身勇气之人方会前来挑战。不知这座空岛日后是否还能迎来新的挑战者……","transcript_en":"The ceremony held here was a trial of heart, strength, and technique. There was a time where everyone who came of age would undertake this test, but as Zonai devices developed and spread, only those wishing to challenge their courage would take part. I wonder if this island will ever see a new challenger..."},{"seq":29,"id":"vm_rauru_029","no":"No.029","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":-1058,"y":-3680,"z":1796,"gx":-3680,"gy":1058,"gz":1796,"title_zh":"祓暗之岛","title_en":"Lightcast Island","place_zh":"祓暗之岛","place_en":"Lightcast Island","transcript_zh":"这座岛屿，是身负光之力量者的修行之地。唯有持之以恒地锤炼这份力量，方能成长到足以战胜深重邪恶的境界。唉，回想起年少之时，我也不知曾来过此地多少回了……","transcript_en":"This island is a training site for those who carry the power of light. By practicing at length with this power, one can grow strong enough to overcome great evil. Oh, to recall all the times I had visited this place in my youth..."},{"seq":30,"id":"vm_rauru_030","no":"No.030","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":320,"y":-3493,"z":1931,"gx":-3493,"gy":-320,"gz":1931,"title_zh":"星见之岛","title_en":"Starview Island","place_zh":"星见之岛","place_en":"Starview Island","transcript_zh":"这座岛屿原本用作存放物资的库房，只是早已荒废多年，不再承担此任。虽然它并无正式之名，但世人渐渐习惯称其为“星见之岛”。不过于我而言，世间真正闪耀的星辰，唯有索尼娅眼眸中流转的那一抹星光罢了……","transcript_en":"Though this island was originally used as a place to store things, it has been a long time since it fulfilled that role. And while the island lacks an official name, many have come to call it Starview Island. As for me, the only real stars are those sparkling in Sonia's eyes..."},{"seq":31,"id":"vm_rauru_031","no":"No.031","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":2113,"y":-1722,"z":1149,"gx":-1722,"gy":-2113,"gz":1149,"title_zh":"逐渐崩塌的要塞","title_en":"Crumbling Fortress","place_zh":"东格鲁德天空诸岛","place_en":"East Gerudo Sky Archipelago","transcript_zh":"这座岛屿原本旨在筑起一道固若金汤的要塞高墙，可它的崩塌速度似乎比其他空岛都要快上许多……莫非是受了格鲁德地区干燥气候的影响？无论如何，我得尽快委托制造魔像前来修缮；倘若整座岛屿坠落大地，必将酿成大祸。","transcript_en":"This island was intended to be a fortress with a strong wall, but it seems to be collapsing faster than other islands... I wonder if the dry climate of the Gerudo region is at fault. Regardless, I should commission a Maker Construct to help as soon as possible; it would be a disaster if the island fell to the surface."},{"seq":32,"id":"vm_rauru_032","no":"No.032","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":3305,"y":-1794,"z":1010,"gx":-1794,"gy":-3305,"gz":1010,"title_zh":"野猪所司掌的迷宫","title_en":"Ruled by the Boar","place_zh":"南洛美城堡上层","place_en":"South Lomei Castle Top Floor","transcript_zh":"有传闻言，在被那位据称身躯巍峨、顶天立地的力量守护者涤去傲慢之前，灵魂便会永远徘徊在这些长廊之中。或许正是在这间厅堂里，那些过分炫耀自身力量之辈受到了裁决……","transcript_en":"There are stories that claim a soul will wander these halls until the guardian of power—said to reach from depths to sky, it was so large—has cleansed them of their pride. Perhaps it was in this room that judgment was passed on those overly boastful of their power..."},{"seq":33,"id":"vm_rauru_033","no":"No.033","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":2630,"y":721,"z":737,"gx":721,"gy":-2630,"gz":737,"title_zh":"雷鸣之岛","title_en":"Thunderhead Isles","place_zh":"雷鸣之岛","place_en":"Thunderhead Isles","transcript_zh":"这里原本是一座用于转运并储存地底物资的港口，如今则由妹妹接管，改作了存放魔像的仓库。此地戒备森严得非比寻常，便连我前来也颇费了一番周折。不过以我对妹妹的了解，她这么做定有她的深意。","transcript_en":"This was originally a port where materials from the Depths were imported and stored, but it is currently being managed by my sister as a construct warehouse. Security is unusually tight—even I had trouble coming here—but knowing my sister, she has her reasons."},{"seq":34,"id":"vm_rauru_034","no":"No.034","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":2902,"y":895,"z":758,"gx":895,"gy":-2902,"gz":758,"title_zh":"雷龙信仰","title_en":"Faith in the Lightning Dragon","place_zh":"雷鸣之岛","place_en":"Thunderhead Isles","transcript_zh":"大地上的子民坚信此物乃是雷龙神佑的明证。殊不知，这其实只是左纳乌族为防范雷击而建的避雷针。或许关于雷龙的信仰便是由此萌生……世间信仰，究竟有多少是源自这般毫无关联的巧合呢。","transcript_en":"The people on the surface believe this to be proof of the lightning dragon's divine protection. In actuality, it is a lightning rod the Zonai constructed to prevent lightning strikes. Perhaps this is how belief in the lightning dragon began... I wonder how often belief results from unrelated coincidence."},{"seq":35,"id":"vm_rauru_035","no":"No.035","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":3111,"y":957,"z":755,"gx":957,"gy":-3111,"gz":755,"title_zh":"宝藏地图","title_en":"Treasure Maps","place_zh":"雷鸣之岛","place_en":"Thunderhead Isles","transcript_zh":"身处此地，心中不由得涌起一股浓浓的怀念。年少之时，我对搜寻和研读宝藏地图痴迷不已。不知不觉间，不仅将诸座空岛的地形地貌了然于胸，也顺带熟稔了各种左纳乌装置的用法。哈哈哈……果然，唯有纯粹的好奇心，才是驱动人求知的最大动力啊。","transcript_en":"I get a strong sense of nostalgia in this place. When I was young, I was intensely interested in finding and studying treasure maps. Before I knew it, I had become quite familiar with the topography of the sky islands and, incidentally, with Zonai devices. Hahaha...nothing motivates one to learn like a healthy sense of curiosity."},{"seq":36,"id":"vm_zelda_001","no":"No.001","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-613,"y":-253,"z":42,"gx":-253,"gy":613,"gz":42,"title_zh":"海拉鲁城堡大门","title_en":"Hyrule Castle Gates","place_zh":"海拉鲁城堡大门","place_en":"Hyrule Castle Gate","transcript_zh":"听说这座城堡大门凝聚了希卡族的智慧与鼓隆族的工艺。父王生前总说它绝不会陷落，从某种意义上讲他说得没错——这是整座城堡中唯一至今仍完好无损的地方。","transcript_en":"I have heard the castle gate is the product of Sheikah wisdom and Goron engineering. Father always said it would never fall, and he was technically correct; it is the only part of the castle that remains unblemished."},{"seq":37,"id":"vm_zelda_002","no":"No.002","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-871,"y":-102,"z":104,"gx":-102,"gy":871,"gz":104,"title_zh":"王族餐桌","title_en":"The Royal Family's Dining Table","place_zh":"餐厅","place_en":"Dining Room","transcript_zh":"这里是餐厅……父王一向偏爱壁炉前的座位，而我用餐时，林克总习惯守在入口附近。现在回想起我接连去拿第二块、甚至第三块水果蛋糕时，林克脸上那副惊讶的表情，还是忍不住想笑。","transcript_en":"The dining hall... Father was partial to the seat in front of the fireplace, and Link preferred to stand watch near the entrance while I ate. I still laugh when I remember the look of surprise on Link's face as I returned for my second...and then third helping of fruit cake."},{"seq":38,"id":"vm_zelda_003","no":"No.003","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-746,"y":-254,"z":104,"gx":-254,"gy":746,"gz":104,"title_zh":"一去不返的景色","title_en":"A Missing View","place_zh":"观察室","place_en":"Observation Room","transcript_zh":"我以前很喜欢在这间观察室里眺望城邑……如今眼前的景象早已物是人非，但……我一定会让它恢复往日的模样。","transcript_en":"I loved gazing out at castle town here in the observation room... The view is completely different now, but...I will see to its restoration."},{"seq":39,"id":"vm_zelda_004","no":"No.004","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-830,"y":-356,"z":109,"gx":-356,"gy":830,"gz":109,"title_zh":"坚不可摧的城寨","title_en":"Sturdy Fortifications","place_zh":"三殿","place_en":"First Gatehouse","transcript_zh":"三殿是进入海拉鲁城堡的最外围关口。虽然城墙多处已经坍塌，但塔楼似乎依然坚固。这里很适合用来存放日后修复城堡所需的物资。","transcript_en":"The first gatehouse is the outermost point of entry to Hyrule Castle. While the ramparts themselves are crumbling in many places, the towers appear to have endured. This seems like an excellent place to store the materials we will need as we work to restore the castle."},{"seq":40,"id":"vm_zelda_005","no":"No.005","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-829,"y":-356,"z":60,"gx":-356,"gy":829,"gz":60,"title_zh":"来龙去脉","title_en":"The Honest Truth","place_zh":"警卫室","place_en":"Guards' Chamber","transcript_zh":"警卫室。不担任我的贴身护卫时，林克常会来这里和士兵们一起训练。唔……他们有一次也让我加入试了试，结果我射出的箭不仅偏离了靶心，还擦着了火把的火苗，害得大家手忙脚乱地赶忙救火……","transcript_en":"The guards' chamber. When he was not occupied by his duties as my protector, Link would often come here to train alongside the regular soldiers. Hm... They once let me join in, but the arrow I loosed went...off target. It also caught the flame of a torch, and everyone frantically raced to put out the resulting fire..."},{"seq":41,"id":"vm_zelda_006","no":"No.006","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1110,"y":-400,"z":22,"gx":-400,"gy":1110,"gz":22,"title_zh":"传说中的大盗","title_en":"The Great Bandit","place_zh":"牢房","place_en":"Lockup","transcript_zh":"据我所知，从未有过罪大恶极到需要被关进这里的犯人。不过我倒是记得，很久很久以前曾有一位名叫“拉姆达”的大盗在此落网，只是近来他似乎更因独到的时尚品味而声名大噪呢。","transcript_en":"As far as I am aware, there were never criminals foul enough to warrant imprisonment here. And while I do recall a bandit named \"Misko\" being captured long, long ago, it seems in recent times they have risen to greater fame for their keen sense of fashion."},{"seq":42,"id":"vm_zelda_007","no":"No.007","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1188,"y":-242,"z":10,"gx":-242,"gy":1188,"gz":10,"title_zh":"往日的繁华","title_en":"Busy Days Gone By","place_zh":"船坞","place_en":"Docks","transcript_zh":"昔日这座船坞整日舟楫往来、络绎不绝。多亏了四方商贾云集，这里曾是城堡里最热闹的地方。如今人去楼空，显得格外冷清……一想到它曾经的繁华，这份寂寥便愈发令人感伤。","transcript_en":"Ships would come and go all day here at the docks. It truly was the most lively part of the castle, and it always felt thus thanks to the numerous merchants. It feels lonely now, abandoned as it is... A feeling magnified as I reflect on what it once was."},{"seq":43,"id":"vm_zelda_008","no":"No.008","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1069,"y":-156,"z":214,"gx":-156,"gy":1069,"gz":214,"title_zh":"秘密","title_en":"A King's Secret","place_zh":"图书馆","place_en":"Library","transcript_zh":"城堡的图书馆，如今已布满灰尘。乍看之下着实令人忧心，但只要费些心思修补，绝大多数藏书应该都能抢救回来。父王平日并不怎么看书，却常常光顾这里。真好奇他究竟是来做什么的呢……","transcript_en":"The castle's library, now covered in dust. At first glance, I found this worrying, but I believe nearly all the books can be salvaged with some effort. Though Father never cared much for books, he would often visit this place. I wonder why..."},{"seq":44,"id":"vm_zelda_009","no":"No.009","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1063,"y":-253,"z":335,"gx":-253,"gy":1063,"gz":335,"title_zh":"避难壕","title_en":"A Place of Shelter","place_zh":"王座厅","place_en":"Throne Room","transcript_zh":"尽管王座如今空置着，这片空间却仍诉说着许多往事。比如，王座后方的雕像格外坚固，紧急关头可作藏身之处——但历代坐在这张王座上的人，却从未有人选择躲进去过。","transcript_en":"Though this throne sits vacant, the space it occupies still speaks volumes. For instance, while the sculpture behind the throne is especially sturdy and serves as a hiding place in an emergency, no one that occupied that seat has ever chosen to use it."},{"seq":45,"id":"vm_zelda_010","no":"No.010","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1066,"y":-255,"z":465,"gx":-255,"gy":1066,"gz":465,"title_zh":"不报时的钟","title_en":"The Bell That Tolled","place_zh":"钟楼","place_en":"Bell Tower","transcript_zh":"钟楼……关于它的记忆，总是伴随着深深的无力感。每当钟声敲响，都在提醒我修行尚未圆满。而我最后一次听到它鸣响，正是它向我们发出灾厄降临的警报之时。","transcript_en":"The bell tower... My memories of it are filled with a terrible sense of helplessness. When that bell tolled, it reminded me that my training was incomplete. And the last time I heard it ring out, it was warning us of the Calamity's arrival."},{"seq":46,"id":"vm_zelda_011","no":"No.011","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-993,"y":-325,"z":300,"gx":-325,"gy":993,"gz":300,"title_zh":"冰冷的床铺","title_en":"A Neglected Room","place_zh":"塞尔达公主的房间","place_en":"Princess Zelda's Room","transcript_zh":"我的房间……比起这里，我待在书房的时间要多得多。侍从们或许也觉得意外吧，因为我常常拉上床幔，好掩饰自己又一次偷偷溜出去继续研究的事实。","transcript_en":"My room... I spent far less time here than I did in my study. That fact may have surprised my attendants, as I often closed the bed curtains to hide the fact I had once again slipped away to continue my research."},{"seq":47,"id":"vm_zelda_012","no":"No.012","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-995,"y":-379,"z":314,"gx":-379,"gy":995,"gz":314,"title_zh":"坚强的公主","title_en":"A Strong Princess","place_zh":"塞尔达公主的书房","place_en":"Princess Zelda's Study","transcript_zh":"我的书房……在这间荒凉破败的屋子角落里，我发现了一朵静谧公主……它究竟在暗处默默等待了几年，甚至几十年，才终于等到合适的时机绽放呢？想不到我曾以为静谧公主注定会灭绝。你比任何人都要坚强啊……","transcript_en":"My study... I found a silent princess in a corner of this desolate room... How many years—or decades—has it patiently waited for the right conditions, that it might finally emerge? To think I once believed the silent princess was doomed to extinction. You're stronger than anyone..."},{"seq":48,"id":"vm_zelda_013","no":"No.013","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-915,"y":-363,"z":284,"gx":-363,"gy":915,"gz":284,"title_zh":"昔日的露台","title_en":"Memories at the Gazebo","place_zh":"海拉鲁城堡凉亭","place_en":"Hyrule Castle Gazebo","transcript_zh":"在众多观景处之中，我最喜欢的就是这里。我记得曾和母后一起在这里度过许多时光。那时的父王还常常展露笑颜……不知有朝一日，我们是否还能像当年那样一同欢笑。","transcript_en":"Among the many overlooks, this is my favorite. I remember spending time with Mother here. Back then, Father still laughed—frequently... I wonder if the day will come when we can laugh together like that again."},{"seq":49,"id":"vm_zelda_014","no":"No.014","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-430,"y":-247,"z":24,"gx":-247,"gy":430,"gz":24,"title_zh":"城邑的喷泉","title_en":"Castle Town Fountain","place_zh":"中央广场遗迹","place_en":"Central Square","transcript_zh":"这里是海拉鲁城邑的中心，也就是中央广场。喷泉周围总是熙熙攘攘，游人与商贩络绎不绝，热闹非凡。这里的氛围与气息有时会勾起我心底的怀念，让我想起小时候母后在这里给我买的那顶花冠。","transcript_en":"This is the center of Castle Town, otherwise known as Central Square. The fountain area is crowded with people and vendors—it's always so lively. The mood and scents here sometimes cause a wave of nostalgia in me, reminding me of the flower crown Mother bought me here when I was little."},{"seq":50,"id":"vm_zelda_015","no":"No.015","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-647,"y":78,"z":32,"gx":78,"gy":647,"gz":32,"title_zh":"大圣堂的回忆","title_en":"Cathedral Reminiscence","place_zh":"海拉鲁大圣堂遗迹","place_en":"Hyrule Cathedral","transcript_zh":"海拉鲁大圣堂遗迹……我曾无数次来这里祈祷，期盼体内的力量能够早日觉醒……这里虽能给我带来些许慰藉，但想起那些始终未能得到回应的祈愿，心中难免还是有些苦涩……","transcript_en":"The ruins of Hyrule Cathedral... I often came here to pray that my powers would finally awaken... Though this place does bring me comfort, I also feel bitter at my many unanswered prayers..."},{"seq":51,"id":"vm_zelda_016","no":"No.016","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-360,"y":-244,"z":21,"gx":-244,"gy":360,"gz":21,"title_zh":"安魂的祈愿","title_en":"Requiem for the Dead","place_zh":"海拉鲁城邑遗迹","place_en":"Hyrule Castle Town Ruins","transcript_zh":"一座纪念碑……据说带着遗憾离世的亡灵会沉入地底深处，为了追寻光芒而四处徘徊……我打算在那些蒙受惨重牺牲的地方也立起这样的纪念碑，祈愿它们能为那些彷徨的灵魂带去一丝光亮。","transcript_en":"A memorial... It is said that spirits who are weighed down with regret when they pass on sink deep beneath the ground and wander in search of light... I will place similar memorials at scenes of great loss and pray they will bring light to those wandering souls."},{"seq":52,"id":"vm_zelda_017","no":"No.017","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-811,"y":-675,"z":15,"gx":-675,"gy":811,"gz":15,"title_zh":"禁地","title_en":"Barred from the Prison","place_zh":"监狱遗迹","place_en":"Castle Town Prison","transcript_zh":"护城河桥的对面是一座监狱，用来关押犯下重罪的犯人。从小到大，我一直被严禁踏足桥的那一侧。","transcript_en":"Beyond the moat bridge lies a prison where those who have committed grave crimes are sent. Ever since I was small, I have been forbidden to cross here."},{"seq":53,"id":"vm_zelda_018","no":"No.018","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1017,"y":-1267,"z":102,"gx":-1267,"gy":1017,"gz":102,"title_zh":"幸存之人的义务","title_en":"Our Responsibility","place_zh":"王室古代研究所遗迹","place_en":"Royal Ancient Lab Ruins","transcript_zh":"这里曾是一座颇具规模的研究设施，但在遭受灾厄摧毁后，如今只剩下了王室古代研究所遗迹。普尔亚尤其为当年在这里失落的知识与样本痛心不已，不过我们可以重新开始。现在轮到我们去创造能够留给后世的成果了。","transcript_en":"This was once an impressive research site, but after being devastated by the Calamity, it is now known as the Royal Ancient Lab Ruins. Purah in particular has lamented the knowledge and samples that were lost here, but we can start again. It's our turn to build something we can leave to future generations."},{"seq":54,"id":"vm_zelda_019","no":"No.019","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1609,"y":-1667,"z":113,"gx":-1667,"gy":1609,"gz":113,"title_zh":"玛丽塔的纪念碑","title_en":"Maritta Memorial","place_zh":"玛丽塔交易所遗迹","place_en":"Maritta Exchange Ruins","transcript_zh":"这片土地遭到了怪物的践踏。当初想着附近有深谷作天然屏障，又有利特族在旁守望，便觉得无需额外加强防卫。遗憾的是，事实证明这个判断错了。愿在这里逝去的人们，都能在海利亚女神的怀抱中得到安息……","transcript_en":"The land here has been trampled by monsters. With the deep valley nearby and the Rito already watching over the area, there seemed little need for additional protection. Unfortunately, that proved an incorrect assumption. I pray that those who lost their lives here found peace with Goddess Hylia..."},{"seq":55,"id":"vm_zelda_020","no":"No.020","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1776,"y":-1550,"z":106,"gx":-1550,"gy":1776,"gz":106,"title_zh":"移动的驿站","title_en":"Solitary Moving Stable","place_zh":"海拉鲁大森林","place_en":"Great Hyrule Forest","transcript_zh":"听说玛丽塔驿站的人们才刚搬到这里，难怪四周堆满了木箱。驿站最初是由游牧民创办的，用来招待过往旅人——如今驿站里的帐篷，似乎就是那个时代留下的传统。现在的驿站大多固定在一处，像这样能够迁徙的驿站可真是少见。","transcript_en":"I've been told the people of Serenne Stable just moved here, hence the many wooden boxes all around. Originally, stables were started up by nomadic people who would host travelers—it seems the tents at these stables are a relic of such times. Nowadays, stables stay put, so finding a mobile one such as this is a rare thing."},{"seq":56,"id":"vm_zelda_021","no":"No.021","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-3122,"y":226,"z":174,"gx":226,"gy":3122,"gz":174,"title_zh":"沉眠于黑暗的遗迹","title_en":"Slumbering Ruins","place_zh":"德依布朗遗迹","place_en":"Thyphlo Ruins","transcript_zh":"已经确认德依布朗遗迹里存在一座神庙。这片漆黑，莫非是针对退魔之剑所选之人的试炼吗？只是，我恐怕没法再往深处走了。难道要请他来调查吗？不，这种事我不想依赖他。","transcript_en":"The existence of a shrine has been confirmed here at Thyphlo Ruins. Could that darkness act as a test to the one chosen by the sword that seals the darkness? I don't think I can go much farther, however. I wonder if I will have to ask him to come investigate? No, I don't want to have to rely on him for this."},{"seq":57,"id":"vm_zelda_022","no":"No.022","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-3749,"y":1554,"z":100,"gx":1554,"gy":3749,"gz":100,"title_zh":"化石调查的收获","title_en":"Importance of Fossil Studies","place_zh":"奥尔汀大化石","place_en":"Eldin Great Skeleton","transcript_zh":"奥尔汀大化石……海拉鲁的地质调查向来停滞不前，但这其实蕴含着无比珍贵的价值！通过深入研究，我们不仅能查明物种灭绝的经过与成因，还能找到环境剧变或灾害的痕迹，甚至有可能预防它们再次发生！而这一切的线索都系于化石之上。我们无论如何都必须加大对化石的研究力度。","transcript_en":"The Eldin Great Skeleton... Geological surveys of Hyrule have largely been at a standstill, but they could be incredibly valuable! Through careful study, we could identify extinction events and their causes... We could see evidence of environmental changes or disasters and possibly prevent them from happening again! And this all ties back to fossils. We simply must put more effort into their study."},{"seq":58,"id":"vm_zelda_023","no":"No.023","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2725,"y":-1033,"z":-78,"gx":-1033,"gy":2725,"gz":-78,"title_zh":"忘却神殿","title_en":"Forgotten Temple","place_zh":"忘却神殿","place_en":"Forgotten Temple","transcript_zh":"据推测，这座遗迹的历史可以追溯到王国建立之初。这一带分布着许多守护者，想必过去曾存放着极为珍贵的东西。此外，根据古籍记载，女神像后方原本还有一间密室，只是现在似乎已经被泥沙掩埋了。","transcript_en":"These ruins are thought to date back to the kingdom's founding. It seems likely that something of great value was once here, as there are many Guardians in the area. Additionally, according to ancient documents, there was a room beyond the Goddess Statue, but it now appears to be buried in sediment."},{"seq":59,"id":"vm_zelda_024","no":"No.024","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-3535,"y":-962,"z":234,"gx":-962,"gy":3535,"gz":234,"title_zh":"以北洛美之名","title_en":"Bearing the Name North Lomei","place_zh":"北洛美城堡遗迹","place_en":"North Lomei Labyrinth","transcript_zh":"北洛美城堡遗迹不仅环境严酷，构造也果真如迷宫般错综复杂……它虽筑有高墙，却与寻常要塞大不相同。这里曾安放着留给退魔之剑持有者的古代遗物，或许它本身就是某种试炼或考验吧？看来，这件事还是得请林克来调查一番了……","transcript_en":"The North Lomei Labyrinth is a harsh environment and an unsurprisingly labyrinthine structure... It has high walls but is otherwise unlike most fortifications. It did once hold an ancient relic meant for the bearer of the sword that seals the darkness, so perhaps it was a trial or test of some kind? I may just have to ask Link to investigate..."},{"seq":60,"id":"vm_zelda_025","no":"No.025","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-3571,"y":-3414,"z":367,"gx":-3414,"gy":3571,"gz":367,"title_zh":"明弗拉的秘泉","title_en":"Goflam's Secret Hot Spring","place_zh":"戈弗拉姆的秘密温泉","place_en":"Goflam's Secret Hot Spring","transcript_zh":"隐匿在深山中的一处温泉。我循着动物痛苦的哀鸣找来，发现一匹受了伤的马正泡在舒适的泉水里疗伤。我本打算去调查北面山顶的那具巨大化石，但这匹马看起来如此亲人……算了，化石又不会长脚跑掉。眼下，离这里最近的驿站有多远呢……","transcript_en":"A hot spring hidden deep within the mountain. I heard the pained cries of an animal and have now found an injured horse soothing its wounds in the refreshing waters. I had meant to investigate the immense skeleton on the northern summit, but this horse seems so friendly... Oh, the skeleton isn't going anywhere. Now how far away is the nearest stable..."},{"seq":61,"id":"vm_zelda_026","no":"No.026","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2572,"y":-1645,"z":233,"gx":-1645,"gy":2572,"gz":233,"title_zh":"金黄色的马","title_en":"The Golden Horse","place_zh":"雪原驿站","place_en":"Snowfield Stable","transcript_zh":"我偶然遇到一匹受伤的马，便将它带到雪原驿站来疗伤。我本想带它一起踏上旅途，但它还需要更多时间休养，于是我只好默默祈祷，希望有位心地善良的人能来好好照料它。对了，我还用从母后那里学来的祈祷词，为它的鬃毛也祈了福呢。","transcript_en":"I came upon an injured horse and brought it to Snowfield Stable to be treated. I had hoped to bring it with me on my travels, but it needed more time to recover, so instead I offered a prayer that some kindhearted person would come to care for it. I may have also said a prayer—one I learned from Mother—to help with its mane."},{"seq":62,"id":"vm_zelda_027","no":"No.027","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1770,"y":-3244,"z":118,"gx":-3244,"gy":1770,"gz":118,"title_zh":"咖罗的烦恼","title_en":"Galli's Worries","place_zh":"白诘报社","place_en":"Lucky Clover Gazette","transcript_zh":"我跟利特驿站的咖罗聊了聊，他似乎正在发愁驿站还能不能继续经营下去，不过听说居然有一家报社提出想把这里买下来……无论如何，报社和驿站对海拉鲁来说都是不可或缺的好事，说不定双方能在这里找到共存之道呢。","transcript_en":"I spoke with Galli at Rito Stable, who seems worried about whether he can keep the stable open, though it sounds like he's had an offer to sell it to a newspaper, of all things... In any case, Hyrule is all the better with newspapers and stables; maybe the two can find a way to coexist here."},{"seq":63,"id":"vm_zelda_028","no":"No.028","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1804,"y":-3302,"z":121,"gx":-3302,"gy":1804,"gz":121,"title_zh":"翔天之翼","title_en":"Wings Soaring the Skies","place_zh":"利特村","place_en":"Rito Village","transcript_zh":"一百年前，神兽瓦·梅德翱翔于天际，而利特族的英杰力巴尔总是毫不掩饰对自己操控技艺的自豪。或许不少人会对他的傲气敬而远之，但我却从中感受到了鼓舞——从许多细微之处都能看出，他其实一直在无人看见的地方刻苦磨炼，好让自己的实力配得上那些豪言壮语。","transcript_en":"A hundred years ago, the Divine Beast Vah Medoh soared through the sky, and the Rito Champion, Revali, was ever quick to celebrate his skill as its pilot. Many may have been put off by his bravado, but I found it encouraging; there were often subtle signs that he was someone who worked hard, unseen, to be certain he could back up his bluster."},{"seq":64,"id":"vm_zelda_029","no":"No.029","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1836,"y":-3485,"z":153,"gx":-3485,"gy":1836,"gz":153,"title_zh":"追念力巴尔","title_en":"Honoring Revali","place_zh":"村前鱼塘","place_en":"Fishpond in Front of the Village","transcript_zh":"力巴尔……每当我陷入困境时，你总是第一个飞奔到我身边。抱歉，在你最需要帮助的时候，我却没能帮上忙。以你的性子，想必会把这百年的等待轻描淡写地说成不值一提的小事吧……你当初对林克那么严苛，也是为了确认他有足够的能力保护我，对吧？","transcript_en":"Revali... You were always quickest to rush to my side when I struggled. I'm sorry I wasn't able to help you when you were in need. You being you, I imagine you shrugged off waiting a hundred years like it was the smallest inconvenience... You were so tough on Link to make sure he could protect me, weren't you?"},{"seq":65,"id":"vm_zelda_030","no":"No.030","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1817,"y":-3571,"z":167,"gx":-3571,"gy":1817,"gz":167,"title_zh":"他的名字……","title_en":"His Name...","place_zh":"利特村","place_en":"Rito Village","transcript_zh":"啊，利特村。利特族英杰力巴尔的故乡。在这里，他似乎被传颂为传奇般的人物，他的弓更是只授予利特族最强战士的至高荣誉。力巴尔，你以前最讨厌别人在背后议论你了，但恐怕你的事迹，还会在这里流传很久很久呢……","transcript_en":"Ah, Rito Village. Hometown of Revali, the Rito Champion. It seems he is spoken of as a legend here, and his bow is an honor bestowed on the best Rito warrior. You did hate other people talking about you, Revali, but I'm afraid your story will live on here for quite some time still..."},{"seq":66,"id":"vm_zelda_031","no":"No.031","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1803,"y":-3604,"z":213,"gx":-3604,"gy":1803,"gz":213,"title_zh":"力巴尔广场","title_en":"Revali's Landing","place_zh":"力巴尔广场","place_en":"Revali's Landing","transcript_zh":"这座广场以力巴尔的名字命名。据说灾厄爆发那天，他正是从这里登上神兽的，人们便以此为念，为广场冠上了他的名字。地面上的图案百年来一直被精心维护、丝毫未变，足见村里的人们对这位传奇战士怀有多么深厚的敬意。","transcript_en":"This plaza has been named after Revali. It's said that he boarded the Divine Beast from here the day the Calamity began, and for that reason, and in his honor, it was given its name. The fact that the design on the ground has been carefully maintained and unchanged for a hundred years shows the immense respect the village holds for their legendary warrior."},{"seq":67,"id":"vm_zelda_032","no":"No.032","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1827,"y":-3626,"z":218,"gx":-3626,"gy":1827,"gz":218,"title_zh":"未来的族长","title_en":"The Future Elder","place_zh":"卡昂的家","place_en":"Kaneli's House","transcript_zh":"利特村的族长卡昂告诉我，他打算把族长之位传给特巴。他过去一直认为，单凭一名利特族战士很难同时肩负起治理村庄与守护族人的重任。可当他亲眼看到林克与特巴并肩迎战瓦·梅德之后……自然也就彻底放心把利特族的未来交到特巴手上了。","transcript_en":"Kaneli, the village elder of the Rito, told me that he intends to pass his role on to Teba. He hadn't believed that a single Rito could serve both as the elder and the protector of the village at the same time. But when he saw Link and Teba face Medoh... Needless to say, he has no concerns whether the Rito will be in good hands with Teba."},{"seq":68,"id":"vm_zelda_033","no":"No.033","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2316,"y":-3791,"z":161,"gx":-3791,"gy":2316,"gz":161,"title_zh":"备受崇敬的战士","title_en":"A Warrior to Aspire To","place_zh":"飞行训练场","place_en":"Flight Range","transcript_zh":"许多利特族人都憧憬着成为像力巴尔一样的战士，村里的孩子们也大都以他为榜样苦练弓术。而飞行训练场，正是他们平日训练的主要去处。虽说他从前总嘴硬说这片训练场只属于他一个人，但他其实一直都在为后世创造更美好的世界而努力，而这份梦想也正是在这里延续了下来。","transcript_en":"Many of the Rito aspire to be like Revali, and most of the children follow his example and practice with the bow. The Flight Range is where they do the majority of their training. Though he always claimed the practice range was only meant for him, he did strive to make a better world for future generations, and that dream lives on here."},{"seq":69,"id":"vm_zelda_034","no":"No.034","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2882,"y":-2832,"z":564,"gx":-2832,"gy":2882,"gz":564,"title_zh":"1万年前的痕迹","title_en":"Scar from 10,000 Years Ago","place_zh":"海布拉山山顶","place_en":"Hebra Peak","transcript_zh":"如今再仰望海布拉山，我终于能够接受一百年前怎么也不敢相信的事实——一万年前削平这座山峰的能量冲击，确实是从城堡方向袭来的。或许这片群山一直在试图向我们诉说过去的历史……我应当组建一支调查队前来勘察，以免错漏了其他类似的讯息。","transcript_en":"When I look at the Hebra Mountains now, I can accept something I couldn't one hundred years ago; the energy blast that shaped the peak 10,000 years in the past indeed came from the castle. Perhaps these mountains were always trying to teach us about the past... I should put together a survey team to investigate and make sure we aren't missing any other such messages."},{"seq":70,"id":"vm_zelda_035","no":"No.035","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-441,"y":-3474,"z":278,"gx":-3474,"gy":441,"gz":278,"title_zh":"后悔与忏悔","title_en":"Regret and Repentance","place_zh":"古代石柱群","place_en":"Ancient Columns","transcript_zh":"这些古代石柱标志着此处曾矗立着一座神庙……灾厄之前，我为了调查遗迹四处奔走，常常专挑那些难以抵达的险峻之地。即便如此，林克也总能找到我。那时候我对他真是太过分了……后来我向他道歉时，他自然是宽慰我说自己并不介意。可一想到曾让他受了那么多委屈，我至今仍深感愧疚。","transcript_en":"These ancient columns mark where a shrine once stood... Before the Calamity, when I was frantically searching ruins, I would often seek hard-to-reach places. Despite this, Link always managed to find me. I was so terrible to him then... And of course when I apologized for it later, he reassured me that he didn't mind. I regret putting him through that."},{"seq":71,"id":"vm_zelda_036","no":"No.036","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-552,"y":-2917,"z":169,"gx":-2917,"gy":552,"gz":169,"title_zh":"饲养员的忧虑","title_en":"Worries of a Caretaker","place_zh":"塔邦挞大桥驿站","place_en":"Tabantha Bridge Stable","transcript_zh":"塔邦挞大桥驿站是当年荒废多年的塔邦挞大桥重修时建起来的。然而大桥在灾厄中损毁，直到最近才重新通行，因此驿站的负责人很担心根本没人知道这里有座驿站。他买来几只山羊，打算用山羊黄油研制一道招牌菜，只不过在饲养山羊这件事上，他显然还有不少功课要补呢……","transcript_en":"Tabantha Bridge Stable was built when the Tabantha Great Bridge was repaired after many years of neglect. However, the bridge was destroyed during the Calamity and only recently reopened, so the manager here is worried that no one knows about his stable. He purchased some goats and is trying to develop a signature dish using goat-milk butter, but there are definitely some things he needs to learn about the animals..."},{"seq":72,"id":"vm_zelda_037","no":"No.037","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-883,"y":-2254,"z":110,"gx":-2254,"gy":883,"gz":110,"title_zh":"雷鸣不再的台地","title_en":"The Plateau Where Thunder Fell Silent","place_zh":"雷之台地","place_en":"Thundra Plateau","transcript_zh":"雷之台地因昔日终日雷声轰鸣不绝而得名。我原本还有些犹豫要不要来这里，但雷鸣消散之后，这里竟……如此宁静祥和。那经年不息的雷电，莫非与过去这里的神庙有关吗……或许，那也是某种试炼吧。","transcript_en":"Thundra Plateau was so named for the endless rolling thunder that used to echo across it. I was hesitant to even come here, but with the thunder gone, this place is...incredibly peaceful. I wonder if the thunder was connected to the shrine that was here before... Maybe it was some sort of test."},{"seq":73,"id":"vm_zelda_038","no":"No.038","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":695,"y":-1622,"z":140,"gx":-1622,"gy":-695,"gz":140,"title_zh":"学习需用心","title_en":"Learning to Have an Open Heart","place_zh":"撒丁公园遗迹","place_en":"Sanidin Park Ruins","transcript_zh":"林克常在撒丁公园遗迹这片开阔的草地上陪我练习驭马。我记得当时还心想，自己骑术本就不差，他恐怕也没什么能教我的。然而，他教给我的并非骑马的技巧，而是更加深刻的东西——那就是体谅与同理心。","transcript_en":"Link often used the vast meadows of the Sanidin Park Ruins to help me practice horse handling. I recall thinking there was little I could learn from him. After all, I am quite capable on horseback. However, it wasn't technique he was showing me but rather deeper lessons in compassion."},{"seq":74,"id":"vm_zelda_039","no":"No.039","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":342,"y":-2263,"z":344,"gx":-2263,"gy":-342,"gz":344,"title_zh":"樱花的渊源","title_en":"Spreading Cherry Blossoms","place_zh":"萨托利山","place_en":"Satori Mountain","transcript_zh":"萨托利山的樱花树……以前明明只有两棵，现在看来却增加了不少。不过，相传樱花拥有净化邪恶的力量……它们之所以纷纷绽放，究竟是因为灾厄已经消散，还是为了应对某种即将到来的新威胁呢？","transcript_en":"The Satori Mountain cherry blossom tree... While there were only two of these trees before, there seem to be many more now. However, it is said that cherry blossoms can purify evil... Does that mean more are appearing because the Calamity has disappeared, or are they appearing in preparation for some new threat?"},{"seq":75,"id":"vm_zelda_040","no":"No.040","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1274,"y":-1431,"z":32,"gx":-1431,"gy":-1274,"gz":32,"title_zh":"奇缘驿站","title_en":"The \"Meet-Up\" Stable","place_zh":"平原外围的驿站","place_en":"Outskirt Stable","transcript_zh":"这座驿站名叫平原外围的驿站，但格鲁德族似乎称它为“邂逅驿站”。乌尔波扎曾告诉我，许多芭伊都是在这里第一次见到沃伊的。或许驿站老板也深谙此道，所以才特意在店里挂出了樱花树的地图——那可是再浪漫不过的地方了……","transcript_en":"This stable is called Outskirt Stable, but the Gerudo apparently refer to it as the \"meet-up stable.\" Urbosa told me that this is where many vai see voe for the first time. Perhaps the stable master knows this, and that's why a map to cherry-blossoms—quite the romantic setting—is on display..."},{"seq":76,"id":"vm_zelda_041","no":"No.041","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2162,"y":-1581,"z":-22,"gx":-1581,"gy":-2162,"gz":-22,"title_zh":"环境恶劣的大地","title_en":"Harsh Lands","place_zh":"格鲁德峡谷入口","place_en":"Gerudo Canyon Pass","transcript_zh":"格鲁德峡谷入口处干涸龟裂的岩壁，无声地诉说着这片土地的干旱少雨。虽然这里的酷热还不至于必须仰仗高级药剂才能忍受，但只要一踏入此地，灼人的热浪便扑面而来，仿佛在警示着前方沙漠的严酷。","transcript_en":"The dried rock face of the entrance to Gerudo Canyon shows how little rain this region gets. While it may not be so perilously hot as to require advanced elixirs, the sweltering air does strike you the moment you set foot here, and it serves as a warning of the rugged desert ahead."},{"seq":77,"id":"vm_zelda_042","no":"No.042","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2304,"y":-1956,"z":0,"gx":-1956,"gy":-2304,"gz":0,"title_zh":"瓦·娜波力斯的出土现场","title_en":"Vah Naboris Excavation Site","place_zh":"格鲁德峡谷","place_en":"Gerudo Canyon","transcript_zh":"这里就是神兽瓦·娜波力斯的发掘地。听格鲁德族的英杰乌尔波扎说，操控神兽的感觉与她驾驭雷电颇为相似——两者都需要极其强大的意志力，只不过操控神兽要比那艰难得多、得多。","transcript_en":"This is where Divine Beast Vah Naboris was found. According to the Gerudo Champion, Urbosa, controlling the Divine Beast was similar in practice to how she controlled lightning. Both required considerable force of will, but with the Divine Beast, it was much, much more difficult."},{"seq":78,"id":"vm_zelda_043","no":"No.043","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2235,"y":-2789,"z":29,"gx":-2789,"gy":-2235,"gz":29,"title_zh":"怪物扎根的水井","title_en":"Monsters in the Well","place_zh":"格鲁德峡谷驿站","place_en":"Gerudo Canyon Stable","transcript_zh":"有报告称格鲁德峡谷驿站的水井里出现了怪物。虽然我们已经用岩石封住了它们巢穴的入口，但我担心这终究不是长久之计……为防万一，我也叮嘱了驿站负责人暂时不要使用这口井。虽说会带来诸多不便，但安全始终是第一位的。","transcript_en":"There have been reports of monsters in the well here at Gerudo Canyon Stable, and though we have sealed the entrance of their den with rocks, I doubt that is a permanent solution... As an additional measure, I have also told the stable manager to avoid using the well. It will be inconvenient, but safety is of the highest priority."},{"seq":79,"id":"vm_zelda_044","no":"No.044","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2322,"y":-2934,"z":32,"gx":-2934,"gy":-2322,"gz":32,"title_zh":"格鲁德沙漠","title_en":"Gerudo Desert","place_zh":"格鲁德沙漠入口","place_en":"Gerudo Desert Gateway","transcript_zh":"或许是我的错觉吧，总觉得这里的空气比过去更加炽热了。然而，尽管酷暑难耐、环境看似荒芜，我却觉得这片沙漠蕴藏着比任何地方都要旺盛的生命力。大概是因为我亲眼见证过以这里为家的人们是多么坚强吧。","transcript_en":"It may be my imagination, but it feels like there is even more heat in the air here than in the past. And despite that oppressive heat and the seemingly desolate environment, I believe there is more vitality in this desert than anywhere else. Perhaps I feel this way because I have seen the strength of those who call this place home."},{"seq":80,"id":"vm_zelda_045","no":"No.045","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2521,"y":-3211,"z":23,"gx":-3211,"gy":-2521,"gz":23,"title_zh":"绿洲蜃景","title_en":"Desert Oasis","place_zh":"卡拉卡拉集市","place_en":"Kara Kara Bazaar","transcript_zh":"卡拉卡拉集市为那些无法进入格鲁德小镇的人们提供了交易的场所。既然小镇只允许女性入内，这样的安排实在非常周全。乌尔波扎叮嘱我在这里要提防依盖队，但我实在难以想象他们会在如此人潮涌动的地方发动袭击。她未免有些操心过度了。","transcript_en":"Kara Kara Bazaar serves as a trading post for those who cannot enter Gerudo Town. It's a smart thing, since the town only allows women to enter. Urbosa warned me to be on alert for the Yiga Clan here, but I cannot imagine they would attack in a place as crowded as this. She worries a bit too much."},{"seq":81,"id":"vm_zelda_046","no":"No.046","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2896,"y":-3817,"z":44,"gx":-3817,"gy":-2896,"gz":44,"title_zh":"年幼的族长","title_en":"The Young Chief","place_zh":"格鲁德小镇","place_en":"Gerudo Town","transcript_zh":"格鲁德族的主城——格鲁德小镇，如今由露珠族长治理。她年纪虽小，却为了族人竭尽全力，接连克服了神兽与依盖队的威胁。事实上，如今的小镇比以往任何时候都要充满生机！看着她如此勇敢地直面艰难险阻，真令我自愧不如。想当年母后离世时，我只顾着悲痛欲绝，久久无法振作……","transcript_en":"The main settlement of the Gerudo, Gerudo Town, is ruled by Chief Riju. Though young, she seems to be working hard in service to her people, overcoming both the Divine Beast and the threat the Yiga Clan posed. In fact, the town is more lively than ever! It is...humbling to see her face such challenges. When Mother died, I was inconsolable..."},{"seq":82,"id":"vm_zelda_047","no":"No.047","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2956,"y":-3877,"z":50,"gx":-3877,"gy":-2956,"gz":50,"title_zh":"谒见露珠","title_en":"An Audience With Riju","place_zh":"王宫王座厅","place_en":"Royal Palace's Throne Room","transcript_zh":"现任格鲁德族长露珠过去曾留着一头及腰长发——那是唯有格鲁德王族才被允许蓄留的发型。然而如今，她却将长发剪短了。我想，这既是她为自己没能独自阻止神兽与依盖队而立下的自省，也是给自己定下的目标：等到长发重新蓄起之时，她一定要成为像乌尔波扎那样强大的族长。","transcript_en":"The current chief of the Gerudo, Riju, used to have long hair reaching all the way to her waist—a style only permitted to Gerudo royalty. Today, however, she wears it cut short. I believe this is both in penance for not being able to stop the Divine Beast or the Yiga Clan on her own, but also to give herself a goal to aspire to. By the time her hair grows long again, she must be a strong chief like Urbosa was."},{"seq":83,"id":"vm_zelda_048","no":"No.048","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2987,"y":-3855,"z":43,"gx":-3855,"gy":-2987,"gz":43,"title_zh":"帕特丽夏","title_en":"Patricia","place_zh":"王宫庭院","place_en":"Palace Courtyard","transcript_zh":"露珠心爱的沙海象帕特丽夏，似乎是她母亲留给她的礼物。在露珠多年学习与修行的岁月里，她们之间结下了深厚的羁绊。我……觉得她们甚至能够彼此心意相通，尽管我完全听不懂帕特丽夏在说些什么。","transcript_en":"Riju's beloved sand seal, Patricia, was apparently a gift from her mother. They seem to have formed a close bond over the many years of Riju's studies and training. I...think they can even communicate with one another, though I am not able to understand Patricia at all."},{"seq":84,"id":"vm_zelda_049","no":"No.049","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2916,"y":-3899,"z":43,"gx":-3899,"gy":-2916,"gz":43,"title_zh":"格鲁德士兵强化计划","title_en":"Gerudo Soldier Training","place_zh":"兵舍","place_en":"Barracks","transcript_zh":"这里是格鲁德士兵的兵舍。露珠最近提起她想加强士兵们的训练，却又苦于至今收效甚微。听闻此事，我便向她转述了乌尔波扎生前常说的话——格鲁德族应当更加贴近并顺应沙漠。露珠听后恍然大悟，随即对着地图沉思了许久。看来，即便历经百年岁月，乌尔波扎依然能为我们指点迷津啊。","transcript_en":"These are the barracks for Gerudo soldiers. Riju recently spoke of wanting to improve the training her soldiers receive, sharing, too, how she has been frustrated with the results so far. Hearing this, I told her of how Urbosa always felt the Gerudo should be more in touch with the desert. A look of realization crossed Riju's face, and then she spent some time studying a map. It seems Urbosa can offer wise guidance even a hundred years later."},{"seq":85,"id":"vm_zelda_050","no":"No.050","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2929,"y":-3765,"z":43,"gx":-3765,"gy":-2929,"gz":43,"title_zh":"沙海象的回忆","title_en":"Memories of the Sand Seals","place_zh":"沙海象租赁店东门分店","place_en":"Sand-Seal Rental Shop East Gate Booth","transcript_zh":"露珠夸赞我驾驭沙海象的手法很娴熟，其实这全亏了很久以前乌尔波扎的悉心教导。接着，我向露珠讲起当年我忘了带盾牌，结果被沙海象和乌尔波扎双双抛在身后的糗事，把这小姑娘逗得前仰后合！有时我甚至会忘了，眼前这个“小姑娘”已是一族的族长了。","transcript_en":"Riju complimented my technique when handling a sand seal, a skill I only possess thanks to the training Urbosa gave me so long ago. I then told Riju of the time I forgot a shield and was left behind by both my sand seal and Urbosa, and the young girl doubled over laughing! I still sometimes forget that this \"young girl\" is chief of her people."},{"seq":86,"id":"vm_zelda_051","no":"No.051","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2860,"y":-3857,"z":46,"gx":-3857,"gy":-2860,"gz":46,"title_zh":"时隔100年再度挑战","title_en":"Another Attempt, 100 Years Later","place_zh":"高贵酒馆","place_en":"The Noble Canteen","transcript_zh":"我又一次去尝试点格鲁德小镇那款人气饮品「芭伊之梦」，结果还是被告知「为时尚早」。不过店里的人告诉我，等在海外生活的格鲁德年幼孩子们回到小镇时，我可以再来一趟。听说届时会为她们准备特制饮品，到那时再去问问看吧……","transcript_en":"I tried once again to get the popular Gerudo Town drink, Noble Pursuit, and I was once again told I was not ready for it yet. They did tell me I should come back when the young Gerudo children who have been living abroad return to town. Apparently some special drinks will be prepared for their arrival, and I should ask again then..."},{"seq":87,"id":"vm_zelda_052","no":"No.052","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2507,"y":-3762,"z":32,"gx":-3762,"gy":-2507,"gz":32,"title_zh":"不为人知的遗迹","title_en":"Mysterious Ruins","place_zh":"北格鲁德遗迹","place_en":"North Gerudo Ruins","transcript_zh":"北格鲁德遗迹通过一条地下通道与格鲁德小镇相连，那是露珠带我看到的。她告诉我，这是紧急情况下的逃生通道，但除非发生极其重大的灾难，否则很难想象会派上用场。说这话时她笑着，表面上显得很轻松，但我看得出来，她无时无刻不在牵挂着子民们的安危。","transcript_en":"The North Gerudo Ruins are connected to Gerudo Town via an underground pathway that Riju showed me. She told me it was an escape route in the event of an emergency, but that short of some immense disaster, she couldn't imagine using it for such a purpose. She laughed as she said this, and though she seemed unconcerned in the moment, it's clear the safety of her people is never far from her mind."},{"seq":88,"id":"vm_zelda_053","no":"No.053","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1929,"y":-3661,"z":118,"gx":-3661,"gy":-1929,"gz":118,"title_zh":"深穴所通之处","title_en":"Exploring Where the Chasm Leads","place_zh":"比利丁高地的深穴","place_en":"Birida Lookout Chasm","transcript_zh":"这里就是位于比利丁高地附近的深穴……文献中记载，古人曾居住在遥远的地底深处，我推测，像这样的深穴或许正是连接地面与地底的通道……但若想找到证据来证实我的猜想，就需要能全身心投入这项调查的研究人员。得去问问普尔亚，看她认不认识合适且有能力胜任的人选……","transcript_en":"This is the chasm located near Birida Lookout... There are records that suggest ancient people lived far below ground in the Depths, and I suspect holes such as this one could connect the surface to that place... But if I want to find evidence proving my theories, I will need researchers wholly dedicated to the task. I should speak with Purah to see if she knows anyone qualified and capable of tackling this..."},{"seq":89,"id":"vm_zelda_054","no":"No.054","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":3115,"y":-3422,"z":84,"gx":-3422,"gy":-3115,"gz":84,"title_zh":"沙漠中的哨所","title_en":"Desert Watchtower","place_zh":"瞭望台","place_en":"Lookout Post","transcript_zh":"这座瞭望台据说最初是为了监视在沙漠中徘徊的神兽瓦·娜波力斯而建造的，如今则成了观测沙漠地形变化的地方。听说它高得足以越过最猛烈的沙尘暴，加上露珠计划在卡拉卡拉集市建造的灯塔，今后在沙漠中安全通行应该会变得容易许多吧。","transcript_en":"This lookout post was supposedly originally built to keep watch on Divine Beast Vah Naboris as it lumbered through the desert, but now it is a place to observe changes in the desert landscape. I've heard it is tall enough to see above the worst sandstorms, and between this place and the lighthouse Riju has planned for Kara Kara Bazaar, safely traveling the desert should become easier soon."},{"seq":90,"id":"vm_zelda_055","no":"No.055","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":3840,"y":-4857,"z":-21,"gx":-4857,"gy":-3840,"gz":-21,"title_zh":"化石考察的收获","title_en":"Concerning the Fossils","place_zh":"格鲁德大化石","place_en":"Gerudo Great Skeleton","transcript_zh":"巨大的格鲁德大化石就沉睡在这里。传说在很久很久以前，海拉鲁曾是一片汪洋海底。考虑到世界各地陆续发现的海洋生物化石，这个传说恐怕并非空穴来风。只是……我觉得留存下来的化石数量似乎太少了些。难道当年的海洋生物顺着什么通道去往了更深的地方？比如通过比利丁高地附近那样的深穴，一直到了地底……不，我未免想得太远了。","transcript_en":"The immense Gerudo Great Skeleton lies here. Legends say that long, long ago, Hyrule was actually the bottom of a vast ocean. Considering the marine fossils that have been found across the world, I see little reason to doubt this. Except...it seems to me that there are too few fossils. Maybe sea life found routes even deeper? Maybe through chasms like the one near Birida Lookout? Maybe as far as the Depths... No, I'm getting carried away."},{"seq":91,"id":"vm_zelda_056","no":"No.056","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":3331,"y":-1794,"z":72,"gx":-1794,"gy":-3331,"gz":72,"title_zh":"以南洛美之名","title_en":"Bearing the Name South Lomei","place_zh":"南洛美城堡遗迹","place_en":"South Lomei Labyrinth","transcript_zh":"南洛美城堡遗迹是海拉鲁境内三座以「洛美」命名的遗迹之一。每一座构造都极其复杂，环境又十分严酷，探索起来困难重重。话虽如此，里面或许沉睡着重要的古代遗物，最好还是派遣一支专门的调查队前来勘察。","transcript_en":"South Lomei Labyrinth is one of three ruins in Hyrule that have been named after Lomei. Each are incredibly complex in design and present harsh environments, which make them very difficult to explore. That said, they may contain important ancient relics, so it would be best to send out a dedicated survey team here."},{"seq":92,"id":"vm_zelda_057","no":"No.057","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2562,"y":-2053,"z":367,"gx":-2053,"gy":-2562,"gz":367,"title_zh":"追念乌尔波扎","title_en":"Honoring Urbosa","place_zh":"眼镜岩","place_en":"Spectacle Rock","transcript_zh":"乌尔波扎，我终于见到了你曾看过的这片壮丽景色。真希望这一切不必付出那样的代价……但正因为有你和大家教给我的一切，还有我们共同度过的时光，我才能昂首阔步地向前迈进。多亏了你，我已经没关系了……能请你代我转告母后吗？","transcript_en":"I finally get to see all these amazing sights you saw, Urbosa. I wish that it hadn't cost what it did... But thanks to the things you—and everyone else—taught me, and the time we spent together, I can move forward with my head held high. Thanks to you, I am going to be OK... Could you tell my mother that for me, please?"},{"seq":93,"id":"vm_zelda_058","no":"No.058","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1506,"y":-578,"z":19,"gx":-578,"gy":-1506,"gz":19,"title_zh":"驿站村的纪念碑","title_en":"Outpost Memorial","place_zh":"门前驿站村遗迹","place_en":"Gatepost Town Ruins","transcript_zh":"这里曾是一片繁华热闹之地。附近建有好几家旅馆，大道上往来着驻军地的士兵和前往时之神殿的旅人。如今，却只剩下风吹过此地……愿曾在这里生活与驻足的每一个人，都能在女神海利亚的庇佑下安息。","transcript_en":"This area was once alive and bustling with activity. There were several inns nearby, and the roads were busy with soldiers from the local garrison or travelers heading for the Temple of Time. Nowadays, only the wind moves through this place... I pray everyone who passed through here has found peace with Goddess Hylia."},{"seq":94,"id":"vm_zelda_059","no":"No.059","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1497,"y":-539,"z":18,"gx":-539,"gy":-1497,"gz":18,"title_zh":"海拉鲁的建国之地","title_en":"Birthplace of Hyrule","place_zh":"门前驿站村遗迹","place_en":"Gatepost Town Ruins","transcript_zh":"通往初始台地的道路被泥土和岩石填埋了。其中固然有守护者来袭造成的破坏，但有些土石看起来像是人为堆砌的。我想，当年是为了尽可能阻止怪物闯入林克沉睡休养的复苏神庙所在的初始台地吧。可是……我现在该怎么上去呢？","transcript_en":"The passage up to the Great Plateau has been filled with dirt and rocks. Certainly some of this damage was caused by the Guardians' invasion, but some of the debris looks to have been placed deliberately. I imagine the intention was to keep as many monsters as possible from reaching the Great Plateau, where Link recovered in the Shrine of Resurrection. But...how am I supposed to reach the Great Plateau now?"},{"seq":95,"id":"vm_zelda_060","no":"No.060","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1907,"y":-1125,"z":129,"gx":-1125,"gy":-1907,"gz":129,"title_zh":"勇者苏醒","title_en":"The Hero Awakened","place_zh":"修复室","place_en":"Restoration Room","transcript_zh":"正是在这座复苏神庙中，古代希卡族的技术挽救了林克的性命。当他从长达百年的沉睡中苏醒的那一刻，我清晰地感受到了。我的声音能够传达到他那里，真是太好了……","transcript_en":"It was here in the Shrine of Resurrection that ancient Sheikah technology preserved Link's life. I was able to clearly sense when he woke from his hundred-year slumber, and I am so happy that my voice could reach him..."},{"seq":96,"id":"vm_zelda_061","no":"No.061","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2004,"y":-818,"z":116,"gx":-818,"gy":-2004,"gz":116,"title_zh":"沧海桑田","title_en":"The Passage of Time","place_zh":"时之神殿遗迹","place_en":"Temple of Time Ruins","transcript_zh":"许多古籍和文献中都曾提及「时之神殿」之名，但它们所描绘的建筑形制，却都与我们如今见到的这座大相径庭。海拉鲁的历史源远流长，这其中的差异，也是这片土地尚未解开的谜团之一……","transcript_en":"There are several ancient texts and works of literature that speak of the Temple of Time by name, but all of them describe a structure that differs in design from the one we see today. Hyrule's history is long, and this discrepancy is one of the unsolved mysteries of our land..."},{"seq":97,"id":"vm_zelda_062","no":"No.062","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2216,"y":-1291,"z":311,"gx":-1291,"gy":-2216,"gz":311,"title_zh":"必须守护之物","title_en":"A King's Rest","place_zh":"王之墓","place_en":"King's Tomb","transcript_zh":"这里是父王的墓碑。听说当时能为父王做的，也只有垒起这些石头而已……不过，这里真是再合适不过的地方了。他可以长眠于此，永远眺望着海拉鲁……母后，父王，尽管这片大地如今依然满目疮痍，但我向你们起誓，我一定会复兴海拉鲁。请……守护着我吧。","transcript_en":"Father's grave. I heard that stacking these rocks was the best that could be done for him... Well, they could not have picked a better place. That he will rest here, forever looking out over Hyrule... Mother, Father, though the land is still littered with ruins, I promise you that I will restore it. Please... watch over me as I do."},{"seq":98,"id":"vm_zelda_063","no":"No.063","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2256,"y":-788,"z":88,"gx":-788,"gy":-2256,"gz":88,"title_zh":"小屋的主人是……","title_en":"The Hut's Owner","place_zh":"老人的小屋","place_en":"Old Man's Cabin","transcript_zh":"一百年前我来这座山间小屋时，并不知道它的主人是谁。现在想来，难怪我当时说这间屋子「破破烂烂的，早该拆掉了」时，父王会露出一副既为难又落寞的神情。我怎么会想到这竟是父王自己的隐居之处呢……不过，现在再仔细看看……哎呀，父王，这间小屋莫非是您亲手搭的吗？","transcript_en":"When I last visited this mountain hut a hundred years ago, I did not realize who the owner was. Now that I do, it explains why Father looked so troubled—even sad—when I described the building as \"shabby\" and in need of demolition. How could I have guessed it was his own little retreat... Though, looking at it now... Oh, Father, did you build this yourself?"},{"seq":99,"id":"vm_zelda_064","no":"No.064","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1672,"y":-1181,"z":83,"gx":-1181,"gy":-1672,"gz":83,"title_zh":"林克的心理阴影","title_en":"Link's Trauma","place_zh":"青蛙池塘","place_en":"Hopper Pond","transcript_zh":"青蛙池塘从前满是速速蛙……大概是被怪物给吓跑了吧？说起来，这里正是我好不容易抓到一只速速蛙的地方。当时我兴奋极了，想拿给林克看，结果他却吓得直往后缩呢……","transcript_en":"Hopper Pond used to be filled with hot-footed frogs... Perhaps the monsters have driven them away? In any case, this is the place I finally managed to catch one. I was incredibly excited, and I tried to show Link, but he kept flinching and backing away from me..."},{"seq":100,"id":"vm_zelda_065","no":"No.065","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":565,"y":-591,"z":22,"gx":-591,"gy":-565,"gz":22,"title_zh":"不灭尊严","title_en":"Unshaken Bravery","place_zh":"海拉鲁驻军地遗迹","place_en":"Hyrule Garrison Ruins","transcript_zh":"海拉鲁驻军地遗迹……和其他军事要地一样，这里也曾遭到大批守护者的袭击。不过，原本驻守于此的大部分士兵当时恐怕已被派往其他地区了。留守的寥寥数人虽然装备不足以对抗如此致命的强敌，却依然英勇奋战到了最后。","transcript_en":"The Hyrule Garrison ruins... As with other fortified locations, many Guardians attacked this place. However, it is likely most of the soldiers normally stationed here had already been deployed to other regions. Those few who remained fought bravely, though they were certainly ill-equipped to deal with such deadly foes."},{"seq":101,"id":"vm_zelda_066","no":"No.066","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":439,"y":-1108,"z":64,"gx":-1108,"gy":-439,"gz":64,"title_zh":"腐朽的千年古树","title_en":"Ancient Tree Stump","place_zh":"腐朽的千年古树","place_en":"Ancient Tree Stump","transcript_zh":"在海拉鲁境内，有不少像这截树桩一样树龄恐怕超过千年的腐朽古树。而关于这一棵，传说曾有一位尊贵的精灵栖息其中。我自己也能从这棵古树身上感受到某种非同寻常的气息。很快就会有考古调查队来这里勘察，真期待听到他们的发现。","transcript_en":"In Hyrule, there are a number of large, decaying trees that are likely over one thousand years old, not unlike this tree stump. There is a legend about this tree in particular that says it was inhabited by a dignitary spirit. I, too, sense something important from this tree. An archaeological survey will soon take place here, so I cannot wait to hear about their findings."},{"seq":102,"id":"vm_zelda_067","no":"No.067","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-97,"y":-253,"z":8,"gx":-253,"gy":97,"gz":8,"title_zh":"忐忑不安","title_en":"Precautions on Top of Precautions","place_zh":"避难壕","place_en":"Emergency Shelter","transcript_zh":"当我把打算前往城堡地下调查瘴气的计划告诉普尔亚时，她表示了……极为强烈的反对。就算有林克陪我同行，也没能动摇她分毫。直到我提议在这里建立一座据点——既能观测瘴气动向，又能通往城堡地下的密道——她才勉为其难地点了头。","transcript_en":"When I told Purah of my plan to venture beneath the castle to investigate the gloom, she expressed... strong opposition. That Link would accompany me did not sway her in the slightest. It was only my suggestion to establish an outpost here—a place to observe the gloom from and to reach the hidden path beneath the castle—that earned her begrudging acceptance."},{"seq":103,"id":"vm_zelda_068","no":"No.068","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-130,"y":-285,"z":19,"gx":-285,"gy":130,"gz":19,"title_zh":"招募！测量员！","title_en":"Surveyors Wanted!","place_zh":"监视堡垒 鸟望台","place_en":"Lookout Landing Skyview Tower","transcript_zh":"这是普尔亚为助力海拉鲁复兴而设计的鸟望台之一。虽然还未彻底完工，但工程推进得如此迅速，全靠松达建筑店的鼎力相助。眼下要是普尔亚也能这么顺利地招募到愿意乘着滑翔伞从高空测绘地形的志愿者就好了……","transcript_en":"This is one of the Skyview Towers that Purah designed to aid in the restoration of Hyrule. Though it is not quite finished, we have Hudson Construction to thank for how quickly it is coming along. Now if only Purah could have similar success finding any volunteers to use the paraglider to survey the land from above..."},{"seq":104,"id":"vm_zelda_069","no":"No.069","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-150,"y":-234,"z":26,"gx":-234,"gy":150,"gz":26,"title_zh":"调查队成立","title_en":"Assembling the Survey Team","place_zh":"研究所","place_en":"Research Lab","transcript_zh":"我们能从历史中学到许多东西。毕竟，若不是当年研究了古代遗物，我们甚至无从得知要为大灾厄做好准备。深知这一点，又亲眼见识了旅途中结识的考古学者们的热忱，我决定组建一支调查队，专门勘察海拉鲁各地的古代遗迹与文献。相信在复兴这片土地的道路上，我们一定能从中获益匪浅。","transcript_en":"There are many things we can learn from history. After all, we would not have known to prepare for the Calamity if we had not studied ancient relics from our past. Knowing this, and having seen the passion of the archaeologists I have met on my travels, I have decided to form a team to survey ancient ruins and texts across Hyrule. I am sure there are many things we can learn from them as we restore the land."},{"seq":105,"id":"vm_zelda_070","no":"No.070","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":40,"y":-270,"z":19,"gx":-270,"gy":-40,"gz":19,"title_zh":"建材放置场","title_en":"Materials Cache","place_zh":"鸟鸣草原","place_en":"Passeri Greenbelt","transcript_zh":"修缮海拉鲁的道路与桥梁刻不容缓。遗憾的是，尽管松达建筑店和驿站协会都在竭尽全力，我们依然人手不足。好在物产还算丰饶，于是我们专门设立了用于复兴建设的建材放置场，供大家自由取用。","transcript_en":"It is critical that we repair Hyrule's roads and bridges. Unfortunately, despite the efforts of Hudson Construction and the Stable Association, we lack the labor to tackle this task. We are blessed with abundant resources, however, so we've established material caches dedicated to the rebuilding efforts and made them freely available."},{"seq":106,"id":"vm_zelda_071","no":"No.071","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":217,"y":-63,"z":23,"gx":-63,"gy":-217,"gz":23,"title_zh":"牛奶色的黄昏","title_en":"Flavor Memories","place_zh":"麦贝镇遗迹","place_en":"Mabe Village Ruins","transcript_zh":"麦贝镇遗迹……那是离城堡最近的农庄，过去我常会微服造访。那里的村民总是热情地端出多到我根本吃不完的食物，我还记得他们把饲养的动物都当成家人一般疼爱。想必大难临头时，这里没有一个人是独自丢下同伴逃跑的吧……","transcript_en":"The ruins of Mabe Village... It was the farm closest to the castle, and I would often visit it incognito. They always shared far more food than I could possibly eat, and I remember that they treated their animals like members of their family. I imagine no one here fled alone when the time came..."},{"seq":107,"id":"vm_zelda_072","no":"No.072","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-801,"y":245,"z":21,"gx":245,"gy":801,"gz":21,"title_zh":"春风吹又生","title_en":"New Sprouts","place_zh":"海拉鲁森林公园遗迹","place_en":"Hyrule Forest Park","transcript_zh":"这座森林公园由王室直辖，历经数代君王悉心照料与营建。虽说部分区域曾毁于战火，但这并不意味着先祖的遗产就此断绝。事实上，我似乎已经看到有嫩芽破土而出了。","transcript_en":"This forest park was the direct responsibility of the royal family, cared for and built upon by each successive generation of rulers. Though it has been partially destroyed by fire, that does not spell the end of our ancestors' legacy. In fact, I believe I caught sight of some new growth emerging already."},{"seq":108,"id":"vm_zelda_073","no":"No.073","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1243,"y":720,"z":33,"gx":720,"gy":1243,"gz":33,"title_zh":"劳鲁村落的纪念碑","title_en":"Rauru Settlement Memorial","place_zh":"劳鲁村落遗迹","place_en":"Rauru Settlement Ruins","transcript_zh":"尽管军事演习场的士兵们奋起反击，这座村落还是被一具失控暴走的守护者付之一炬。松软的泥土几乎没能留下那场英勇激战的痕迹……愿他们无畏的英灵能在女神海利亚的身旁安息。","transcript_en":"Although the soldiers at the training camp fought back, this settlement was burned to the ground by a single rampaging Guardian. The loose ground has left little trace of the heroic battle they waged... I pray their brave spirits have found peace with Goddess Hylia."},{"seq":109,"id":"vm_zelda_074","no":"No.074","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1145,"y":1042,"z":22,"gx":1042,"gy":1145,"gz":22,"title_zh":"驿站的乐团","title_en":"The Stable Trotters","place_zh":"森林驿站","place_en":"Woodland Stable","transcript_zh":"森林驿站令我记忆犹新。我曾在这里见到驿站协会会长的孙子挥舞着指挥棒。看来他正四处网罗乐手，组建了一支乐团。虽然他的举止还有些笨拙，但那副全情投入的模样和满腔热忱，深深吸引着周围的人们。等调查告一段落后，我一定要去听听他们的演奏。","transcript_en":"I'll always remember Woodland Stable. It is where I saw the president of the Stable Association's grandson swinging a baton around. It seems he has formed a band, gathering one musician after another. While his mannerisms are clumsy, others are enthralled by his appearance and enthusiasm. Once I have finished my investigation, I should try to see them perform."},{"seq":110,"id":"vm_zelda_075","no":"No.075","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1382,"y":858,"z":103,"gx":858,"gy":1382,"gz":103,"title_zh":"为士兵们祈福","title_en":"A Prayer for Brave Soldiers","place_zh":"海拉鲁军事演习场遗迹","place_en":"Military Training Camp","transcript_zh":"在大灾厄发生前，这里是一处重要的军事演习场。据说灾厄降临时，身经百战的老兵都已被派往别处，留守此地的只有新兵。尽管缺乏实战经验，这些勇敢的新兵依然齐心协力，击倒了一具守护者。愿他们的在天之灵得以安息……","transcript_en":"This was an important training camp in the days before the Calamity. It is said that when the Calamity occurred, all of the veteran soldiers had been deployed and only trainees remained here. Despite their inexperience, the brave trainees worked together and defeated a Guardian. I pray their souls have found peace..."},{"seq":111,"id":"vm_zelda_076","no":"No.076","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1620,"y":1603,"z":289,"gx":1603,"gy":1620,"gz":289,"title_zh":"新的道路","title_en":"A New Route","place_zh":"鼓大湖","place_en":"Goronbi Lake","transcript_zh":"这一带从前遍布熔岩，常人根本难以靠近；但随着火山喷发平息，如今就连海利亚人不做任何耐火措施也能前来。于是便开辟了这条新路！听说沿途还计划开设新店铺，看来这里很快就要迎来一番崭新的气象了。","transcript_en":"This area used to be covered in lava and was largely unapproachable, but now that the volcanic eruptions have subsided, even Hylians can come here without taking fire-resistance measures. Thus, the new path! I've heard there are even plans for new shops along the road; this place is about to see some significant changes."},{"seq":112,"id":"vm_zelda_077","no":"No.077","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2434,"y":1613,"z":387,"gx":1613,"gy":2434,"gz":387,"title_zh":"食岩饕客","title_en":"Rock Connoisseurs","place_zh":"鼓隆城","place_en":"Goron City","transcript_zh":"动身来鼓隆城之前，我为了应对酷热特意买了不少耐火药。看到现在已经用不上了，真是让人松了口气。不过，鼓隆族爱吃岩石这一点倒是一如既往。眼下看到这幅光景，我不禁想起当年达尔克尔递给林克一块岩石……而林克竟然真的一口吃下去了呢！","transcript_en":"When I was preparing to come here to Goron City, I bought lots of fireproof elixirs to counter the extreme heat. It's a relief to see those are no longer needed. One thing that hasn't changed, though, is the Gorons' love of eating rocks. Seeing it now, I am reminded of when Daruk gave Link a rock to eat... and he did!"},{"seq":113,"id":"vm_zelda_078","no":"No.078","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2394,"y":1709,"z":395,"gx":1709,"gy":2394,"gz":395,"title_zh":"重叠的身影","title_en":"A Familiar Visage","place_zh":"鼓隆城","place_en":"Goron City","transcript_zh":"初次见到阿沅时，我着实吃了一惊。这位年轻的鼓隆族身形与他的先祖如出一辙，我差点就激动得脱口喊出「达尔克尔！」了。当然，他并没有达尔克尔那般豪迈无畏的气魄，但他是个真诚率直、心地无比善良的好孩子。","transcript_en":"I was surprised when I first saw Yunobo. The young Goron is built just like his grandfather, and I nearly shouted \"Daruk!\" in excitement. Of course, he doesn't have the same bold spirit Daruk had, but he is an honest boy with a truly kind heart."},{"seq":114,"id":"vm_zelda_079","no":"No.079","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2469,"y":1662,"z":386,"gx":1662,"gy":2469,"gz":386,"title_zh":"肌肉亭","title_en":"Peak Protein Provisions","place_zh":"鼓隆美食店","place_en":"Goron Gusto Shop","transcript_zh":"这家店专营各类烤肉料理，不过他们似乎打算把这里交给一位手艺精湛的厨师打理，自己则去大路旁另开一家新店。临走前，他们还非常热情地送了我一份烤兽肉作为临别赠礼。","transcript_en":"This restaurant specializes in grilling various foods, though it seems they are planning on leaving this location to a skilled chef and opening a new shop along the road. Since they were moving on, they were kind enough to give me a seared steak as a gift."},{"seq":115,"id":"vm_zelda_080","no":"No.080","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2505,"y":1695,"z":397,"gx":1695,"gy":2505,"gz":397,"title_zh":"私人锻造师","title_en":"Blacksmith on Retainer","place_zh":"鼓隆城","place_en":"Goron City","transcript_zh":"这家铁匠铺似乎并没有挂招牌。我感觉这位铁匠比起起名字，更在意的是锤炼自己的手艺。他确实是位技艺登峰造极的大师，身姿巍峨而不屈。挥锤打铁的手一刻未停，他便自豪地告诉我，达尔克尔的那把碎岩巨剑正是出自他手。","transcript_en":"This blacksmithing shop doesn't seem to have a name. I get the sense that the blacksmith himself is more concerned with his skills than he is about naming things. Truly, he is a master at his craft—his stature both grand and indomitable. Without so much as a momentary pause while striking the iron, he proudly told me that he was the very one who made Daruk's Boulder Breaker."},{"seq":116,"id":"vm_zelda_081","no":"No.081","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2409,"y":1665,"z":458,"gx":1665,"gy":2409,"gz":458,"title_zh":"追念达尔克尔","title_en":"Honoring Daruk","place_zh":"鼓隆桥","place_en":"Stolock Bridge","transcript_zh":"达尔克尔……林克已经把你灵魂得到解放那时的事告诉我了。真抱歉，让你直到最后一刻都还在挂念着我；也无比感谢你，信守了一百年前许下的承诺。我的挚友，我一定会让你感到骄傲的。我定会为这片大地带来和平。请……守护着我吧。","transcript_en":"Oh, Daruk... Link told me of when your spirit was released. I am so sorry that you worried after me all the way to the end, and I cannot thank you enough for keeping the promise you made a hundred years ago. I will make you proud, my friend. I will bring peace to this land. Please...watch over me."},{"seq":117,"id":"vm_zelda_082","no":"No.082","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2326,"y":2169,"z":526,"gx":2169,"gy":2326,"gz":526,"title_zh":"平息的火山","title_en":"A Slumbering Volcano","place_zh":"奥尔汀桥","place_en":"Bridge of Eldin","transcript_zh":"不久之前，死亡之山还频繁而猛烈地喷涌着熔岩。如今，这座火山似乎终于归于沉寂了。唔……我听说古代鼓隆族曾在山腹深处建造过居所。不知道当年的死亡之山，是不是也像现在这样呢？","transcript_en":"It was not long ago that lava was frequently and fiercely erupting from Death Mountain. These days, the mountain seems to have quieted though. Hmm... I've heard stories that ancient Gorons built dwellings far down in the depths of the mountain. I wonder if this is similar to how the mountain looked back then."},{"seq":118,"id":"vm_zelda_083","no":"No.083","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2822,"y":1608,"z":423,"gx":1608,"gy":2822,"gz":423,"title_zh":"改善风气的阿沅","title_en":"Yunobo Is Making the World Better","place_zh":"阿沅队本部","place_en":"YunoboCo HQ","transcript_zh":"死亡之山的骤变让许多鼓隆族人都感到不安，但我听说年轻的阿沅每天都会上山，在裸露的岩壁上开采矿石。他的这份干劲似乎鼓舞了同胞们，让大家走出了迷茫，重新找到了方向……多亏了阿沅，鼓隆城的未来一定会更加光明。","transcript_en":"The sudden changes on Death Mountain left many Gorons feeling uneasy, but I hear young Yunobo goes to the mountain every day to mine ore from the exposed rock face. It seems his efforts are motivating his fellow Gorons, shaking them out of their worry and giving them purpose... Certainly the future of Goron City is brighter thanks to Yunobo."},{"seq":119,"id":"vm_zelda_084","no":"No.084","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2243,"y":1774,"z":477,"gx":1774,"gy":2243,"gz":477,"title_zh":"违反规矩","title_en":"Accidentally Ill-Mannered","place_zh":"鼓隆温泉","place_en":"Goron Hot Springs","transcript_zh":"鼓隆族人们泡在这温泉里显得无比惬意……可对我来说实在太烫了，我只敢泡泡脚。可怜的林克想兑点冷水降降温，还被鼓隆族人数落了一顿——原来这种水温对他们来说，竟然还只是温热而已。","transcript_en":"The Gorons looked so comfortable as they lounged in these hot springs... As for me, the heat was too much, and I only put my feet in. Poor Link even caught a scolding from the Gorons when he tried to add a little water to cool it down; apparently this temperature is merely tepid to them already."},{"seq":120,"id":"vm_zelda_085","no":"No.085","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1132,"y":2597,"z":147,"gx":2597,"gy":1132,"gz":147,"title_zh":"文武双全的教诲","title_en":"Train Mind and Body","place_zh":"山麓驿站","place_en":"Foothill Stable","transcript_zh":"驿站是情报的宝库，也是很容易遇见调查队成员的地方。虽然我们的工作才刚刚起步，但各地的调查报告已经陆续传回来了。随着调查深入，我也得确保大家掌握一定的防身本领才行……毕竟探索未知之地，总是伴随危险的。","transcript_en":"Stables are a treasure trove of information and a great place to find members of the research team. Though we've only just begun our work, we've already received research reports from every region. As we continue working, I should ensure they know how to defend themselves... Exploring the unknown can be dangerous, after all."},{"seq":121,"id":"vm_zelda_086","no":"No.086","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1233,"y":2431,"z":116,"gx":2431,"gy":1233,"gz":116,"title_zh":"封闭的登山口","title_en":"Blocked Trailhead","place_zh":"死亡之山登山口","place_en":"Maw of Death Mountain","transcript_zh":"这里从前是死亡之山的登山口，但山路已经崩塌，怪物也盘踞于此，把绝大多数旅人都吓退了。如果达尔克尔还在的话，一定转眼间就能把这些拦路的怪物清理干净吧——前提是里面没有小狗……","transcript_en":"This was previously the trailhead for Death Mountain, but the path has collapsed, and monsters have descended on the area, scaring off most of the travelers. If Daruk were here, I'm sure he'd clear out any opposition in no time. Assuming there are no dogs among them..."},{"seq":122,"id":"vm_zelda_087","no":"No.087","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1372,"y":3048,"z":285,"gx":3048,"gy":1372,"gz":285,"title_zh":"阿卡莱堡垒的纪念碑","title_en":"Akkala Citadel Memorial","place_zh":"阿卡莱高原","place_en":"Akkala Highlands","transcript_zh":"我们曾以为阿卡莱堡垒固若金汤，可那一战却证明并非如此……我们必须将这场战役的教训铭记于心。为了不辜负在此牺牲的英烈们，我在此起誓——我将竭尽全力复兴海拉鲁，为子民开创一个和平的未来。","transcript_en":"We thought Akkala Citadel impregnable, but the battle here proved it was anything but... We must carry the lessons learned from this battle forward with us. I vow to honor the sacrifices of those who died here—I will work tirelessly to restore Hyrule and to create a peaceful future for its people."},{"seq":123,"id":"vm_zelda_088","no":"No.088","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1679,"y":3131,"z":201,"gx":3131,"gy":1679,"gz":201,"title_zh":"守护者所到之处","title_en":"Path of the Guardians","place_zh":"南阿卡莱驿站","place_en":"South Akkala Stable","transcript_zh":"南阿卡莱驿站……当年大批守护者席卷了这一带，驿站建筑虽毁于一旦，但所有工作人员都得以安全撤离。这无疑要归功于阿卡莱堡垒的士兵们为他们争取了宝贵的时间……如今驿站协会已经重建了这里，几乎看不出当年满目疮痍的痕迹了。","transcript_en":"South Akkala Stable... Many, many Guardians swept through this area, and though the building was destroyed, the workers were all able to get to safety. No doubt that is thanks to the soldiers of Akkala Citadel buying them time... But now the Stable Association has rebuilt the stable, and you can hardly see any traces of the past destruction."},{"seq":124,"id":"vm_zelda_089","no":"No.089","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2286,"y":3044,"z":334,"gx":3044,"gy":2286,"gz":334,"title_zh":"不为人知的夏特","title_en":"The Lost Hamlet","place_zh":"夏特村落遗迹","place_en":"Shadow Hamlet Ruins","transcript_zh":"其实没有人知道大灾厄发生时，夏特村落究竟遭遇了什么。这里原本是一座与世隔绝的村子，村民们也安于这样的生活。就连当年我亲自前来警示大灾厄将至时，都被他们拒之门外。如果那时我能更努力地劝说他们听我一言，这里会不会就不至于沦为废墟了呢……","transcript_en":"No one actually knows what happened here at the Shadow Hamlet during the Calamity. They were a very isolated village, and they liked it that way. They even turned me away when I came to warn them about the Calamity. I wonder if this place would be more than ruins if I had tried harder to get them to listen..."},{"seq":125,"id":"vm_zelda_090","no":"No.090","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2656,"y":3745,"z":3,"gx":3745,"gy":2656,"gz":3,"title_zh":"是正是邪","title_en":"Good and Evil","place_zh":"力量之泉","place_en":"Spring of Power","transcript_zh":"力量之泉虽然尚存，却已荒废破败。我想，大概是许多人将「力量」视作魔王的象征，因而对此地避而远之吧，但这其实是一种误解。力量本身并无善恶之分，决定其正邪的，始终是掌握它的人。","transcript_en":"Though the Spring of Power remains, it has been neglected and fallen into ruin. I imagine many see power as a symbol of the Demon King and thus avoid the spring, but there is a misunderstanding there. Power itself is neither inherently evil nor good; it is the individual wielding that power that defines it."},{"seq":126,"id":"vm_zelda_091","no":"No.091","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2732,"y":4239,"z":125,"gx":4239,"gy":2732,"gz":125,"title_zh":"特产 赈灾包子","title_en":"The Signature Steamed Buns","place_zh":"东阿卡莱驿站","place_en":"East Akkala Stable","transcript_zh":"听说东阿卡莱驿站的起源，是当年驿站协会用修建其他驿站剩下的余料，为家园被烧毁的灾民搭建了一处避难所。当时厨房为大家准备了热腾腾的包子，那份食谱流传至今，便成了这里的招牌特产。","transcript_en":"Apparently, East Akkala Stable got its start when the Stable Association used scrap wood left over from other stables to construct a shelter for people whose homes had burned down. The kitchen prepared steamed buns for the people then, and the recipe has become a signature meal here."},{"seq":127,"id":"vm_zelda_092","no":"No.092","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-3144,"y":4505,"z":245,"gx":4505,"gy":3144,"gz":245,"title_zh":"天才们的执着","title_en":"Particular Geniuses","place_zh":"阿卡莱古代研究所","place_en":"Akkala Ancient Tech Lab","transcript_zh":"阿卡莱古代研究所原本是一座被守护者摧毁的灯塔，后来由普尔亚和洛贝利改建成了研究所。他们口头上说选址于此是因为临近遗迹，但我觉得真正的原因是为了劝退访客。毕竟，他们所从事的研究实在太危险了……","transcript_en":"The Akkala Ancient Tech Lab was originally a lighthouse Guardians destroyed. Apparently, Purah and Robbie later converted it into a lab. They claim its proximity to ruins is why they chose this place, but I think the real reason they settled here was to discourage visitors. Their research was dangerous, after all..."},{"seq":128,"id":"vm_zelda_093","no":"No.093","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1620,"y":4023,"z":127,"gx":4023,"gy":1620,"gz":127,"title_zh":"理想世界","title_en":"An Ideal World","place_zh":"一始村","place_en":"Tarrey Town","transcript_zh":"一始村——一座将海拉鲁各族汇聚一堂的村落。建村的主力是松达，不过听说林克也出了一份力呢。唔……海利亚人、利特族、鼓隆族、卓拉族与格鲁德族在这里和睦共处——这正是我所期盼的未来世界的缩影。","transcript_en":"Tarrey Town, a village that brought all the peoples of Hyrule together. Hudson is the driving force behind its founding, though they say Link played a role as well. Hmm... This place—where Hylians, Rito, Goron, Zora, and Gerudo all live together in peace—is a model of the world I hope to see in the future."},{"seq":129,"id":"vm_zelda_094","no":"No.094","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1593,"y":3941,"z":128,"gx":3941,"gy":1593,"gz":128,"title_zh":"寡言的社长","title_en":"Taciturn President","place_zh":"一始村","place_en":"Tarrey Town","transcript_zh":"松达建筑店……松达为了给复兴工程招募人手四处奔波，似乎很少留在店里。听说他的孩子很快就要出生了，虽然他平日里寡言少语，但我能看得出他内心掩饰不住的喜悦。","transcript_en":"Hudson Construction... It seems Hudson is rarely in the shop, as he is busy recruiting workers for the restoration efforts. I hear he is expecting a child soon, and though he is a reserved man, I can see his quiet excitement."},{"seq":130,"id":"vm_zelda_095","no":"No.095","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1600,"y":3924,"z":128,"gx":3924,"gy":1600,"gz":128,"title_zh":"“达”的老规矩","title_en":"Successor \"Son\"","place_zh":"一始村","place_en":"Tarrey Town","transcript_zh":"听说松达建筑店沿袭了前身樱达建筑店的老规矩——所有员工的名字都必须以「达」字结尾。不过严格来说有一个例外：据说有位名叫哈吉的先生在面试时，自我介绍听起来像是「哈吉达」，结果被松达误以为他的名字里真的带「达」字呢。","transcript_en":"They say Hudson Construction adopted the name policy from its predecessor, Bolson Construction; all employees must have a name that ends in \"son.\" There is technically one exception though. A man named Hagie supposedly introduced himself as \"Hagie, son\" in his interview, which Hudson mistook for \"Hagieson.\""},{"seq":131,"id":"vm_zelda_096","no":"No.096","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1606,"y":3911,"z":129,"gx":3911,"gy":1606,"gz":129,"title_zh":"危险的载具","title_en":"A Less-Than-Safe Ride","place_zh":"一始村","place_en":"Tarrey Town","transcript_zh":"这条轨道是用来往返村子与作业场所的。它的构造并不复杂，只是利用高低落差让绳索和滑轮顺着轨道滑行。不过这是单向的，想回村子的话，就得绕着外围走回去。唔……不知道能不能用希卡族的技术来改良一下呢……","transcript_en":"This track facilitates transit from the village to the work area. It is not a complex creation, relying on the height difference to send the rope and pulley down the rails. However, it is only one way, so a person would have to walk back along the perimeter to reach the village. Hmm... I wonder if Sheikah technology could improve this..."},{"seq":132,"id":"vm_zelda_097","no":"No.097","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1608,"y":3769,"z":89,"gx":3769,"gy":1608,"gz":89,"title_zh":"松达建筑店作业场所","title_en":"Hudson Construction Workshop","place_zh":"松达建筑店 作业场所","place_en":"Hudson Construction Site","transcript_zh":"听说塔林湿地的水位退去、露出坚实的地面后，松达建筑店便决定在这里修建作业场所。如今这里已成为生产海拉鲁复兴所需建材的核心基地。真期待看到它日渐兴旺的模样。","transcript_en":"Apparently, when the water levels in Torin Wetland receded and solid ground emerged, Hudson Construction decided to build a workspace here. That workspace has come to be the main site for producing the building materials used in our restoration efforts. I'm excited to see how this place flourishes."},{"seq":133,"id":"vm_zelda_098","no":"No.098","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1484,"y":3662,"z":89,"gx":3662,"gy":1484,"gz":89,"title_zh":"士兵们的奇策","title_en":"Cunning Tactics","place_zh":"塔林湿地","place_en":"Torin Wetland","transcript_zh":"塔林湿地从前曾散落着无数守护者的残骸，如今却已踪迹全无。想来是泥泞的湿地限制了守护者的机动性，让它们无从躲避彼此的误击。阿卡莱能免遭更大劫难，无疑要归功于堡垒士兵们的机智奇策。若非守护者在这里受阻，阿卡莱地区恐怕会遭受更加惨重的破坏。","transcript_en":"Torin Wetland was once littered with the broken remains of countless Guardians, though there are no longer any traces of them. I imagine the wetlands reduced the Guardians' mobility, making it impossible for them to avoid each other's attacks. No doubt Akkala owes thanks to the quick thinking of soldiers from the citadel for this. If the Guardians hadn't been so hindered, the Akkala region would have suffered more damage."},{"seq":134,"id":"vm_zelda_099","no":"No.099","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":41,"y":3257,"z":234,"gx":3257,"gy":-41,"gz":234,"title_zh":"镌刻的卓拉历史","title_en":"Inscriptions of Zora History","place_zh":"露朵山","place_en":"Ruto Mountain","transcript_zh":"这些石碑由卓拉族所立，从前镌刻着多雷凡大王的箴言，如今则换成了希多的记述。他在碑文中写下了对抗神兽的那场战役，还提到了自己让林克骑在背上并肩作战的事。这足以见得他对林克何等信赖——毕竟，卓拉族可是极少允许旁人骑上自己背部的……","transcript_en":"The Zora created these stone monuments, and while they once were engraved with the words of King Dorephan, they now bear those of Sidon. He has written of the battle against the Divine Beast, when he allowed Link to ride on his back. That really shows how completely he trusts Link; it is rare for a Zora to let anyone on their backs, after all..."},{"seq":135,"id":"vm_zelda_100","no":"No.100","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-276,"y":3530,"z":289,"gx":3530,"gy":276,"gz":289,"title_zh":"友谊之桥","title_en":"Building a Relationship","place_zh":"露朵台地","place_en":"Ruto Precipice","transcript_zh":"为了防范河水泛滥成灾，卓拉族与海拉鲁王国携手修建了这座蓄水湖。其实在这项工程之前，双方也只是维持着和睦的关系；正是共同修建蓄水湖的历程，让卓拉族与海拉鲁王国结下了真正的深厚友谊。","transcript_en":"In order to prevent the damage a flooding river would cause, the Zora people and the Kingdom of Hyrule worked together to build this reservoir. In fact, though they were only amicable toward each other before the project, it was the act of building this that formed a true friendship between the Zora and the Kingdom of Hyrule."},{"seq":136,"id":"vm_zelda_101","no":"No.101","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-262,"y":3207,"z":136,"gx":3207,"gy":262,"gz":136,"title_zh":"大灾厄的亲历者","title_en":"Those Who Remember the Calamity","place_zh":"卓拉大桥","place_en":"Great Zora Bridge","transcript_zh":"卓拉族寿命漫长，因此卓拉领地中至今仍有许多人记得百年前大灾厄发生时的情景，以及米法当时所做的一切。我想，我在这里或许并不受欢迎，但将她最后的经历如实相告，是我义不容辞的责任……","transcript_en":"Thanks to their long lifespans, many Zora here in Zora's Domain still remember the events of the Calamity and Mipha's part in all of it a hundred years ago. I do not think I will be welcomed, but it is my duty to tell them what happened to her in the end..."},{"seq":137,"id":"vm_zelda_102","no":"No.102","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-463,"y":3298,"z":139,"gx":3298,"gy":463,"gz":139,"title_zh":"米法雕像的转移","title_en":"Statue Relocation","place_zh":"卓拉领地广场","place_en":"Zora's Domain Square","transcript_zh":"百年前，人们为了赞颂卓拉英杰米法而建造了这座雕像，如今它已成为缅怀她英勇献身的纪念碑。雕像之所以矗立在那里，似乎多亏了希多的提议——正是他提出，要将雕像迁至一处风景优美的地方。","transcript_en":"A hundred years ago, a statue was made to celebrate Mipha, the Zora Champion. It is now a memorial to her sacrifice. Apparently it is thanks to Sidon that it stands where it does. It was he who proposed it be relocated to a place with a wonderful view."},{"seq":138,"id":"vm_zelda_103","no":"No.103","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-540,"y":3333,"z":164,"gx":3333,"gy":540,"gz":164,"title_zh":"谒见多雷凡大王","title_en":"Audience with King Dorephan","place_zh":"王座厅","place_en":"Throne Room","transcript_zh":"统治卓拉族的多雷凡大王，正是米法的父亲。他以惊人的力量闻名，甚至无需手持武器，仅凭鱼鳍便能战斗。这里的一位卫兵还兴奋地向我讲述过，大王曾一击便将一支怪物大军尽数击溃。","transcript_en":"King Dorephan rules over the Zora and is father to Mipha. He's known for his incredible strength—in fact, he fights with his fins rather than wielding a weapon. One of the guards here even told me excitedly about an army of monsters who were eradicated with a single blow from the king."},{"seq":139,"id":"vm_zelda_104","no":"No.104","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-491,"y":3333,"z":140,"gx":3333,"gy":491,"gz":140,"title_zh":"少女的祈祷","title_en":"A Maiden's Prayer","place_zh":"铁锤商店","place_en":"Hammerhead","transcript_zh":"我听说，在制作卓拉铠甲的过程中，怀着祈愿心爱之人平安的心情至关重要。米法似乎曾常常来到这里，亲手为林克打造铠甲。然而最后，她却将铠甲托付给了多雷凡大王……或许她早已预感到，自己无法亲手将它交到林克手中吧。","transcript_en":"I have heard that an important part of the process of crafting Zora Armor is a prayer for the safety of a loved one. Apparently, Mipha often came to this place to work on armor she made for Link. However, in the end she left the armor with King Dorephan... Perhaps she knew she would not be able to hand it to Link herself."},{"seq":140,"id":"vm_zelda_105","no":"No.105","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-507,"y":3297,"z":140,"gx":3297,"gy":507,"gz":140,"title_zh":"鱼乡旅馆","title_en":"Seabed Inn","place_zh":"水底旅馆","place_en":"Seabed Inn","transcript_zh":"卓拉旅馆的床铺太硬，在旅人之间似乎颇受诟病。店主为此向我请教，说卓拉族平时都在水中入睡，实在分不清怎样的床才算舒适。我便提议，不如做一张让人仿佛漂浮在水中的床。现在想来，这个主意或许太不切实际了……","transcript_en":"The beds in the Zora inn are hard and apparently quite unpopular among travelers. The owner consulted with me about it, saying that since Zora sleep in the water, they aren't sure what makes a bed good or bad. I offered a suggestion of creating a bed that's akin to floating in water. That may have been too unrealistic..."},{"seq":141,"id":"vm_zelda_106","no":"No.106","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-591,"y":3642,"z":197,"gx":3642,"gy":591,"gz":197,"title_zh":"大王净身之所","title_en":"Kings' Purification Ceremony","place_zh":"清流王居","place_en":"Pristine Sanctum","transcript_zh":"清流王居是历代卓拉国王退位时遵循传统仪式的圣地。据说，先王们退位之际都会在此以清澈的泉水洁净身心，并向这座王座献上自己的一片鳞片，以此象征远离尘世。","transcript_en":"The Pristine Sanctum is part of the traditions a retiring Zora king follows upon abdicating their title. It is said that many generations of kings have cleansed their bodies in the pristine waters here, as well as offering one of their scales to this throne. In so doing, they symbolically abandon the earthly world."},{"seq":142,"id":"vm_zelda_107","no":"No.107","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-421,"y":3759,"z":539,"gx":3759,"gy":421,"gz":539,"title_zh":"追念米法","title_en":"Honoring Mipha","place_zh":"尝试海角","place_en":"Shatterback Point","transcript_zh":"米法，从这里眺望领地的景色，你一定也很喜欢吧？我已经把你的遗言转告给多雷凡大王了，他向我道了谢。可真正该说谢谢的人其实是我……我要向你道谢。谢谢你，米法。只恨我们能共度的时光，实在太短暂了……","transcript_en":"I'm sure that you love the view of the village from here, don't you, Mipha? I shared your final words with King Dorephan, you know. He told me \"thank you.\" But I should be the one offering my thanks... and I do. I offer them to you. Thank you, Mipha. I wish only that we had more time together..."},{"seq":143,"id":"vm_zelda_108","no":"No.108","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":307,"y":1571,"z":10,"gx":1571,"gy":-307,"gz":10,"title_zh":"与马儿共存的村子","title_en":"The Horse-Rearing Village","place_zh":"科彭嘉村遗迹","place_en":"Goponga Village Ruins","transcript_zh":"科彭嘉村的人们正尝试着只凭寥寥数人来照料马匹——他们计划利用散布在拉聂尔湿地中的小岛作为天然的马厩。村口有一片草地，马儿们在那里生活得十分自在。这里的村民甚至还称赞我的白马十分美丽呢。","transcript_en":"Here in Goponga Village, they're working to make it possible to manage horses with just a few people. This would be achievable by using the small islands scattered about Lanayru Wetlands as stables. There's a grassy field at the village's entrance where the horses seem to be living at ease. And the villagers here even told me my white horse is beautiful."},{"seq":144,"id":"vm_zelda_109","no":"No.109","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":162,"y":894,"z":25,"gx":894,"gy":-162,"gz":25,"title_zh":"驿站协会","title_en":"The Stable Association","place_zh":"湿地驿站","place_en":"Wetland Stable","transcript_zh":"为了应对大灾厄，父王决定将各地的驿站设为避难所。他曾说：“守护子民的方式，并不只有战斗。”为了进一步加强各驿站间的协作，驿站协会应运而生，湿地驿站的店主梅兹托也被任命为首任会长。","transcript_en":"Father decided that the stables would be places of refuge in preparation for the Calamity. In his words, \"There is more to protecting our people than simply fighting.\" The Stable Association was thus established to further strengthen cooperation, and Mestro, proprietor of Wetland Stable, was appointed as its first chairman."},{"seq":145,"id":"vm_zelda_110","no":"No.110","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":832,"y":853,"z":10,"gx":853,"gy":-832,"gz":10,"title_zh":"笑靥如花","title_en":"Blooming Joy","place_zh":"花之中州","place_en":"Floret Sandbar","transcript_zh":"花之中州与在此精心育花的奥克芭给了我灵感，让我也想打造一处能让海拉鲁各地花卉一同盛放的花园。虽然从驿站借来了工具，但我实在……不太擅长这类农活，弄得浑身都是泥土。不过，我得集中精力才行。宁静公主、潜行草、大剑草……接下来该种什么好呢？","transcript_en":"The Floret Sandbar and Magda, who cultivates flowers here, inspired me to create a place where flowers from all over Hyrule could bloom together. Though I was able to borrow tools from a stable, I am not... adept at this kind of work. The dirt has gotten everywhere. Still, I must focus. Silent princess... Blue nightshade... Mighty thistle... What next?"},{"seq":146,"id":"vm_zelda_111","no":"No.111","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1082,"y":334,"z":9,"gx":334,"gy":-1082,"gz":9,"title_zh":"美食家云集的驿站","title_en":"Gathering of Gourmets","place_zh":"河畔驿站","place_en":"Riverside Stable","transcript_zh":"河畔驿站向来以美食家云集而闻名。来到这里，我不禁想起曾与几位自称“饥饿是最好的调味料”的人共进肉类盖饭的往事。不过当时他们已经整整三天没吃东西，在营地里几乎动弹不得了。希望他们能从中吸取教训吧……","transcript_en":"Riverside Stable is known to many as a gathering place for gourmets. Visiting here reminds me of a time I shared a meal of meat and rice with a few who claimed \"hunger is the best sauce.\" Though at the time, they had not eaten in three days and were nearly immobilized at their campsite. I hope they learned their lesson..."},{"seq":147,"id":"vm_zelda_112","no":"No.112","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":3438,"y":518,"z":47,"gx":518,"gy":-3438,"gz":47,"title_zh":"马术传道师","title_en":"Sharing the Joy of the Equestrian Arts","place_zh":"高原驿站","place_en":"Highland Stable","transcript_zh":"啊，是高原驿站。大灾厄之前，骑射曾在这里盛极一时，但如今人们的兴致似乎减退了不少。取而代之的，这里正大力向旅人们传授如何驾驭马车，以及更重要的——如何悉心照料拉车的马儿。","transcript_en":"Ah, Highland Stable. Horseback archery was very popular before the Calamity, though it appears interest has waned in modern times. Instead, there is considerable effort being made to teach travelers how to handle horse-drawn wagons, and more importantly, how to care for the horses that pull them."},{"seq":148,"id":"vm_zelda_113","no":"No.113","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2384,"y":879,"z":18,"gx":879,"gy":-2384,"gz":18,"title_zh":"向龙展示勇气","title_en":"Courage Proven","place_zh":"勇气之泉","place_en":"Spring of Courage","transcript_zh":"很久以前，我因为害怕而不敢踏入勇气之泉……不仅是在孩提时代——那时至少还能怪罪于石像上那句令人畏惧的碑文：“缺乏勇气之人将被龙吞噬”。但即便长大成人后，我也总是担心自己不够勇敢。不过今天，我想我已经能够毫无畏惧地调查这里的每一个角落了。","transcript_en":"Long ago, I was too scared to enter the Spring of Courage... Not even just as a child, though then I could at least blame the intimidating message on the stone statue: \"Those who lack courage will be eaten by a dragon.\" But even as an adult, I always worried that I wasn't brave enough. Today, I think I can investigate every corner of this place without fear."},{"seq":149,"id":"vm_zelda_114","no":"No.114","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":3520,"y":1550,"z":60,"gx":1550,"gy":-3520,"gz":60,"title_zh":"咚构","title_en":"Dondons","place_zh":"湖畔驿站","place_en":"Lakeside Stable","transcript_zh":"湖畔驿站是离我初次发现“咚构”的地点最近的驿站。我在密林深处遇见了这种由我命名的生物，当下便决心要竭尽所能保护它们。我想它们是利用背部那宛如岩石般的突起隐藏身形的，但目前我所了解的也仅此而已。看来，我还需要再多花些时间观察它们……","transcript_en":"Lakeside Stable is the closest stable to where I first discovered the creatures I have named Dondons. I found them deep in the jungle, and I knew I had to do what I could to protect them. I believe they use the rock-like bumps on their backs as a way to conceal themselves, but that is all I have learned so far. I think I will spend some more time observing them..."},{"seq":150,"id":"vm_zelda_115","no":"No.115","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":3543,"y":2585,"z":184,"gx":2585,"gy":-3543,"gz":184,"title_zh":"如愿以偿","title_en":"A Wish Realized","place_zh":"恋人池","place_en":"Lover's Pond","transcript_zh":"我曾听说过一处名为“恋人池”的心形池塘。我几乎可以肯定，从前这里并没有这座池塘，不过……这片地方过去被称为“祈愿山”，听说曾有许多人慕名而来。莫非是大家的心愿汇聚在一起，化作了这方池塘？或许有人会觉得这种想法很可笑，但……我很喜欢这个念头。","transcript_en":"I have heard stories about a heart-shaped pond, known as the Lover's Pond. I am almost certain it wasn't here before, although... This place was once thought of as the \"wish-making mountain,\" and I hear many people would visit. Perhaps all their wishes manifested as the pond? Some may laugh at this idea, but... I think I like it."},{"seq":151,"id":"vm_zelda_116","no":"No.116","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":3602,"y":2561,"z":238,"gx":2561,"gy":-3602,"gz":238,"title_zh":"祈愿山","title_en":"Mountain of Prayers","place_zh":"卡尔山","place_en":"Tuft Mountain","transcript_zh":"卡尔山是许多登山者向往的地方，也被称作“结缘之山”。按照习俗，登山时必须全程保持沉默，抵达山顶后再迎着落日祈祷。我也曾打算亲自攀登，却被林克以山势过于陡峭为由拦了下来。在我看来，他实在有些太过谨慎了。","transcript_en":"Tuft Mountain is a destination for many mountaineers. It's also known as the matchmaking mountain. The custom is to climb in total silence, and upon reaching the top, pray as the sun dips below the horizon. I set out to climb the mountain myself, but I was stopped by Link who observed how very steep it is. Personally, I feel he was being overly cautious."},{"seq":152,"id":"vm_zelda_117","no":"No.117","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":3381,"y":2829,"z":2,"gx":2829,"gy":-3381,"gz":2,"title_zh":"款待","title_en":"Hospitality","place_zh":"沃托里村","place_en":"Lurelin Village","transcript_zh":"沃托里村的海湾里停泊着许多船只，显得格外热闹。甚至在大家还没认出我的身份之前，就对我热情款待。村民们用一种色彩鲜艳的美味鱼儿招待了我，那是在城堡附近绝难见到的鱼。这里的每个人都如此开朗善良……与他们相处的时光，让我得以暂时忘却眼前的重重艰辛。","transcript_en":"The cove here in Lurelin Village is so lively with its many boats. Even before anyone recognized who I was, I was treated with hospitality and warmth. The villagers served me a dish with an exquisite, vibrantly colored fish. You cannot find such a fish anywhere around the castle. Everyone here is so cheerful and kind... Spending time among them, I was able to forget the current hardships, even if momentarily."},{"seq":153,"id":"vm_zelda_118","no":"No.118","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":3415,"y":2893,"z":6,"gx":2893,"gy":-3415,"gz":6,"title_zh":"228道料理","title_en":"Two Hundred and Twenty-Eight Recipes","place_zh":"拉聂尔湾","place_en":"Azure Bay","transcript_zh":"这里有一位厨艺精湛的女士，她款待我的料理美味得令人惊叹。听说她在结婚定居之前，曾游历海拉鲁各地，收集了多达228道食谱。我建议她不妨开一家餐厅，她听后虽只是笑着摆摆手，但我能看出，对于这份赞美，她内心还是颇为自豪的。","transcript_en":"I was amazed at the delicious food I was treated to by the fantastic cook here. It seems she traveled far and wide in Hyrule, gathering an incredible 228 recipes, before getting married and settling down. I suggested she open a restaurant, and while she seemed to laugh at the idea, I saw a quiet pride at the compliment."},{"seq":154,"id":"vm_zelda_119","no":"No.119","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":3425,"y":2924,"z":2,"gx":2924,"gy":-3425,"gz":2,"title_zh":"船形的房子","title_en":"Ship-Shaped Shelter","place_zh":"海滨度假村","place_en":"Fishing Resort","transcript_zh":"他们似乎将一艘废弃的船体改造成了房屋，甚至还用棕榈树来固定船身！这里如今不仅成了当地的标志性建筑，还成了招待客人的住所。考虑到它如此宽敞，拿来当作旅馆确实再合适不过了。","transcript_en":"It seems they turned an abandoned ship hull into a house, even using palm trees to hold the ship in place! It has become something of a local landmark, as well as a place for guests to stay. Considering its size, it really does make sense they would use it as an inn."},{"seq":155,"id":"vm_zelda_120","no":"No.120","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":3443,"y":2920,"z":0,"gx":2920,"gy":-3443,"gz":0,"title_zh":"大海的守护神","title_en":"Guardian of the Ocean","place_zh":"沃托里村","place_en":"Lurelin Village","transcript_zh":"沃托里村的女神像如今被人们尊奉为大海的守护神。我记得它从前曾是渔业的守护神，但随着村里渔民的减少，女神像所承载的寄托也随村子一同发生了变化。嗯……并非所有人都能坦然适应时代与生活的变迁，这座村子的人们，有许多值得我们学习的地方。","transcript_en":"The goddess statue in Lurelin Village is now worshipped as the guardian of the ocean. I believe it used to be thought of as the guardian of fishing, but it seems that, as the number of fishers shrank here, the role of the goddess statue has changed along with the village itself. Hmm... Not everyone can adapt to the changes that life brings. There is much we can learn from the people of this village."},{"seq":156,"id":"vm_zelda_121","no":"No.121","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":3638,"y":3794,"z":0,"gx":3794,"gy":-3638,"gz":0,"title_zh":"魔王的钩爪","title_en":"Demon King's Claw","place_zh":"伊萨奇海角","place_en":"Soka Point","transcript_zh":"伊萨奇海角常被人们称作“魔王的钩爪”，却似乎无人知晓这个名字的由来。邪灵聚集之地，偶尔会出现奇特的地形变化。我不禁在想，这里是否正是那样的一处所在……","transcript_en":"Cape Cresia is commonly referred to as \"Demon King's Claw,\" but nobody seems to know the origin of that name. Areas where evil spirits gather occasionally experience unique topographical shifts. I find myself wondering if this is such a place..."},{"seq":157,"id":"vm_zelda_122","no":"No.122","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":3656,"y":2964,"z":0,"gx":2964,"gy":-3656,"gz":0,"title_zh":"随浪而逝的天方夜谭","title_en":"A Wild Idea Lost to the Sea","place_zh":"科尔奈海滩","place_en":"Korne Beach","transcript_zh":"当沃托里村的村长向我请教如何提升村子的知名度时，我立刻就想到了这里。科尔奈海滩有着绵长的沙滩，海里也没有珊瑚礁……我曾想，或许可以依托这片大海建一处水上乐园，但转念一想，这个点子实在太天方夜谭了，我终究还是没好意思说出口。","transcript_en":"When the head of Lurelin Village asked me how he might raise awareness about his village, I immediately thought of this place. Korne Beach has such long stretches of sand, and it's free of coral reefs... I thought perhaps some sort of playground that incorporates the ocean would be a wonderful addition, but no, it really is an outlandish idea. I couldn't even bring myself to suggest it."},{"seq":158,"id":"vm_zelda_123","no":"No.123","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":3445,"y":4504,"z":0,"gx":4504,"gy":-3445,"gz":0,"title_zh":"尽头的岛屿","title_en":"Eventide Island","place_zh":"托隆波海滩","place_en":"Toronbo Beach","transcript_zh":"百年前的塞哈特诺岛怪物横行，根本无法安全靠近。这次林克随行护卫，可刚一登岛，他却突然捂住了眼睛。好在岛上的怪物似乎都已随大灾厄一同消散……不管怎么说，当我问他为何那样做时，他说自己上次来这里时，一上岸就被剥去了……咳咳……随身携带的所有物品。这种事……他在我踏上沙滩之前，好歹也该先提醒我一声才对吧……","transcript_en":"A hundred years ago, Eventide Island was filled with monsters and impossible to safely approach. Link came along to protect me, but he suddenly covered his eyes the moment we landed. Fortunately, it seems all the monsters vanished with the Calamity... Regardless, when I asked him what he was doing, he said the last time he was here, he had been stripped of...ahem...all his possessions when he arrived. He...could have mentioned that possibility before I set foot on the shore..."},{"seq":159,"id":"vm_zelda_124","no":"No.124","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1874,"y":764,"z":14,"gx":764,"gy":-1874,"gz":14,"title_zh":"双子山的纪念碑","title_en":"Dueling Peaks Memorial","place_zh":"西哈特尔","place_en":"West Necluda","transcript_zh":"曾有许多人从海拉鲁城下町撤离，但能够一路逃到这里的却不足半数……即便如此，当人们看到守护者出现在双子山前时，仍以为一切都结束了。幸亏有这些英勇的战士挺身而出守护了他们。愿他们的英灵最终得以安息。","transcript_en":"Many people evacuated from the town around Hyrule Castle, but less than half of them made it from there to this point... And even then, as they saw the Guardians appear before the Dueling Peaks, they thought they were done for. Thankfully, these brave souls were here to protect them. I pray they found peace at last."},{"seq":160,"id":"vm_zelda_125","no":"No.125","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1938,"y":1325,"z":12,"gx":1325,"gy":-1938,"gz":12,"title_zh":"救赎的双子","title_en":"Twin Saviors","place_zh":"双子山","place_en":"Dueling Peaks","transcript_zh":"双子山……一想到当初若不是林克带领大家逃到这里会是怎样的后果，我至今仍心有余悸。险峻的地势为我们提供了掩护，也带来了许多躲避守护者的藏身之处。包括我在内，许多人的性命才得以保全。那时的我，总是受人保护啊……","transcript_en":"The Dueling Peaks... I shudder to think of what would have happened if Link hadn't lead everyone here. The steep terrain gave us some protection and plenty of places to hide from the Guardians. Many lives were saved, including my own. I was always being protected back then..."},{"seq":161,"id":"vm_zelda_126","no":"No.126","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1945,"y":2033,"z":18,"gx":2033,"gy":-1945,"gz":18,"title_zh":"悼亡之剑","title_en":"Grave Markers","place_zh":"克罗切利平原","place_en":"Blatchery Plain","transcript_zh":"克罗切利平原……守护者曾在这里肆虐，无数士兵献出了生命。如今，遍布原野的剑成为了他们的墓碑。一路走来，我经过了不知多少柄这样的剑……铭记他们与他们的牺牲，是我们永远不可推卸的责任。","transcript_en":"The Blatchery Plain... Many soldiers lost their lives here when Guardians rampaged through the area. Now numerous swords throughout the field mark their graves. I passed by so many as I made my way here... It is our duty to never forget them nor the sacrifice they made."},{"seq":162,"id":"vm_zelda_127","no":"No.127","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1835,"y":2318,"z":11,"gx":2318,"gy":-1835,"gz":11,"title_zh":"哈特诺堡垒的纪念碑","title_en":"Fort Hateno Memorial","place_zh":"哈特诺堡垒","place_en":"Fort Hateno","transcript_zh":"虽然有人认为哈特诺堡垒曾降临过奇迹，但真相并非神明所为。我们之所以能够获救，全赖包括林克在内的士兵们在这里奋不顾身地战斗。倘若我的力量能早一步觉醒，他们本不必如此牺牲……无论如何，我祈愿他们的灵魂能得到女神海利亚的抚慰。","transcript_en":"Though some believe a miracle occurred here at Fort Hateno, the truth is less divine. We were all saved thanks to the soldiers, including Link, who chose to risk their lives here. Though they would not have had to do so if my power had awakened sooner. Regardless, I pray their spirits were comforted by Goddess Hylia."},{"seq":163,"id":"vm_zelda_128","no":"No.128","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1919,"y":1741,"z":10,"gx":1741,"gy":-1919,"gz":10,"title_zh":"伫立在激战地带的驿站","title_en":"The Stable on a Battlefield","place_zh":"双子驿站","place_en":"Dueling Peaks Stable","transcript_zh":"双子驿站是新建成的驿站之一。考虑到这一带曾在大灾厄中遭受重创，一度被守护者彻底占领，从前这里没有修建驿站，反倒算是不幸中的万幸吧……","transcript_en":"Dueling Peaks Stable is one of the newly established stables. Considering this whole area was devastated by the Calamity and completely overrun by Guardians, it's a good thing there was not a stable here before..."},{"seq":164,"id":"vm_zelda_129","no":"No.129","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1025,"y":1940,"z":130,"gx":1940,"gy":-1025,"gz":130,"title_zh":"隐秘 希卡族","title_en":"Hidden Sheikah Tribe","place_zh":"卡卡利科村","place_en":"Kakariko Village","transcript_zh":"啊，是卡卡利科村……居住在这里的希卡族性情温和，但这绝不意味着他们不愿或无力自卫。这座村子能在大灾厄中免遭最惨重的浩劫，或许正是因为所有企图进犯的怪物，都被村民们亲自干脆利落地解决了呢。","transcript_en":"Ah, Kakariko Village... The Sheikah that live here are quite peaceful, but that does not mean they are unwilling or unable to defend themselves. I would not be surprised if this village avoided the worst of the Calamity because any monsters that threatened it were summarily dealt with by the villagers themselves."},{"seq":165,"id":"vm_zelda_130","no":"No.130","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":984,"y":1784,"z":123,"gx":1784,"gy":-984,"gz":123,"title_zh":"百年友谊","title_en":"Hundred-Year-Old Friendship","place_zh":"族长宅邸","place_en":"Chief's Hall","transcript_zh":"我来此探望一位百年未见的挚友。她曾是王室的参谋，在大灾厄之后成为了这座村子的族长，一直静候着我的归来。见到我时，她脸上那如释重负的神情……我们促膝长谈了许久许久，仿佛想要弥补那逝去的漫长岁月。","transcript_en":"I came here to visit a friend that I had not seen in a hundred years. She had been an advisor to the royal family, and following the Calamity, she became the leader of this village while awaiting my return. The relief on her face when she saw me... We talked for hours and hours, trying to make up for all the time we'd lost."},{"seq":166,"id":"vm_zelda_131","no":"No.131","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1010,"y":1790,"z":115,"gx":1790,"gy":-1010,"gz":115,"title_zh":"三色鲤鱼","title_en":"Sanke Carp","place_zh":"卡卡利科村","place_en":"Kakariko Village","transcript_zh":"瀑布下的池水中，游弋着花纹独特的美丽鱼儿……那一定就是百年前希卡族的研究者们在此孜孜不倦培育的观赏鱼吧。他们的研究无疑因大灾厄而受阻，但希卡族最终还是想方设法完成了这项心血之作，这倒一点也不令我意外。","transcript_en":"There are beautiful fish with a unique patterning living in the waters beneath the falls... They must be the ornamental fish Sheikah researchers worked tirelessly to breed here a hundred years ago. Their efforts were certainly hindered by the Calamity, but it doesn't surprise me that the Sheikah would still find a way to finish their work."},{"seq":167,"id":"vm_zelda_132","no":"No.132","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1000,"y":1856,"z":115,"gx":1856,"gy":-1000,"gz":115,"title_zh":"青蛙地藏","title_en":"Frog Guardian","place_zh":"卡卡利科村","place_en":"Kakariko Village","transcript_zh":"这座青蛙石像是旅人的守护神，不过似乎没人知道为何偏偏是青蛙的造型……像希卡族这样科技高度发达的部族，竟依然笃信着此类祈福的象征，实在令人耐人寻味。或许，这与当年希卡族因对王室的立场分歧而分裂一事有所关联……寄托着有朝一日重归于好的期盼吧？","transcript_en":"This frog statue is the guardian of travelers, though I don't believe anyone knows why it's a frog, specifically... It is fascinating that a group as technologically advanced as the Sheikah would still believe in such symbols of good fortune. Maybe it somehow relates to when the Sheikah splintered after a disagreement regarding the royal family... A symbol of hope to one day reunite, perhaps?"},{"seq":168,"id":"vm_zelda_133","no":"No.133","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1017,"y":1873,"z":117,"gx":1873,"gy":-1017,"gz":117,"title_zh":"美洛的梅花园","title_en":"Mellie's Plum Garden","place_zh":"梅莉的梅花园","place_en":"Mellie's Plum Garden","transcript_zh":"这是一座种植梅树的梅花园。百年前，英帕为了庆祝一个孩子的诞生，在这里亲手种下了一棵梅树。百年过去，它已出落得如此繁茂动人，可见梅莉平日里照料得何等用心。这么说来，难道她就是……","transcript_en":"A garden for growing plums. A hundred years ago, Impa planted a plum tree here to celebrate a child's birth. It really has grown into something beautiful since that time; the care Mellie has put into maintaining this place is clear to see. Now that I think of it, could she be..."},{"seq":169,"id":"vm_zelda_134","no":"No.134","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":955,"y":1868,"z":123,"gx":1868,"gy":-955,"gz":123,"title_zh":"珂珂娜的花环","title_en":"Koko's Garland","place_zh":"卡卡利科村","place_en":"Kakariko Village","transcript_zh":"这里是珂珂娜居住的家……她为我采了满满一捧鲜花，于是我们便决定一起编织花环。她还说，以后也要教妹妹普莉珂编呢。看着她那样认真专注的模样，我不由得想起从前母后教我编织花环时的情景。只不过……我起初觉得太难，似乎还急得哭鼻子了呢……","transcript_en":"The house where Koko lives... She picked such an abundance of flowers for me that we decided to make garlands with them. She said she would teach her little sister, Cottla, how to make them as well. Seeing her work so hard stirred memories of when Mother taught me how to weave garlands together. Though...I found it very difficult at first and may have even cried in frustration..."},{"seq":170,"id":"vm_zelda_135","no":"No.135","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":891,"y":1927,"z":165,"gx":1927,"gy":-891,"gz":165,"title_zh":"可秋拉的内心纠葛","title_en":"Cotera's Considerations","place_zh":"东部高台的深穴","place_en":"East Hill Chasm","transcript_zh":"大妖精可秋拉似乎已经不在这里了。我听说，真正适合供奉给她的其实只有卢比；村民们以为供奉蔬菜也能替代，结果可秋拉很快就衰弱了下去。但她顾及村民们的心意，终究什么也没有说出口……","transcript_en":"It seems the Great Fairy Cotera no longer lives here. I have heard that the only truly appropriate offering to her was rupees, and after the villagers started offering vegetables, thinking that would suffice, Cotera quickly grew weak. She was too considerate of the villagers' feelings to say anything though..."},{"seq":171,"id":"vm_zelda_136","no":"No.136","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1340,"y":3936,"z":467,"gx":3936,"gy":-1340,"gz":467,"title_zh":"智慧之泉","title_en":"Spring of Wisdom","place_zh":"智慧之泉","place_en":"Spring of Wisdom","transcript_zh":"这里是供奉智慧女神聂耳的泉水。“未满十七岁者智慧尚浅，禁止入山。”嗯……今天我只能远远仰望，但明天，我就要登上拉聂尔山了。万一我的封印之力还是没能觉醒……不……一定会觉醒的。一定没问题的。","transcript_en":"This is the spring where Nayru, Goddess of Wisdom, is worshipped. \"Those younger than 17 lack wisdom and are forbidden from entering the mountain.\" Hm. Today, all I can do is look up at it, but tomorrow, I climb Mount Lanayru. If my sealing power doesn't awaken... No...it will. I'm certain it will be fine."},{"seq":172,"id":"vm_zelda_137","no":"No.137","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2142,"y":3281,"z":102,"gx":3281,"gy":-2142,"gz":102,"title_zh":"家一般的港湾","title_en":"Feeling Truly at Home","place_zh":"哈特诺村","place_en":"Hateno Village","transcript_zh":"每次来到哈特诺村，我总有种回到家一般的安心感。耕耘过的泥土与刚修剪完的青草芬芳、从拉聂尔山吹拂而下的清爽微风，还有村里孩子们嬉戏的欢笑声……看到这里的生活正一步步恢复往日的宁静，我由衷地感到欣慰。","transcript_en":"I always feel at home when I am in Hateno Village. The smells of well-tended soil and freshly cut grass... The refreshing breeze coming off Mount Lanayru washing over me... The sound of children at play in the village... I am so glad to see life slowly returning to normal here."},{"seq":173,"id":"vm_zelda_138","no":"No.138","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2130,"y":3356,"z":121,"gx":3356,"gy":-2130,"gz":121,"title_zh":"传闻中的时尚追求者","title_en":"The Rumored Fashionista","place_zh":"东风服饰店","place_en":"Ventest Clothing Boutique","transcript_zh":"人们有了余裕去讲究并享受时尚，这正是海拉鲁的生活重归正轨的明证。这股时尚热潮，想来很大程度上要归功于萨格诺的执着与灵感。听说，她设计蘑菇图案的灵感，正是在造访阿卡莱地区的一始村时萌生的。","transcript_en":"That people have time to consider and enjoy fashion is a sure sign that life is returning to normal in Hyrule. I'm sure much of the credit for the interest in fashion is thanks to Cece's determination and inspiration. I hear the idea for the mushroom pattern came to her when she visited Tarrey Town in Akkala."},{"seq":174,"id":"vm_zelda_139","no":"No.139","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2141,"y":3401,"z":121,"gx":3401,"gy":-2141,"gz":121,"title_zh":"巧匠的灵感","title_en":"Splash of Inspiration","place_zh":"染坊","place_en":"Kochi Dye Shop","transcript_zh":"哈特诺村的这家染坊专营染色生意。店主塞吉竟把自己的头伸进了染色机里，把自己那头标志性的红发染成了黑色。听说，这是因为他从儿子塞法罗的画作中获得了灵感，正在潜心钻研什么新点子。说实话，我也很好奇他究竟在琢磨些什么呢。","transcript_en":"Kochi Dye Shop, here in Hateno Village, specializes in dyes. The owner, Sayge, stuck his own head into his dyeing machine and turned his trademark red hair black. Apparently, it happened while he was working on an idea he got from some drawings his son, Sefaro, made. I must admit I am intrigued with what he's up to."},{"seq":175,"id":"vm_zelda_140","no":"No.140","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1989,"y":3367,"z":128,"gx":3367,"gy":-1989,"gz":128,"title_zh":"希望之光","title_en":"Beacon of Hope","place_zh":"哈特诺学校","place_en":"Hateno School","transcript_zh":"随着复兴事业的推进，我衷心祈愿哈特诺学校能成为孩子们探索未来无限可能的地方——愿它化作希望之光，照耀世世代代。","transcript_en":"I pray that, as the restoration work continues, Hateno School will become a place where children can find many paths toward their futures—that it will shine as a beacon of hope for generations to come."},{"seq":176,"id":"vm_zelda_141","no":"No.141","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2090,"y":3620,"z":177,"gx":3620,"gy":-2090,"gz":177,"title_zh":"难以忘怀的味道","title_en":"Unforgettable Flavor","place_zh":"哈特诺牧场","place_en":"Hateno Pasture","transcript_zh":"哈特诺牧场的创始人请我品尝了一种用鲜奶加工而成的食物。它细腻的口感与柔和的奶香实在令人回味无穷，我不知不觉就吃了好多。我向他讨要了食谱，可惜上面的字迹太过潦草，我竟一个字也辨认不出来……","transcript_en":"The founder of Hateno Pasture let me try a sample of food that was processed using milk. The subtle texture and mild flavor were so enjoyable that I couldn't stop myself from eating quite a bit of it. I asked to see the recipe, but unfortunately the handwriting was scrawled in such a way that I couldn't make out a single word..."},{"seq":177,"id":"vm_zelda_142","no":"No.142","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2111,"y":3779,"z":250,"gx":3779,"gy":-2111,"gz":250,"title_zh":"往日如烟……","title_en":"In a Puff of Smoke...","place_zh":"哈特诺古代研究所","place_en":"Hateno Ancient Tech Lab","transcript_zh":"听说大灾厄被击退后，哈特诺古代研究所里的古代遗物全都化作尘埃消失了。如今留存下来的只有仿制品，正因真品已不复存在，这些仿制品才显得愈发珍贵。它们定能帮助我们将海拉鲁的历史流传给后世。","transcript_en":"It seems that when the Calamity was defeated, all of the ancient relics here at the Hateno Ancient Tech Lab turned to dust and disappeared. All that remains are replicas of the originals, and with those gone, these are even more valuable. They will doubtlessly help tell future generations of the history of Hyrule."},{"seq":178,"id":"vm_zelda_143","no":"No.143","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2127,"y":3784,"z":272,"gx":3784,"gy":-2127,"gz":272,"title_zh":"抗衰老的秘密","title_en":"Anti-Aging Secrets","place_zh":"普尔亚的房间","place_en":"Purah's Room","transcript_zh":"普尔亚在房间的黑板上详细写下了她返老还童的方法。我至今还是难以相信，她的灵感居然来自羊脂……不过，她似乎很快就对孩童般的模样感到厌倦了。真有意思，即便百年流转，普尔亚先是变老、又变年轻、再长大了几岁，但有一点她始终未变：对事物总是热衷得飞快，腻得也同样飞快。","transcript_en":"Purah has used the blackboard in her room to write out the details of how she reversed her physical age. I still can't believe she got the idea from sheep's fat... Regardless, it seems she quickly got bored of her childhood form... It is amusing that, despite a hundred years passing and Purah growing old, then young, then a little older, she hasn't changed in at least one way: she will become obsessive about something yet grow tired of it quickly."},{"seq":179,"id":"vm_zelda_144","no":"No.144","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2448,"y":3912,"z":3,"gx":3912,"gy":-2448,"gz":3,"title_zh":"哈特诺海滩","title_en":"Hateno Beach","place_zh":"哈特诺海滩","place_en":"Hateno Beach","transcript_zh":"从这里望去的风景，一如既往地未曾改变。在我所知的地方里，能始终如一的已是屈指可数。为此感到安心的我，是不是有些软弱呢？","transcript_en":"The view from here is, as ever, unchanging. This place is one of the few I know that remains constant. Am I weak for feeling relief at that?"},{"seq":180,"id":"vm_zelda_145","no":"No.145","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2199,"y":3294,"z":112,"gx":3294,"gy":-2199,"gz":112,"title_zh":"天罚","title_en":"Divine Punishment","place_zh":"塔尔荷池塘","place_en":"Firly Pond","transcript_zh":"一尊长着奇特犄角的石像……它突然向我搭话，自称是交易生命与力量的存在，紧接着我便感到一阵强烈的眩晕，仿佛生命力正在被抽离。然而就在下一瞬，一道雷电骤然劈中石像，将它击落水中……那种感觉……我想这尊石像绝非善类，还是让它继续沉在水底为好。","transcript_en":"A strange horned statue... It suddenly spoke to me, calling itself a dealer in life and power, and I felt an overwhelming sensation, like my life was being drained away. But just as suddenly, a bolt of lightning struck the statue, toppling it into the water... That feeling... I do not think the statue had good intentions. It is best left submerged."},{"seq":181,"id":"vm_zelda_146","no":"No.146","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2301,"y":3302,"z":112,"gx":3302,"gy":-2301,"gz":112,"title_zh":"秘密基地","title_en":"Secret Hideout","place_zh":"塞尔达的家的井","place_en":"Zelda's Secret Well","transcript_zh":"在挖掘水井时，我偶然发现了一间隐秘的房间。它从前或许与主屋相连，只是随着岁月流逝渐渐被人遗忘了……不过，只要把破损的地方稍加修葺，应该还能重新派上用场。嗯……那个宝箱里从前一定珍藏过什么贵重之物吧。那我该在里面放些什么好呢？","transcript_en":"While we were digging a well, I came upon a hidden room. It may have been connected to the main building at one time, but it seems it was forgotten as years passed... Still, it could be used again—with a little work on the more decayed areas. Hmm. I imagine something precious was once stored in that treasure chest... What could I put there?"},{"seq":182,"id":"vm_zelda_147","no":"No.147","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2288,"y":3317,"z":130,"gx":3317,"gy":-2288,"gz":130,"title_zh":"塞尔达的家","title_en":"Zelda's Home","place_zh":"塞尔达公主的家","place_en":"Princess Zelda's House","transcript_zh":"这个房间总觉得有些冷清，于是我决定挂上旅途中邂逅的人们与风景的画作来装点它。还有……我最珍视的伙伴们的回忆……","transcript_en":"This room feels a little lonely, so I've decided to decorate it with pictures of the people and places I encountered on my travels. And also...with the memories of my dearest friends..."},{"seq":183,"id":"vm_zelda_148","no":"No.148","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1897,"y":880,"z":175,"gx":880,"gy":1897,"gz":175,"title_zh":"德库树森林","title_en":"Forest of the Deku Tree","place_zh":"迷途森林","place_en":"Lost Woods","transcript_zh":"穿过迷途森林，便能抵达德库树长老所在的森林。我第一次来到这里时，吓得几乎迈不开步子，但母后轻声安抚了我——在我眼中扭曲骇人的古木，在她看来却是一张张生动有趣的面孔。正是从那时起，我才真正懂得了换个角度看世界的可贵。","transcript_en":"Once you pass through the Lost Woods, you'll arrive at the forest where the Great Deku Tree lives. When I first visited here, I could hardly move from fright, but Mother soothed my fears by pointing out that where I saw scary, twisted trees, she saw interesting, expressive faces. That is when I truly learned the value of appreciating different perspectives."},{"seq":184,"id":"vm_zelda_149","no":"No.149","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2144,"y":430,"z":162,"gx":430,"gy":2144,"gz":162,"title_zh":"剑的守护者","title_en":"A Sword's Protector","place_zh":"克洛格森林","place_en":"Korok Forest","transcript_zh":"德库树长老一直守护着驱魔之剑。从某种意义上说，我也视他为人生的导师。当初，那位骑士被选为驱魔之剑的持有者时，我的心绪几乎陷入崩溃。就在那一刻，德库树长老赠予我充满智慧的话语，鼓励我不要放弃，每个人都有属于自己的道路。那些话语，至今仍在抚慰着我。","transcript_en":"The Great Deku Tree watches over the sword that seals the darkness. I also view this tree as a mentor, in a sense. When the knight was chosen to wield the darkness-sealing sword, I felt nearly overcome by my feelings. But the Great Deku Tree offered me words of wisdom in that moment, encouraging me not to give up and that I had my own path to follow. Those words provide comfort to me still."},{"seq":185,"id":"vm_zelda_150","no":"No.150","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2112,"y":432,"z":144,"gx":432,"gy":2112,"gz":144,"title_zh":"大师之剑","title_en":"Master Sword","place_zh":"克洛格森林","place_en":"Korok Forest","transcript_zh":"当林克命悬一线之时……若不是有你的声音指引着我，我也不会站在这里了。尽管如今我已听不见你的声音，但我依然要向你致谢。正是因为有你，这个世界才得以获救。请你……安心地在这里沉睡，治愈你的伤痕吧……","transcript_en":"When Link was on the brink of death...had it not been for your voice to guide me, I wouldn't be here now. Though I cannot hear your voice anymore, I still offer you my thanks. It is because of you that the world was saved. Please...rest here and heal your wounds..."},{"seq":186,"id":"vm_kohga_001","no":"No.001","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":1332,"y":-3437,"z":-780,"gx":-3437,"gy":-1332,"gz":-780,"title_zh":"可盖大人再临！","title_en":"Master Kohga Returns!","place_zh":"依盖队基地的深穴","place_en":"Yiga Clan Hideout Chasm","transcript_zh":"这里难道是……阴曹地府？黄泉彼岸？本大爷的最终归宿？不对，浑身还疼得要命，肯定还活着……能捡回一条命，全靠这块鼓鼓囊囊的怪布！真是太管用了，哪像那个卑鄙无耻的混账林克！竟敢破了本大爷——依盖队总长的绝世秘技！可恶……等等。这里莫非就是“地底”……听说以前住着一大帮古代人。大概吧？","transcript_en":"Is this...the afterlife? The great beyond? My final reckoning? Nah, it still hurts like I'm alive... And I'm alive thanks to this weird inflated cloth! Talk about helpful, unlike that dastardly Link! How dare he foil the secret technique of the leader of the Yiga Clan! Grrrr... Hang on. Maybe I'm in the Depths... That's where a buncha ancient people lived. Maybe?"},{"seq":187,"id":"vm_kohga_002","no":"No.002","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":1360,"y":-3402,"z":-780,"gx":-3402,"gy":-1360,"gz":-780,"title_zh":"破魔之根","title_en":"Lightroots","place_zh":"姆马兹罗之根","place_en":"Umamustor Lightroot","transcript_zh":"这地方也太——黑了吧！要是这些微微发亮的玩意儿能更亮一点就好了……或者这块绿色的……纹章一样的东西好歹给点反应啊！话说这到底是什么，某种巨型植物吗？直通到那么高的地方……该不会是从这儿一路长到地上的吧？！","transcript_en":"This place is waaay too dark! Maybe if these dim, glowing things could get brighter...or if this green...crest thingy reacted at all! And what even is this—some kind of massive plant? It goes so far up... Does it reach all the way from here to the surface?!"},{"seq":188,"id":"vm_kohga_003","no":"No.003","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":1321,"y":-3360,"z":-779,"gx":-3360,"gy":-1321,"gz":-779,"title_zh":"游荡的魄","title_en":"Wandering Poes","place_zh":"格鲁德高地地底","place_en":"Gerudo Highlands Depths","transcript_zh":"哦嚯！刚才它颤了一下！不过一碰它，连本大爷的后背都凉飕飕的。嗯……这些玩意儿该不会是……幽魂吧？可要是幽魂的话，那、那这里岂不还真是阴曹地府啊！","transcript_en":"Hoho! It shook a little there! But touching it also sent a shiver down MY spine. Huh... Maybe they're...spirits? But if they are, then th-that means this IS the afterlife!"},{"seq":189,"id":"vm_kohga_004","no":"No.004","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":1521,"y":-2934,"z":-920,"gx":-2934,"gy":-1521,"gz":-920,"title_zh":"敏锐的第六感","title_en":"A Keen Sixth Sense","place_zh":"格鲁德高地地底","place_en":"Gerudo Highlands Depths","transcript_zh":"这个飘在空中的绿色玩意儿是什么？嗯……呼……某种瓶子吗？里面装了啥？看本大爷把它……给……算了！不开就不开！不过本大爷还是得把你收好。我的第六感告诉我，你肯定是个宝贝。","transcript_en":"What's this floating green thing? Hrm...huff... This some kinda bottle? What's inside? I'll just... JUST... Fine! Don't open! I'm still gonna hang on to you. My sixth sense says you're important."},{"seq":190,"id":"vm_kohga_005","no":"No.005","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":1680,"y":-2557,"z":-869,"gx":-2557,"gy":-1680,"gz":-869,"title_zh":"可盖大人的收获①","title_en":"Master Kohga's Education, Part 1","place_zh":"格鲁德高地地底","place_en":"Gerudo Highlands Depths","transcript_zh":"嗯，这又是某种古代小玩意儿？这边是平的，那边是尖的……嘿咻……哎哟，我的屁股！疼死了，坐着真难受，破凳子！看本大爷踢死你，破凳子！哈！哇啊！……什、什么情况？你怎么发光了？","transcript_en":"Hrm. This some kinda ancient doodad? It's flat there and pointed here... Huuup... Aah, my butt! Ow, what a terrible seat. Oh, take this, terrible seat. Ha! Gah! ...Wh-what? Why are you glowing?"},{"seq":191,"id":"vm_kohga_006","no":"No.006","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":1916,"y":-2915,"z":-732,"gx":-2915,"gy":-1916,"gz":-732,"title_zh":"可盖大人的收获②","title_en":"Master Kohga's Education, Part 2","place_zh":"格鲁德高地地底","place_en":"Gerudo Highlands Depths","transcript_zh":"啊哈，又有好多古代小玩意儿！还有不少跟上次那个一样的……刚才那鬼东西猛地冲上天，差点把本大爷的香蕉都吓飞了。嗯……我敢打赌，古代人肯定是拿这些东西当交通工具的！也就是说……本大爷也能用！过来吧，圆咕隆咚的家伙！快让可盖大人见识见识你的本事！嘿呀！","transcript_en":"Aha, more ancient doodads! Lots like the last one too... Crazy thing firing off into the air scared the bananas outta me. Huh... I bet the ancients used them to get around! Which means...I can too! C'mere, round thingy! Time to show Master Kohga what you can do. Hee-yah!"},{"seq":192,"id":"vm_kohga_007","no":"No.007","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":2362,"y":-2701,"z":-516,"gx":-2701,"gy":-2362,"gz":-516,"title_zh":"烟雾蘑菇","title_en":"Puffshroom","place_zh":"格鲁德高地地底","place_en":"Gerudo Highlands Depths","transcript_zh":"哦哦，是个没见过的新蘑菇！在地上可从没见过这种玩意儿……我就偷偷咬一小口。咳咳！哪来这么大一股烟？！啥也看不见了……哦，简直跟烟雾弹一样！我得多留几个带在身上，下次情况不妙的时候正好派上用场……","transcript_en":"Ooo, this is a new mushroom! I've never seen anything like it on the surface... Maybe just one little bite. Ack! What is this smoke?! I can't see anything... Oh, just like a smoke screen! I should hang on to a few of these for the next time things are looking dicey..."},{"seq":193,"id":"vm_kohga_008","no":"No.008","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":2381,"y":-2989,"z":-477,"gx":-2989,"gy":-2381,"gz":-477,"title_zh":"邀请加入依盖队","title_en":"Invitation to Join the Yiga Clan","place_zh":"格鲁德沙漠地底","place_en":"Gerudo Desert Depths","transcript_zh":"好吧，原来地底也有波克布林啊……而且还挺聪明，懂得拿工具挖……什么东西……可它们一见到本大爷二话不说就动手。我还以为同为那位大人的忠实仆从，大家都能交个朋友呢……好歹先聊两句嘛……","transcript_en":"OK, so there are Bokoblins down here... And they're smart enough to mine for...something...using tools... But they attack me right away. Here I thought faithful servants of the Magnificent One would want to be friends... Could have at least talked first..."},{"seq":194,"id":"vm_kohga_009","no":"No.009","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":2511,"y":-3290,"z":-475,"gx":-3290,"gy":-2511,"gz":-475,"title_zh":"和波克布林决裂","title_en":"Escaping the Bokoblins","place_zh":"塔塔亚马之根","place_en":"Tatayam Lightroot","transcript_zh":"哼，总算甩掉那帮波克布林了……看来它们不喜欢这儿的光。本大爷本来还打算发发慈悲，收编它们加入新建的“依盖队地底分队”呢，结果它们一个个就只想着揍我。唉，这倒让我有点想念依盖队的弟兄们了。不知道他们现在都在干嘛呢……","transcript_en":"Heh, good riddance to those Bokoblins... I guess they don't like this light. I was going to let them join my new Yiga Clan Depths Squad, but they definitely like attacking me too much. Makes me miss the Yiga Clan. I wonder what they're up to..."},{"seq":195,"id":"vm_kohga_010","no":"No.010","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":2511,"y":-3196,"z":-475,"gx":-3196,"gy":-2511,"gz":-475,"title_zh":"卡拉卡拉废矿","title_en":"Abandoned Kara Kara Mine","place_zh":"卡拉卡拉废矿","place_en":"Abandoned Kara Kara Mine","transcript_zh":"这地方怎么回事？熔炉烧得正旺，却连个人影都看不见……不过刚才远远看着，这绿色玩意儿好像动了一下！嗯，本大爷还是赶紧找点吃的吧。要是饿出幻觉来，可就大事不妙了。","transcript_en":"What's the deal with this place? The furnace is blazing away but no one to be seen... Though from a distance, it did look like this green thing was moving! Hm. Maybe I should go find something to eat. Things will go bad if I start hallucinating."},{"seq":196,"id":"vm_kohga_011","no":"No.011","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":2719,"y":-3205,"z":-481,"gx":-3205,"gy":-2719,"gz":-481,"title_zh":"混乱花的诱惑","title_en":"Tempted by the Muddle Bud","place_zh":"格鲁德沙漠地底","place_en":"Gerudo Desert Depths","transcript_zh":"啊哈！那股要命的腐臭味就是从这儿飘出来的吗？真、是、太、臭、了！受不了了！讨厌死了！可我……居然还想再闻闻。哇哦，突然有点头晕……喂，那边！那些不是波克布林——是依盖队的弟兄们！伙计们！伙——计——们！","transcript_en":"Ah-ha! Is THIS the source of that horrible, rotting smell? It. Is. AWFUL. I can't stand it. I hate it! I...don't want to stop smelling it. Whoa. Little bit dizzy all of a... Hey, over there! Those aren't Bokoblins—they're Yiga! Guys! GUUUYS!"},{"seq":197,"id":"vm_kohga_012","no":"No.012","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":2844,"y":-3216,"z":-472,"gx":-3216,"gy":-2844,"gz":-472,"title_zh":"伫立的人影","title_en":"Standing Shadows","place_zh":"格鲁德沙漠地底","place_en":"Gerudo Desert Depths","transcript_zh":"那是……终于！有人来救本大爷了！后头有一帮波克布林在追……咦？我明明发誓刚才这儿站着个人的……可恶！也没人告诉过我，孤家寡人居然这么寂寞啊……这会儿就算让那个叫林克的家伙来作伴我都……不行！本大爷在胡说八道些什么！他把我打落到地底这笔账，我绝不原谅！绝不！","transcript_en":"Is that... At last! Someone to help me! There are Bokoblins chasing... Huh? Coulda sworn there was someone here... Grrr! No one tells you how lonely solitude is... I'd even accept the company of that Link character... NO! What am I saying? I'll never forgive him for casting me down into the Depths! Never!"},{"seq":198,"id":"vm_kohga_013","no":"No.013","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":3033,"y":-3214,"z":-471,"gx":-3214,"gy":-3033,"gz":-471,"title_zh":"在外靠朋友","title_en":"Silent Companions","place_zh":"格鲁德沙漠地底","place_en":"Gerudo Desert Depths","transcript_zh":"唉，本大爷还铁了心以为这个肯定是活人呢。结果呢，又是一尊石像。意料之中……喂，地底下的石像还真不少啊。要不我就顺着这尊石像望的方向，一尊接一尊往前走吧。反正本大爷也没别的地方好去……","transcript_en":"Ugh, I was SURE this one was a person. But nope, just another statue. Figures... Hey, there are a lot of statues down here. Maybe I'll just head from one to the next, starting with where this one is looking. I haven't got anywhere else to be..."},{"seq":199,"id":"vm_kohga_014","no":"No.014","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":2909,"y":-3838,"z":-487,"gx":-3838,"gy":-2909,"gz":-487,"title_zh":"香蕉的记忆","title_en":"Essence of Banana","place_zh":"格鲁德废矿","place_en":"Abandoned Gerudo Mine","transcript_zh":"好嘛，又是废墟。就不能是个正经村子吗？哼，连口水都没有。我都开始幻听依盖队的弟兄们在喊我了。“可盖大人……可盖大人……”感觉继承“可盖”这个名号还像昨天一样呢……明明都过去那么久了——等等，这股香味！这是……放了整整五天催熟的大剑香蕉！正是本大爷最爱的熟度！一定是他们！依盖队！伙计们？！","transcript_en":"Oh good, more ruins. Couldn't be an actual village, could it? Hrmph, and no water either. I keep hallucinating Yiga calling out to me. \"Kohga... Kohga...\" Feels like yesterday that I inherited that name... So long ago—that smell! That's...banana, set out to ripen for five days! JUST HOW I LIKE IT. It must be them! Yiga Clan! GUYS?!"},{"seq":200,"id":"vm_kohga_015","no":"No.015","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":3456,"y":-3760,"z":-469,"gx":-3760,"gy":-3456,"gz":-469,"title_zh":"可盖大人的收获③","title_en":"Master Kohga's Education, Part 3","place_zh":"格鲁德沙漠地底","place_en":"Gerudo Desert Depths","transcript_zh":"依盖队的弟兄们正在收集至关重要的香蕉——咳，是物资——好让我们建立依盖队地底分部。趁他们忙活的工夫，本大爷得研究明白这装置怎么用。底下开着口的一块布……要是我在这儿点上火呢？嗯……哦豁……不好！糟了！停、停下！别飞走啊！","transcript_en":"The Yiga are gathering critical bananas—I mean supplies—for us to set up the Depths branch of the Yiga Clan. While they do that, I need to figure out how this device works. Cloth with a hole at the bottom... What if I put fire here? Hmm... Uh huh... Oh! Oh, no! S-stop! Don't fly away!"},{"seq":201,"id":"vm_kohga_016","no":"No.016","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":3739,"y":-4088,"z":-466,"gx":-4088,"gy":-3739,"gz":-466,"title_zh":"藏匿在墓地中的秘密","title_en":"The Cemetery's Secret","place_zh":"格鲁德地下坟场","place_en":"Gerudo Underground Cemetery","transcript_zh":"这里是什么坟墓吗……嗯……可连根骨头都没有。看来根本不是什么坟墓嘛？本大爷敢打赌，这儿肯定藏了什么好东西……啊哈！是个宝箱，哈哈！看我来把它……打开……可恶！锈死了！还有别的东西吗？哦，一本笔记！上面的字我是一个也看不懂，不过……哼哼哼，我知道这是什么！看来幸运女神还没抛弃本大爷嘛！","transcript_en":"Is this some kinda grave... Hmm... No bones though. Not a grave after all, are you? I bet you're hiding something... Aha! A treasure chest, ha ha! Now I'll just...open... Grr! Rusted! Anything else here? Ah, a notebook! I can't read the letters, but...... Hehehe, I know what this is! It seems luck hasn't abandoned me yet!"},{"seq":202,"id":"vm_kohga_017","no":"No.017","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":3723,"y":-4308,"z":-480,"gx":-4308,"gy":-3723,"gz":-480,"title_zh":"蛮暴之徒聚集的地方","title_en":"Unsafe Gathering","place_zh":"沙漠竞技场","place_en":"Desert Coliseum","transcript_zh":"休想，哼哼哼！可骗不了本大爷！这地方浑身上下都写着“陷阱”两个字。瞧好了，我要是像这样靠过去……来了！陷阱触发了！哈哈！简直小菜一碟——喂，你是什么玩意儿——住、住手！本大爷可不想跟你打啊！","transcript_en":"Nuh-uh, hehehe! You can't fool me! This place has all the makings of a trap. See, if I get closer, like this... There! Trap sprung! Haha! So easy to— Hey, what are you— S-stop it! I don't wanna fight you!"},{"seq":203,"id":"vm_kohga_018","no":"No.018","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":3676,"y":-4493,"z":-477,"gx":-4493,"gy":-3676,"gz":-477,"title_zh":"地底的大化石","title_en":"Great Skeletons of the Depths","place_zh":"格鲁德暗化石","place_en":"Gerudo Dark Skeleton","transcript_zh":"哇——哦。本大爷在格鲁德沙漠见过不少大骸骨，但在地底还没撞见过这么大的家伙……嗯，嗯嗯嗯嗯。既然地上和地底是连着的，那就说明生活在上面的生物也能跑到这儿来！应该是这样吧！","transcript_en":"Whoooa. I've seen some big skeletons in Gerudo Desert, but I don't think I've run into anything like that down here... Hm. Hmmmmmm. If the surface and the Depths are connected, then that means the creatures living up above could come down here! I think!"},{"seq":204,"id":"vm_kohga_019","no":"No.019","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":3411,"y":-4482,"z":-478,"gx":-4482,"gy":-3411,"gz":-478,"title_zh":"可盖大人的收获④","title_en":"Master Kohga's Education, Part 4","place_zh":"格鲁德沙漠地底","place_en":"Gerudo Desert Depths","transcript_zh":"坟场捡到的那本笔记，里头的插图画得那叫一个清清楚楚。原来这些玩意儿能按不同方式拼在一起，造出全新的东西！这么说来，要是本大爷把这块布……接到这个台子上……再把这个吹风的家伙安在这儿……哈！然后在底下点上火，它就能动起来！哼哼哼……没错，我得好好研读这本笔记。是时候回基地底下的深穴那边去了！","transcript_en":"The pictures in that book from the graveyard were very, very clear. These things all attach in different ways to make something else! So if I this cloth...connect it to the platform...put this wind-blowing thing here... Ha! Then if I lit a fire under it, It'd work! Hehehe... Yeah, I need to study this notebook. Time to head to the hole under the hideout!"},{"seq":205,"id":"vm_kohga_020","no":"No.020","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":1564,"y":-3112,"z":-913,"gx":-3112,"gy":-1564,"gz":-913,"title_zh":"崛起！依盖队帝国！","title_en":"Building Up the Yiga Clan Empire","place_zh":"格鲁德高地地底","place_en":"Gerudo Highlands Depths","transcript_zh":"哼哼哼……好，离基地这么近，在这儿建个据点准没问题……可坟场那本笔记该怎么办呢？里头画的绝——对是某种设计图……但看着简直异想天开，根本造不出来，纯属浪费时间……不过！万一真能造出来呢……本大爷还是得多探索探索地底才行……","transcript_en":"Hehehe... OK, so I think it'll work to set up a base here, close to the hideout... But what do I do about that graveyard notebook? The drawings in it are ab-so-lutely schematics of some kind...but they look like impossible, unbuildable wastes of time... BUT! If they aren't... I should explore the Depths some more..."},{"seq":206,"id":"vm_kohga_021","no":"No.021","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":1299,"y":-4616,"z":-941,"gx":-4616,"gy":-1299,"gz":-941,"title_zh":"贪吃的巨霸迦马","title_en":"The Glutton Frox","place_zh":"格鲁德高地地底","place_en":"Gerudo Highlands Depths","transcript_zh":"你这头又蠢又大的蛤蟆怪！头上顶着那么漂亮的矿石，结果本大爷凑近瞧一眼就想吞了我，什么毛病啊？！希望你喜欢本大爷赏你的那朵炸弹花！祝你吃得满肚子胀气！","transcript_en":"Yooou big, stupid toad thing! Why do you have good-looking ore on your head if you're just gonna try and eat me when I check it out?! I hope you like that bomb flower I gave you! I hope it gives you gas!"},{"seq":207,"id":"vm_kohga_022","no":"No.022","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":979,"y":-4039,"z":-1110,"gx":-4039,"gy":-979,"gz":-1110,"title_zh":"古代的守卫者","title_en":"An Ancient Guard","place_zh":"格鲁德高地地底","place_en":"Gerudo Highlands Depths","transcript_zh":"笔记里肯定写过这玩意儿，我敢打包票。在哪一页来着？嗯……嗯……啊哈！找到了。照图上画的，只要凑太近，这家伙就会变成……人形。多半是某种守卫吧？眼睛还泛着红光，红眼睛向来准没好事。本大爷还是……离远点吧。","transcript_en":"The notebook had info about this thing, I'm sure. What page was that? Ummm...ummm... Aha! Here we go. According to these pictures, this creature gets all...person shaped when you get too close. Must be some kind of guard? It's got glowing red eyes, and those are ALWAYS bad news. I'll...keep my distance."},{"seq":208,"id":"vm_kohga_023","no":"No.023","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":-1794,"y":-1982,"z":-364,"gx":-1982,"gy":1794,"gz":-364,"title_zh":"命名为左纳乌装置！","title_en":"They Shall Be Called Zonai Devices!","place_zh":"海拉鲁丘陵地底","place_en":"Hyrule Ridge Depths","transcript_zh":"本大爷敢打赌，捡到的这本笔记肯定是左纳乌族留下的。要是没猜错的话……这个符号念“左”，这个大概念“纳”，还有这个念“乌”。嗯……“装……置……”……“左纳乌装置……”左纳乌装置！对，就这么叫准没错，就算错了本大爷也不管！","transcript_en":"I bet the notebook I found belonged to a Zonai. And if I'm right about that, then...this shape must be \"zo,\" and I think this one is \"na,\" and THIS is \"i.\" Hmmm... \"De...vice...\" \"Zonai device...\" Zonai device! Yeah, that seems right, and I don't care if it isn't!"},{"seq":209,"id":"vm_kohga_024","no":"No.024","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":-1841,"y":-2419,"z":-716,"gx":-2419,"gy":1841,"gz":-716,"title_zh":"通天输送带","title_en":"A Way Up","place_zh":"塔邦挞边境地底","place_en":"Tabantha Frontier Depths","transcript_zh":"所以说……这玩意儿明摆着是用来往地上送东西的。可本大爷想不通，它是怎么把东西穿破地层送上去的？笔记上的图画得就好像……自然而然就上去了，直接就……穿过去了。可恶……搞不懂啊！要是弄不明白，就没法靠它往地上的据点运东西了！","transcript_en":"So... Obviously this was meant to send things to the surface. What I don't understand is how it moves things through the ground. The pictures in the notebook look like it just...happens. They just...go through. Grrr... I don't get it! And I can't use this to send stuff to a base on the surface if I can't figure it out!"},{"seq":210,"id":"vm_kohga_025","no":"No.025","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":-2692,"y":-1029,"z":-273,"gx":-1029,"gy":2692,"gz":-273,"title_zh":"变成石头的巨人","title_en":"A Stone Giant","place_zh":"断崖魔人像","place_en":"Cliff Bargainer Statue","transcript_zh":"哦——脸在这儿呢。嗯，笔记里可没画你。这么说你不是左纳乌族造的咯？还有，你怎么就变成石头了呢？说不定是因为干了什么坏事，才被女神给石化了……嘛，是按女神的标准算坏事。既然她讨厌你，本大爷敢说咱俩肯定特别投缘。","transcript_en":"Annnd there's the face. Hm. You're not in the notebook. Does that mean the Zonai didn't make you? And how'd you get turned to stone, anyway? Maybe the Goddess did it because you did something bad... Well, bad by her standards. And if she didn't like you, I bet we woulda gotten along."},{"seq":211,"id":"vm_kohga_026","no":"No.026","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":-3123,"y":319,"z":-621,"gx":319,"gy":3123,"gz":-621,"title_zh":"古栗欧克的巢","title_en":"Gleeok Den","place_zh":"古栗欧克的巢","place_en":"Gleeok Den","transcript_zh":"嚯嚯嚯！瞧瞧这片大平地！四面还都是悬崖峭壁……简直是建据点的绝佳宝地！不过……得先把那些石像全拆了。哦！再全换成可盖大人的雕像！不过……摆什么姿势最帅呢？要不……这样！或者摆个……哈！再来个——等等，刚才那声低吼是什么？啊！那是什么怪物？！哇啊——！","transcript_en":"Ho ho ho! Look at this level ground! And cliffs on all sides... This would be the perfect spot for a base! I...would have to get rid of those statues though. Oh! And replace them with statues of me! But...what poses would be best? Maybe...THIS! Or I could do...HA! What about—wait. Is that growling? Ah! What is THAT?! AAH!"},{"seq":212,"id":"vm_kohga_027","no":"No.027","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":-2873,"y":714,"z":-660,"gx":714,"gy":2873,"gz":-660,"title_zh":"可盖大人的收获⑤","title_en":"Master Kohga's Education, Part 5","place_zh":"奥尔汀山脉地底","place_en":"Eldin Mountains Depths","transcript_zh":"哇哦，太棒了！就是这个！终于找到一根棍子模样的左纳乌装置，看着就能用来掌控方向！简直就是……操纵杆！有了这玩意儿，依盖队的弟兄们只要稍微练练，就能熟练驾驭左纳乌装置了！而且，本大爷现在还能照着笔记试着造那只大鸟一样的东西……","transcript_en":"Whoa, yes! There we go! Finally, a stick-shaped Zonai device that looks like it could steer things! Like a...steering stick! With this, the Yiga Clan will be able to use Zonai Devices with only a little bit of training! Plus, now I can try making this bird-like thing from the notebook..."},{"seq":213,"id":"vm_kohga_028","no":"No.028","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":-2829,"y":1164,"z":-754,"gx":1164,"gy":2829,"gz":-754,"title_zh":"死亡之山的洗礼","title_en":"Death Mountain Initiation","place_zh":"火之神殿","place_en":"Fire Temple","transcript_zh":"越过死亡之山火山口，前方是一片酷热难当的地带。奔流熔岩散发出的高温极其猛烈——猛烈到倘若未做好万全准备，便足以危及性命。随行护卫严令禁止我再往前一步，然而密切关注日后将与我们并肩作战的神兽，乃是我的职责所在。此次使命，实在是险象环生……","transcript_en":"Just beyond the Maw of Death Mountain is a scorching region. The heat from the flow of lava can be intense—so intense, in fact, that it can take one's life should they fail to prepare accordingly. My bodyguards forbade me from going any farther, yet it is my duty to keep a close watch on the Divine Beasts we will be fighting alongside. This mission proves to be exceedingly dangerous..."},{"seq":214,"id":"vm_kohga_029","no":"No.029","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":-1849,"y":909,"z":-634,"gx":909,"gy":1849,"gz":-634,"title_zh":"可盖大人的收获⑥","title_en":"Master Kohga's Education, Part 6","place_zh":"海拉鲁大森林地底","place_en":"Great Hyrule Forest Depths","transcript_zh":"呼，总算逃出那个热死人的鬼地方了……哦！是轮子！大的小的全都有！嗯……小轮子肯定特别灵活，大轮子用来跑烂路准没错……哦哦，咱们依盖队反应这么快、平衡感又这么好，本大爷敢说拿这玩意儿造辆独轮车都不在话下！","transcript_en":"OK, I think I've finally escaped that scorching misery of a place... Oh! Wheels! Big ones AND small ones! Hmm...I bet the small ones are really maneuverable, but those big ones would be great for tough paths... Oooh, we Yiga have such good reflexes and balance, I bet we could even make a unicycle with these!"},{"seq":215,"id":"vm_kohga_030","no":"No.030","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":-1407,"y":1021,"z":-543,"gx":1021,"gy":1407,"gz":-543,"title_zh":"暗萤火虫","title_en":"A Deep Firefly","place_zh":"齐洛利树海","place_en":"Minshi Grove","transcript_zh":"好，那个发亮的生物是啥？某种……虫子吧。说不定能拿来熬成药，对付地底这伸手不见五指的黑……得先捉住它，不过这还不是小菜一碟！穿着依盖队紧身衣的忍者，潜行功夫天下第一……呃，什么鬼？开玩笑的吧？那棵树怎么在走路啊？！","transcript_en":"OK, what is that glowing creature? Some kinda...bug. Maybe we could use it in an elixir that helps with the darkness down here... Gotta catch it first, but that'll be easy! Nothing is sneakier than a Yiga in their Yiga Clan clothes... Uuuh, what? Are you kidding me? Is that tree WALKING?!"},{"seq":216,"id":"vm_kohga_031","no":"No.031","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":-354,"y":2221,"z":-505,"gx":2221,"gy":354,"gz":-505,"title_zh":"卓拉的石像","title_en":"Zora Statues","place_zh":"拉聂尔湿地地底","place_en":"Lanayru Wetlands Depths","transcript_zh":"这尊石像长得真像卓拉族……这么说，之前看到的那尊女性石像，多半就是格鲁德族咯。顺着这尊石像走下去，最后肯定也能找到什么人工建筑……本大爷现在应该在拉聂尔地区的正下方，可照这么算，地底也太辽阔了吧！这辈子都探索不完啊……","transcript_en":"This statue looks a lot like a Zora... Which means that statue of a woman I saw before was probably a Gerudo. And if I follow this statue, I'll probably find something man-made eventually too... I think I'm beneath the Lanayru region, but that'd mean the Depths are massive! I'll never finish exploring them..."},{"seq":217,"id":"vm_kohga_032","no":"No.032","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":-569,"y":3300,"z":-750,"gx":3300,"gy":569,"gz":-750,"title_zh":"拉聂尔废矿","title_en":"Abandoned Lanayru Mine","place_zh":"拉聂尔废矿","place_en":"Abandoned Lanayru Mine","transcript_zh":"原来那些卓拉石像一路指引的就是这儿啊……跟格鲁德石像指路的方式如出一辙。肯定是个要紧地方！而且瞧着结实得很，拿来当依盖队的据点简直再合适不过了！","transcript_en":"So this is where all those Zora statues were leading me to... kinda like how the Gerudo statues pointed the way. Must be important! And sturdy, by the look of it. A perfect place for a Yiga Clan base!"},{"seq":218,"id":"vm_kohga_033","no":"No.033","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":1193,"y":1815,"z":-629,"gx":1815,"gy":-1193,"gz":-629,"title_zh":"废矿的居民","title_en":"What Lives in the Abandoned Mine?","place_zh":"卡卡利科废矿","place_en":"Abandoned Kakariko Mine","transcript_zh":"这玩意儿刚才绝对动了！一察觉到本大爷就立马缩回去了，但我可是看得清清楚楚！它脖子伸得老长，跟笔记里画的一模一样！真不敢相信这么古老的东西居然还能动……还是带走吧。好，用腿发力往上抬——哎哟妈呀，你也太沉了吧！算了算了！回头叫依盖队的年轻小伙子来扛回去吧。","transcript_en":"This thing was definitely moving! It withdrew the moment it noticed me, but I saw it! Its neck was all stretched out just like the pictures in the notebook! I can't believe something so ancient still works... Better take it with me. OK lift with your legs and— Oh, wow you're heavy! Never mind! The younger Yiga can haul this home."},{"seq":219,"id":"vm_kohga_034","no":"No.034","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":1774,"y":2647,"z":-552,"gx":2647,"gy":-1774,"gz":-552,"title_zh":"溢出的狂放之气","title_en":"Oozing Madness","place_zh":"东哈特尔地底","place_en":"East Necluda Depths","transcript_zh":"嚯嚯，打第一眼瞧见我就知道——那滩红糊糊的玩意儿绝非善类。只要稍微沾上一点，就觉得魂儿都要被抽走半截。而且最近这玩意儿到处蔓延。不过！本大爷早就参透了破解之法：别碰它就行！正因如此，“浮空毁灭者1号”才堪称史上最强杰作！","transcript_en":"Ho-ho, I knew it the moment I saw it—that red ooze is NOT good. It feels like part of my soul is being stolen right out of me at the slightest touch. And lately the stuff has been getting everywhere. BUT! I figured out the secret: don't touch it! And THAT is why the HOVERDOOM MK. 1 is the best thing ever."},{"seq":220,"id":"vm_kohga_035","no":"No.035","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":3214,"y":1402,"z":-597,"gx":1402,"gy":-3214,"gz":-597,"title_zh":"魂之神殿","title_en":"Spirit Temple","place_zh":"魂之神殿","place_en":"Spirit Temple","transcript_zh":"原来盯着左纳乌文字看久了，本大爷居然就能看懂了！而且我捡到的这本笔记，作者名叫米涅鲁，似乎是最后一位掌管此地的左纳乌族人……算了，本大爷大老远跑来是找魔像原型的，不是来看一尊大猫头鹰石像的。那玩意儿可不是魔像！呃……应该不是吧？","transcript_en":"Turns out if I stare at Zonai letters long enough, I can learn to read them! It also turns out someone named Mineru wrote this notebook I found. They were apparently the last Zonai to manage this place... Anyway, I came here looking for prototype constructs, not a big owl statue. And that isn't a construct! Err...right?"},{"seq":221,"id":"vm_kohga_036","no":"No.036","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":2195,"y":867,"z":-559,"gx":867,"gy":-2195,"gz":-559,"title_zh":"魔像制造房","title_en":"Construct Factory","place_zh":"魔像制造房","place_en":"Construct Factory","transcript_zh":"好吧，什么魔像原型，这地方根本……空空如也。真行啊。搞得好像本大爷本来没打算把找到的宝贝全用上似的……好歹我手里还有米涅鲁的魔像设计图！我自己造一个不就得了。由可盖大人亲手打造、专属于可盖大人的魔像！嘻嘻嘻嘻嘻……","transcript_en":"All right, so instead of prototype constructs, this place is...empty. That's great. Not like I had plans to use everything I was gonna find... At least I have the schematics for Mineru's construct! I can just make that myself. A construct by me, for me. Heeheeheeheehee..."},{"seq":222,"id":"vm_kohga_037","no":"No.037","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":2616,"y":-1259,"z":-516,"gx":-1259,"gy":-2616,"gz":-516,"title_zh":"超极恶爆炎 可盖尔爆诞","title_en":"Mecha Kohga 5000 - Deluxe","place_zh":"格鲁德高地地底","place_en":"Gerudo Highlands Depths","transcript_zh":"本大爷还以为左纳乌装置只能用来赶路呢，没想到还有会喷火的龙头？这玩意儿也太……危险了吧……哦嚯，我有主意了！要是把这玩意儿再加上尖刺，全都装到我的魔像上……没错，就是这样！这绝对碉堡了！简直所向披靡！就给它命名为……“超极恶爆炎·可盖尔”！","transcript_en":"So I thought Zonai devices were only good for getting around, but a fire-breathing dragon head? That's really...dangerous... Oh-ho, I have an idea! If I take this and some spikes and add them to my construct... Yes, YES! This could be amazing. This could be incredible! This could be...\"Mecha Kohga 5000 - Deluxe\"!"},{"seq":223,"id":"vm_kohga_038","no":"No.038","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":2330,"y":-969,"z":-519,"gx":-969,"gy":-2330,"gz":-519,"title_zh":"不速之客","title_en":"Uninvited Guests","place_zh":"初始台地南边深穴","place_en":"Great Plateau South Chasm","transcript_zh":"上次那场大地震震出了一堆通往地上的大坑，听说塞尔达还招了批新手下，自称什么“调查队”——真土气——已经开始跑到地底东张西望了。太没礼貌了！太过分了！明明是本大爷先来的！我本来大可以见一个灭一个，不过……要不先放任他们到处转转，看看能挖出什么好东西？然后再把他们统统干掉！哈！","transcript_en":"So that last earthquake opened up a bunch of holes to the surface, and apparently Zelda has some new minions. They're calling themselves a \"survey team\"—boring—and they have started poking around down here in the Depths. Rude. RUDE! I was here first! I could erase them from existence the moment I see them, but... Maybe I should let them look around and see what they find? THEN erase them! HA!"},{"seq":224,"id":"vm_kohga_039","no":"No.039","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":1921,"y":-799,"z":-523,"gx":-799,"gy":-1921,"gz":-523,"title_zh":"中央大废矿","title_en":"Great Abandoned Central Mine","place_zh":"中央大废矿","place_en":"Great Abandoned Central Mine","transcript_zh":"没错，笔记里提到的绝对就是这儿。上面说这里的魔像能赋予人左纳乌之力，只要造过一次的东西就能记住设计图并瞬间重现。那得多好用啊，偏偏这儿又冒出来一块那种绿色纹章！怎么摆弄都没反应！可恶……这破事还是丢给手下人去琢磨吧！","transcript_en":"Yeah, this is definitely the place the notebook mentioned. It says a construct here will let you use Zonai power to memorize and rebuild a design once it's been made. That would be really useful, except there's another one of those green crests! And it doesn't do anything! Grrr... Someone else can figure it out!"},{"seq":225,"id":"vm_kohga_040","no":"No.040","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":1594,"y":-226,"z":-469,"gx":-226,"gy":-1594,"gz":-469,"title_zh":"来自卧底的报告","title_en":"Spy Report","place_zh":"中央海拉鲁地底","place_en":"Central Hyrule Depths","transcript_zh":"今天真是天大的好日子！本大爷安插在调查队里的卧底传来密报——魔王大人已经苏醒了！而且塞尔达和林克双双下落不明！这正是绝佳的良机，我们要让那位大人亲眼看看，我们依盖队作为他最得力、最忠心耿耿的部下，早已做好效犬马之劳的准备！","transcript_en":"It is a good day! I got a report from one of my spies in the survey team—they say the Demon King has awakened! And both Zelda and Link have gone missing! This is the perfect opportunity to show the Magnificent One that we, his best and most loyal retainers, are ready to support him!"},{"seq":226,"id":"vm_kohga_041","no":"No.041","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":1852,"y":-1109,"z":-613,"gx":-1109,"gy":-1852,"gz":-613,"title_zh":"复苏的秘泉","title_en":"Secret Spring of Revival","place_zh":"复苏的秘泉","place_en":"Secret Spring of Revival","transcript_zh":"啊——真舒服……行了，据点建在哪儿、怎么建，依盖队的弟兄们都已经门儿清了，剩下的苦力活交给他们就行。至于本大爷嘛，等泡完这池温泉——我就得赶紧去拜见那位大人了。晋见那位大人这种头等大事，可不能随便托付给别人……啊——……","transcript_en":"Ahhhh... OK, the Yiga Clan knows where and how to build the base. They can handle the menial work from here. Meanwhile after I'm done soaking—I need to hurry to the Magnificent One. A meeting with him is not something I would leave to anyone else... Ahhh..."},{"seq":227,"id":"vm_kohga_042","no":"No.042","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":3323,"y":-2285,"z":-474,"gx":-2285,"gy":-3323,"gz":-474,"title_zh":"左纳乌能源","title_en":"Zonai Charge","place_zh":"格鲁德沙漠地底","place_en":"Gerudo Desert Depths","transcript_zh":"本大爷从潜伏在左纳乌调查队的卧底那儿，听到了个超——有趣的情报。地底之所以有这么多左纳乌的玩意儿，原来是因为古代左纳乌族曾在地底四处采掘一种名叫“左纳尼乌姆”的矿石。这么说来，那个架着大熔炉的地方就是废矿咯……而这也就理所当然地意味着，这股惊人的能源天生就该由可盖大人来掌控！","transcript_en":"I heard a reeeally interesting bit of news from one of my spies in the Zonai Survey Team. It seems there's lots of Zonai stuff down here because the ancient Zonai were digging all over the Depths to find an ore called Zonaite. Which must mean the place with the big furnace is an abandoned mine... And THAT obviously means this incredible source of energy was meant for me to control!"},{"seq":228,"id":"vm_kohga_043","no":"No.043","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":-1847,"y":-3513,"z":-416,"gx":-3513,"gy":1847,"gz":-416,"title_zh":"海布拉废矿","title_en":"Abandoned Hebra Mine","place_zh":"海布拉废矿","place_en":"Abandoned Hebra Mine","transcript_zh":"我还在纳闷那些利特石像怎么突然就断了呢，原来入口在地上，而且就在利特村正下方。嗯……莫非这些石像指向的废矿，全都在大村镇的底下？要是真这样，咱们就能趁他们放松警惕，悄悄摸摸从地底发动奇袭，打他们个措手不及！那位大人，希望您会赏识本大爷这绝顶聪明的妙计！","transcript_en":"It seemed really strange that the Rito statues ended abruptly, but turns out the entrance is on the surface, and it's right under Rito Village. Hmm... Maybe all the mines those statues point to are under big settlements? If that's true, we could employ some sneaky-sneaky stabby-stabby and attack from below while they're distracted. Magnificent One, I hope you approve of my incredibly clever plan!"},{"seq":229,"id":"vm_kohga_044","no":"No.044","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":-3531,"y":-892,"z":-682,"gx":-892,"gy":3531,"gz":-682,"title_zh":"洛美遗迹","title_en":"Lomei","place_zh":"北洛美地下层","place_en":"North Lomei Depths Labyrinth","transcript_zh":"唔……呃……吸气……差一点……哇啊！卡住了，根本钻不过去！该死的香蕉肚！这就是贪吃那金黄香甜的美味果实的代价啊……唉，这儿既然有方块魔像把守，里面肯定藏着绝世秘宝。可偏偏，香蕉又一次坏了本大爷的大事。算了不钻了！那宝箱多半也打不开！","transcript_en":"Grrr...ugh...heee... Almost... Gah! No good. Curse my banana gut! The price I pay for those lovely yellow fruits... Ugh, I just KNOW there's gotta be a great treasure if a Flux Construct is here. But no. Bananas are once again my undoing. I'm done with this. That treasure chest probably won't open anyway!"},{"seq":230,"id":"vm_kohga_045","no":"No.045","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":-3709,"y":657,"z":-540,"gx":657,"gy":3709,"gz":-540,"title_zh":"龙行之处","title_en":"The Dragon's Path","place_zh":"奥尔汀山脉地底","place_en":"Eldin Mountains Depths","transcript_zh":"咦？什么动静？感觉头顶上有什么东西……还有这风……是不是突然变大了？可我什么也没……哦、哦哦！那是什么玩意儿？！黑灯瞎火看不真切，但那难道是……龙、龙、一条龙？！那么大一条龙，本大爷刚才怎么愣是没看见啊？！","transcript_en":"Huh? What's that? It feels like something is overhead... And the wind... Did it just pick up? But I don't... Oh. OH! What's that?! It's hard to make it out but... Is that a dra...a dra...a dragon? HOW DID I NOT NOTICE A DRAGON?!"},{"seq":231,"id":"vm_kohga_046","no":"No.046","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":-3031,"y":4014,"z":-612,"gx":4014,"gy":3031,"gz":-612,"title_zh":"水上部队培训所","title_en":"Yiga Clan: Aquatics Division","place_zh":"深远阿卡莱地底","place_en":"Deep Akkala Depths","transcript_zh":"嚯……嚯哦……好大一片湖啊。拿来当依盖队水上部的训练基地简直再合适不过。我们得抓紧时间，打造出更威猛的水上载具，当然还得加紧操练依盖队的弟兄们！无论那位大人有何差遣，我们都必须随时待命！","transcript_en":"Ho...hooo... That is a really big lake. Perfect for the Aquatic Division of the Yiga Clan. We'll have to move quickly to build more powerful water vehicles. And obviously we'll need to train Yiga to use them! We must be ready for whatever the Magnificent One needs!"},{"seq":232,"id":"vm_kohga_047","no":"No.047","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":-2127,"y":4523,"z":-454,"gx":4523,"gy":2127,"gz":-454,"title_zh":"小迦马牧场","title_en":"Little Frox Farm","place_zh":"马秋兹采矿坑","place_en":"Rist Mine","transcript_zh":"地底的魔物一个个都强得离谱！个个能以一敌百！可偏偏……谁也不听本大爷的话！每次一撞见就被追着揍，本大爷最讨厌挨揍了！正——因如此，本大爷隆重启动了“魔物驯养计划”！就像崽儿都亲爹娘一样，本大爷亲手拉扯大的魔物也肯定跟我亲！到时候全拉去效忠魔王大人！哇哈哈哈——喂！本大爷不是食物！真不是啊！别咬我呀——！","transcript_en":"All of the monsters down here are so strong! Stronger than a hundred men! But...none of them listen to me! The moment I find one, I get attacked. I hate getting attacked! Annnd that's why I've launched the \"Monster Training Program.\" Just as every child bonds with their parent, every monster I raise will bond with me! And they will serve the Demon King! Bwahaha—heeey! I'm not food! No I'm nooot. Stop biting meee."},{"seq":233,"id":"vm_kohga_048","no":"No.048","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":32,"y":3339,"z":-709,"gx":3339,"gy":-32,"gz":-709,"title_zh":"瘴气的真面目","title_en":"Origins of the Gloom","place_zh":"拉聂尔大水源地底","place_en":"Lanayru Great Spring Depths","transcript_zh":"原来地底到处都是的那种红玩意儿还有名字，叫“瘴气”啊！早知道它是从那位大人身上溢出来的，本大爷早就顺藤摸瓜找过去了！现在可没辙了——这鬼东西满地乱淌，根本没法反推源头。真是碍事的破玩……呃……我是说……本大爷可喜欢那位大人的瘴气了！超级喜欢！喜欢得不得了！地底回音太大，听着才像我在发牢骚，其实我真没有！瘴气万岁，万岁万岁！","transcript_en":"So there's a name for that red stuff I keep finding all over the Depths: gloom! I wish I'd known it was flowing from the Magnificent One—I would have just followed it to him! I can't now, though—the blasted stuff is all over the place and impossible to back track. Stupid no good... Errr... I mean... I like the Magnificent One's gloom! A lot! So much! the acoustics down here just made it SOUND like I was complaining. But I wasn't. Gloom gloom gloom!"},{"seq":234,"id":"vm_kohga_049","no":"No.049","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":1430,"y":3889,"z":-872,"gx":3889,"gy":-1430,"gz":-872,"title_zh":"背着波克布林的巨人","title_en":"The Giant and the Bokoblin","place_zh":"拉聂尔山地底","place_en":"Mount Lanayru Depths","transcript_zh":"起初本大爷还以为是头巨型波克布林呢——当然，我连眼皮都没眨一下——结果只是尊石像……嗯？等等，这边才是背面吗？干嘛在背上刻张硕大的波克布林脸？难道是某种伪装？嗯……这倒让我想起地上那个专门做怪物面具的怪家伙了。","transcript_en":"At first, I thought this was a giant Bokoblin—and I absolutely didn't even flinch at the sight—but it seems to just be a Statue... Hm? Hang on, is this the back? Why would there be a big Bokoblin face there? Could it be some kind of disguise? Hrm. Reminds me of that guy on the surface who makes monster masks."},{"seq":235,"id":"vm_kohga_050","no":"No.050","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":2235,"y":3545,"z":-587,"gx":3545,"gy":-2235,"gz":-587,"title_zh":"魔王的气息","title_en":"Signs of the Demon King","place_zh":"哈特诺废矿","place_en":"Abandoned Hateno Mine","transcript_zh":"本大爷当然明白，瘴气是那位大人赐予我们的恩泽……踩在上面简直是对大人的大不敬。可是……这玩意儿也铺得太满了点吧。地上虽然没这么浓，但我真不知道上面的人是怎么躲过去的。等等，照这么说难道……那位大人肯定就和我们一样，身在地底啊！","transcript_en":"I understand that the gloom is a blessing given to us by the Magnificent One...and that stepping on it is basically an insult to him. BUT... It's really gotten all over the place. I don't know how people on the surface avoid it, even if it is less thick up there. Wait. Could that mean... The Magnificent One must be in the Depths with us!"},{"seq":236,"id":"vm_kohga_051","no":"No.051","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":3383,"y":2895,"z":-452,"gx":2895,"gy":-3383,"gz":-452,"title_zh":"向阳草","title_en":"Sundelions","place_zh":"沃托里废矿","place_en":"Abandoned Lurelin Mine","transcript_zh":"本大爷愿拿我全部的大剑香蕉打赌，那位大人绝对就在地底！这瘴气浓得……简直像一锅红彤彤的浓汤。可这么浓的瘴气，连依盖队的弟兄们搜寻起来都躲不开。之前有个卧底是不是提过什么向阳草和瘴气的事来着？本大爷得赶紧派人查查……","transcript_en":"I'm willing to bet all my bananas that the Magnificent One is down here. The gloom is so thick...like a red oozy soup. But it's too thick for even the Yiga Clan to avoid it while searching. Wasn't there something one of my spies said about sundelions and the gloom? I'll need to look into that..."},{"seq":237,"id":"vm_kohga_052","no":"No.052","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":3532,"y":2591,"z":-627,"gx":2591,"gy":-3532,"gz":-627,"title_zh":"可盖大人的心愿","title_en":"Master Kohga's Wish","place_zh":"古代地下展望台","place_en":"Ancient Observation Deck","transcript_zh":"笔记上写着，这里是以前的人们祈求姻缘的地方。大概吧……那既然如此，本大爷许愿快点见到魔王大人！嗯……难道有什么诀窍？我要见魔王大人！我要见魔王大人！本大爷要见魔王大人！！","transcript_en":"The notebook says this is where people wished for matchmaking. Or something... Well, in that case, I wish to meet the Demon King! Hm... Maybe there's a trick to it? I wish to meet the Demon King! I wish to meet the Demon King! I WISH TO MEET THE DEMON KING!"},{"seq":238,"id":"vm_kohga_053","no":"No.053","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":3672,"y":362,"z":-498,"gx":362,"gy":-3672,"gz":-498,"title_zh":"依盖队据点","title_en":"Yiga Clan HQ","place_zh":"费罗尼草原地底","place_en":"Faron Grasslands Depths","transcript_zh":"地底的魔物和瘴气好像都不喜欢水，所以湖泊简直是建据点的风水宝地！咱们已经建成了一座堪称完美的据点，弟兄们对左纳乌装置的钻研也突飞猛进，设计图一张接一张地出！哈哈哈……不过本大爷自己也得抓紧开工了，赶紧造出……“超极恶爆炎·可盖尔”！","transcript_en":"Monsters and gloom don't seem to like the water in the Depths, making lakes the perfect place for bases! We've already got a perfect site up and running, and the Yiga are making progress using Zonai devices. They're turning out one schematic after another! Hahaha... But also I should really get to work on...Mecha Kohga 5000 - Deluxe!"},{"seq":239,"id":"vm_kohga_054","no":"No.054","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":374,"y":-336,"z":-478,"gx":-336,"gy":-374,"gz":-478,"title_zh":"坏消息","title_en":"Unwelcome News","place_zh":"中央海拉鲁地底","place_en":"Central Hyrule Depths","transcript_zh":"可恶……那个遭天杀的混账林克居然回来了！我就知道他失踪的传闻哪有这么便宜的事！而且只要林克现身，背后肯定有人在操纵他！但应该不是塞尔达吧，她早就从这个世界上消失了……还是说根本没有？王室那帮人诡计多端……嗯，行！绝不能掉以轻心，不把事儿彻底办妥，本大爷绝不歇着！","transcript_en":"Grrr... That cursed Link is back! I knew rumors of him vanishing were too good to be true! And where you find Link, you'll find someone pulling his strings! It can't be Zelda though. She's long gone from this world... Or is she? The royal family can be tricky... Hmmm. OK. Assume nothing, and only rest when I'm SURE the job is done!"},{"seq":240,"id":"vm_kohga_055","no":"No.055","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":-963,"y":-244,"z":-1015,"gx":-244,"gy":963,"gz":-1015,"title_zh":"寻求神代的力量……","title_en":"Unlocking an Ancient Power","place_zh":"瘴气根源","place_en":"Gloom's Origin","transcript_zh":"那位大人究竟在哪儿呢？咱们把这儿翻了个底朝天也一无所——嗯？喂，你！慌慌张张跑什么呢？慢点说，不用这么急——什么？那个绿色纹章？你们弄明白怎么启动它了？那还等什么，火速赶往中央大废矿！快！再快点！","transcript_en":"Where could the Magnificent One be? We've searched high and low with nothing to— Hmm? Hey, you! Why are you in such a hurry? Slow down, there's no need to— What? The green crest? You've figured out how to make it work? Then we have to hurry to the Great Abandoned Central Mine! Hurry! GO FASTER!"}];
